2124.html,Part 1 of 2 — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring,32,Torque Adapter (303-565) to remove the camshaft sprocket bolt. Remove the RH camshaft sprocket bolt. 31. Remove the chain guide bolt. 32. CAUTION: Remove the camshaft,0.31 inch;0.47 inch;12 mm;8 mm,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;303-565;CAUTION;LEMON;NEUTRAL;NOTE,"Part 1 of 2 — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Cylinder Head Assembly >> Service and Repair >> Part 1 of 2 Part 1 of 2 Cylinder Heads Special Tool(s) Removal Both cylinder heads 1. With the vehicle in NEUTRAL, position it on a hoist. 2. Relieve the fuel system pressure. 3. Drain the cooling system . 4. Remove the intake manifold . 5. Remove the cooling fan shroud. 6. Remove the accessory drive belt. 7. Remove the LH valve cover. 8. Remove the RH valve cover. 9. Disconnect the generator electrical connections. 10. Remove the accessory drive belt tensioner. 11. Remove the generator mounting bracket and the generator as an assembly. 12. Disconnect the crankshaft position (CKP) sensor electrical connector. 13. Remove the wiring harness retainers. 14. Disconnect the water temperature indicator sender unit and the engine coolant temperature (ECT) sensor electrical connectors. 15. NOTE: The coolant bypass hose will be removed with the thermostat housing . Move the coolant bypass hose clamp off the water pump outlet. 16. Remove the thermostat housing and the coolant brass hose. 17. Remove the bolt and the wiring harness routing clip. 18. Remove the bolts and position the accessory bracket aside. 19. Remove the wiring harness casing from the LH cylinder head. 20. Remove the bolt and the oil level indicator tube. 21. Using the special tool, disconnect the LH spark plug wires from the spark plugs . 22. Disconnect the fuel pressure /temperature sensor electrical and vacuum connections and the fuel pulse damper vacuum hose. 23. Remove the fuel injection supply manifold. 1 Remove the fuel supply tube from the fuel manifold. Position the fuel supply tube aside. 2 Remove the fuel injection supply manifold bolts and the supply manifold and the fuel injectors as an assembly. 24. NOTE: Mark each of the roller followers to ensure it is installed in its original position during reassembly. Use the special tool to remove the roller followers. 25. NOTE: Late build pulley shown, early build pulley similar. Using the special tool, set the number 1 piston to top dead center (TDC). RH cylinder head 26. Remove the RH fenderwell splash shield. 27. Remove the RH camshaft chain tensioner. 28. Remove the RH exhaust manifold. 29. Remove the bolt and the bracket. 30. CAUTION: The RH camshaft sprocket is a left-hand threaded bolt. NOTE: If necessary, use the Camshaft Gear Torque Adapter (303-565) to remove the camshaft sprocket bolt. Remove the RH camshaft sprocket bolt. 31. Remove the chain guide bolt. 32. CAUTION: Remove the camshaft sprocket to prevent breaking the cassette and to gain clearance to remove the cylinder head. NOTE: Hold the chain and cassette with a rubber band to aid in removal and prevent the chain from falling into the cylinder block. Remove the RH camshaft sprocket from the cassette. 33. Remove the eight 12 mm (0.47 inch) bolts and the two 8 mm (0.31 inch) bolts in the sequence shown, and remove the RH cylinder head. - Discard the head gasket. - Discard the cylinder head bolts. 34. Clean the gasket mating surfaces. LH cylinder head 35. Remove the LH exhaust manifold. 36. Remove the bolt and the ground strap. 37. Remove the LH hydraulic chain tensioner. 38. Remove the camshaft sprocket bolt. 39. Remove the chain guide bolt. 40. CAUTION: Remove the camshaft sprocket to prevent breaking the cassette and to gain clearance to remove the cylinder head. NOTE: Hold the chain and cassette with a rubber band to aid in removal and prevent the chain from falling into the cylinder block Remove the LH camshaft sprocket from the cassette. 41. Remove the eight 12 mm (0.47 inch) and the two 8 mm (0.31 inch) bolts in the sequence shown and remove the LH cylinder head. - Discard the head gaskets. - Discard the cylinder head bolts. 42. Clean the gasket mating surfaces. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
