2160.html,Camshaft Timing — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,19,"Tighten the bolts. 1 Tighten the special tool top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 2 Tighten the camshaft bolt. 25. Install the LH camshaft tensioner. 26. Inst || tighten the top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 20. Loosen the LH camshaft sprocket bolt. 21. Loosen the top two clamp bolts on the special tool to allow the || torque adapter (303-565) to loosen the camshaft sprocket bolt. Using the special tool, loosen the RH camshaft sprocket bolt. 10. NOTE: The camshaft timing slots are o || torque adapter (303-565) to tighten the camshaft sprocket bolt. Tighten the bolts. 1 Tighten the special tool top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 2 Tighten t",10 Nm;89 inch,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;303-565;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Camshaft Timing — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Timing Components >> Service and Repair >> Camshaft Timing Camshaft Timing Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Timing Special Tool(s) 1. With the vehicle in neutral, position it on a hoist. 2. Remove the intake manifold . 3. Remove the fuel supply manifold. 4. Remove the accessory drive belt. 5. Remove the thermostat housing . 6. Remove the roller followers. 7. NOTE: You must retime the LH and RH camshafts when either camshaft is disturbed. Turn the crankshaft clockwise to position the number one cylinder at top dead center (TDC). 8. NOTE: Late build pulley shown, early build pulley similar. NOTE: The special tool must be installed on the damper and should contact the engine block to position the engine at TDC. Install the special tool. 9. CAUTION: The right-hand camshaft sprocket bolt is a left-hand threaded bolt. NOTE: If necessary, use camshaft gear torque adapter (303-565) to loosen the camshaft sprocket bolt. Using the special tool, loosen the RH camshaft sprocket bolt. 10. NOTE: The camshaft timing slots are off-center. Position the camshaft timing slots below the centerline of the camshaft to correctly fit the special tools. Install the special tools on the front of the RH cylinder head. 11. Remove the RH lower splash shield. 12. Remove the RH camshaft tensioner. 13. NOTE: Leave the top two special tool clamp bolts loose. Install the special tools on the rear of the RH cylinder head. 14. Install the special tool. 15. CAUTION: The right-hand camshaft sprocket bolt is a left-hand threaded bolt. NOTE: If necessary, use camshaft gear torque adapter (303-565) to tighten the camshaft sprocket bolt. Tighten the bolts. 1 Tighten the special tool top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 2 Tighten the camshaft bolt. 16. Install the RH camshaft tensioner. 17. Install the RH lower splash shield. 18. Remove the LH camshaft tensioner. 19. Install the special tools on the front of the LH cylinder head and tighten the top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 20. Loosen the LH camshaft sprocket bolt. 21. Loosen the top two clamp bolts on the special tool to allow the camshaft sprocket to rotate freely. 22. NOTE: The camshaft timing slots are off-center. Position the camshaft timing slots below the centerline of the camshaft to correctly fit the special tools. Install the special tools on the rear of the LH cylinder head. 23. Install the special tool. 24. Tighten the bolts. 1 Tighten the special tool top two clamp bolts to 10 Nm (89 inch lbs.). 2 Tighten the camshaft bolt. 25. Install the LH camshaft tensioner. 26. Install the roller followers. 27. Install the thermostat housing . 28. Install the accessory drive belt. 29. Install the fuel supply manifold. 30. Install the intake manifold . 31. Install the RH valve cover. 32. Install the LH valve cover. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2161.html,"Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Drive Cassette, LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals",Engine,17,Tighten bolt to 45 Nm (33 ft. lbs.) . ^ Stage 2: Tighten bolt an additional 90 degrees. 9. Install the engine front cover. 10. Time the engine. scientia non olet · Abo || tighten the camshaft sprocket bolt. 6. Install the primary chain and gear. 7. Install the primary drive chain tensioner. 8. Hold the crankshaft from turning and tighte,45 Nm;90 degrees,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NOTE,"Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Drive Cassette, LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Timing Components >> Service and Repair >> Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Drive Cassette, LH Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Drive Cassette, LH Timing Drive Components - Camshaft Drive Cassette, LH Special Tool(s) Removal 1. Remove the intake manifold . 2. Remove LH valve cover. 3. Remove the RH valve cover. 4. Remove the fuel supply manifold. 5. Remove the engine front cover. 6. Remove the thermostat housing . 7. Remove all of the roller followers. 8. NOTE: You must retime the LH and RH camshafts when either camshaft is disturbed. Turn the crankshaft clockwise to position number one cylinder at TDC. 9. Remove the LH camshaft chain tensioner. 10. Loosen the LH camshaft sprocket bolt. ^ Install the special tools to hold the camshaft sprocket. ^ Loosen but do not remove the bolt. 11. Remove the tool and bolt. 12. Hold the crankshaft from turning and loosen the jackshaft sprocket bolt. 13. Remove the primary chain tensioner. 14. Remove the primary chain and jackshaft sprocket. 15. Remove the camshaft drive cassette. 1. Remove the chain guide bolts. 2. Remove the sprockets. 3. Lift the chain and guide up and out of the cylinder head. 16. Clean all surfaces. Clean all foreign material from engine. Installation 1. Install the chain guide through the cylinder head. 2. Install the chain. 3. Install the new chain Guide bolts. 4. NOTE: The camshaft chain sprockets must be orientated correctly. Install the chain lower sprocket and the camshaft sprocket. 5. Install, but do not tighten the camshaft sprocket bolt. 6. Install the primary chain and gear. 7. Install the primary drive chain tensioner. 8. Hold the crankshaft from turning and tighten the jackshaft sprocket bolt in two stages. ^ Stage 1: Tighten bolt to 45 Nm (33 ft. lbs.) . ^ Stage 2: Tighten bolt an additional 90 degrees. 9. Install the engine front cover. 10. Time the engine. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
