2184.html,Water Pump: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Interior,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NOTE,"Water Pump: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Water Pump >> Service and Repair Water Pump: Service and Repair Water Pump Material Removal and Installation 1. Drain the engine cooling system . 2. Remove the accessory drive belt. 3. Remove the fan shroud and fan blade assembly. 4. Remove the belt idler pulley. 5. Slide the water bypass hose clamp back. 6. Disconnect the heater hose at the water pump. 1 Release the clamp. 2 Remove the hose. 7. Disconnect the lower radiator hose at the water pump. 1 Release the clamp. 2 Remove the hose. 8. Remove the water pump pulley. 9. Remove the water pump. 10. NOTE: Use metal surface cleaner and a suitable plastic or wooden scraper to clean the sealing surfaces. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
