2269.html,Exhaust System: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,2,torque prevailing design. Use only new fasteners with the same part number as the original. Torque values must be used as specified during reassembly to make sure of,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Exhaust System: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Exhaust System >> Description and Operation Exhaust System: Description and Operation Exhaust System Exhaust System The exhaust system : ^ is constructed of stainless steel ^ has a dual converter Y-pipe ^ has a dual three-way catalytic converter ^ has a muffler and resonator assembly CAUTION: Do not use oil or grease-based lubricants on the insulators. They may cause deterioration to the rubber. CAUTION: Oil or grease-based lubricant on the insulators may cause the exhaust hanger insulator to separate from the exhaust hanger bracket during vehicle operation. Exhaust fasteners are of a torque prevailing design. Use only new fasteners with the same part number as the original. Torque values must be used as specified during reassembly to make sure of correct retention of exhaust components. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
