2544.html,Evaporative Emission Control Canister: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CANISTER;EMISSION;EVAP;EVAPORATIVE;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;WARNING,"Evaporative Emission Control Canister: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Emission Control Systems >> Evaporative Emissions System >> Evaporative Emission Control Canister >> Service and Repair Evaporative Emission Control Canister: Service and Repair EVAPORATIVE EMISSION CANISTER REMOVAL WARNING: - The evaporative emissions system contains fuel vapor and condensed fuel vapor. Although not present in large quantities, it still presents the danger of explosion or fire. Disconnect the battery ground cable from the battery to minimize the possibility of an electrical spark occurring, which can cause a fire or explosion if fuel vapor or liquefied fuel are present in the area. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury. - Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near fuel related components. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and can be ignited. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury. 1. Lower and remove the spare tire. 2. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 3. Raise the vehicle on a hoist. 4. Remove the evaporative emission (EVAP) canister tray mounting bolts. 5. Slightly lower the rear of the EVAP canister assembly to allow access to the top of the assembly. 6. Disconnect the vapor hose from the passenger side EVAP canister and tilt the assembly to allow access to the driver side EVAP canister. 7. Disconnect the vent solenoid electrical connector and the wiring pin-type retainer. Disconnect the vapor hose. 8. Position the EVAP canister assembly on a firm flat surface. 9. Disconnect the vapor crossover tube and the vent solenoid vapor hose. 10. Remove the tie strap from the driver side EVAP canister. 11. Remove the driver side EVAP canister and the vent solenoid as an assembly. 12. Remove the tie strap and vapor crossover tube from the passenger side EVAP canister. Remove the passenger side EVAP canister. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: Lubricate all O-ring seals with O-ring seal lubricant. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Leak test the evaporative emissions system . Evaporative Emission System Leak Test - Carry out the evaporative emissions repair verification drive cycle. Evaporative Emission Repair Verification Drive Cycle scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
