2597.html,Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FUEL FILTERS;LEMON,Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Filter >> Description and Operation >> Gasoline Fuel System Gasoline Fuel System FUEL FILTERS The system contains four filtering or screening devices. Refer to the individual component pictorial for location. 1. The fuel intake sock or screen is a tine nylon mesh sock mounted on the intake side of the fuel pump. It is part of the assembly and cannot be serviced separately. 2. The filter/screen at the fuel rail port of the Injectors is part of the fuel injector assembly and cannot be serviced separately. 3. The filter/screen at fuel inlet side of the fuel pressure regulator is part of the regulator assembly and cannot be serviced separately. 4. The fuel filter assembly is located between the fuel pump (tank) and the pressure test point (schrader valve) or Injectors. This filter may be serviced. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
2598.html,Natural Gas Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FILTER;HIGH PRESSURE FUEL;LEMON,Natural Gas Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Filter >> Description and Operation >> Natural Gas Fuel System Natural Gas Fuel System HIGH PRESSURE FUEL FILTER Fuel Filter: The high pressure fuel filter (Figure 83) is used to protect the engine fuel system components. A natural gas coalescing and particulate filter is positioned on the high pressure side of the fuel system just prior to the pressure regulator. The filter is part of the regulator assembly. The filter can be disassembled to service the element. The drain plug on the bottom of the housing can be removed to drain any water that accumulates. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
