2602.html,Fuel Injector: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,Fuel Injector: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Injector >> Service Precautions Fuel Injector: Service Precautions CAUTION: Do not apply battery positive voltage (B+) directly to the fuel injector electrical connector terminals. The solenoids may be damaged internally in a matter of seconds. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
2603.html,Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;FUEL INJECTOR;LEMON;VPWR,"Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Injector >> Description and Operation >> Gasoline Fuel System Gasoline Fuel System FUEL INJECTOR Fuel Injectors: The fuel injector (Figure 74) is a solenoid -operated valve that meters fuel flow to the engine. The fuel injector is opened and closed a constant number of times per crankshaft revolution. The amount of fuel is controlled by the length of time the fuel injector is held open. The fuel injector is normally closed and is operated by 12 volt VPWR from the electronic engine control power relay. The ground signal is controlled by the PCM. CAUTION: Do not apply battery positive voltage (B+) directly to the fuel injector electrical connector terminals. The solenoids may be damaged internally in a matter of seconds. The injector is the deposit resistant injection (DRI) type and does not have to be cleaned. However, it can be flow checked and, if found outside of specification, the fuel injector should be replaced. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2604.html,Natural Gas Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FUEL INJECTOR;LEMON;VPWR,"Natural Gas Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Injector >> Description and Operation >> Natural Gas Fuel System Natural Gas Fuel System FUEL INJECTOR (S) Fuel Injector: The fuel injector (Figure 81) is a solenoid -operated valve that meters fuel flow to the engine. The fuel injector is opened and closed every other crankshaft revolution. The amount of fuel is controlled by the length of time the fuel injector is held open. The fuel injector is normally closed and is operated by 12 volt VPWR from the power relay. The ground signal is controlled by the PCM. The fuel injectors are used to meter natural gas to each combustion cylinder. Although the natural gas fuel injectors appear very similar to some gasoline fuel injectors, they are unique. Flow capacity of these fuel injectors is 6 to 12 times as large as various gasoline fuel injectors. Electrical resistance is much lower than typical gasoline fuel injectors ( 4.6 ohms as opposed to 14.5 ohms ). To accommodate this lower resistance, a fuel injector driver module is used to convert the PCM fuel injector driver signal to the signal required by the fuel injector. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2605.html,Fuel Injector: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;FUEL INJECTORS;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;WARNING,"Fuel Injector: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Injector >> Service and Repair Fuel Injector: Service and Repair FUEL INJECTORS REMOVAL WARNING: - Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related components. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and may be ignited. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. - Fuel in the fuel system remains under high pressure even when the engine is not running. Before working on or disconnecting any of the fuel lines or fuel system components, the fuel system pressure must be relieved. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. 1. Remove the fuel injection supply manifold. 2. Remove the fuel injectors from the fuel injection supply manifold. 3. Inspect the O-ring seals from each fuel injector . Install new O-ring seals. INSTALLATION 1. CAUTION: Use O-ring seals that are made of special fuel-resistant material. Use of ordinary O-ring seals can cause the fuel system to leak. Do not reuse the O-ring seals. NOTE: Lubricate the new O-ring seals with clean engine oil to aid installation. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
