2628.html,Fuel Tank Draining — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DRAINING;FUEL TANK;LEMON;WARNING,"Fuel Tank Draining — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Tank >> Service and Repair >> Fuel Tank Draining Fuel Tank Draining FUEL TANK DRAINING WARNING: Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related component. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and may be ignited, resulting in possible personal injury. 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. Remove the fuel filler cap . 3. Raise and support the vehicle. 4. Disconnect the fuel filler tube at the fuel tank . 5. Use the fuel storage tanker to siphon the fuel through the fuel tank opening. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2629.html,Fuel Tank — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;EVAP;FUEL TANK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL;WARNING,"Fuel Tank — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Tank >> Service and Repair >> Fuel Tank Fuel Tank FUEL TANK REMOVAL WARNING: Do not smoke, carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related component. Highly flammable mixtures are always present an may be ignited, resulting in possible personal injury. 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. Relieve the fuel system pressure. 3. Raise and support the vehicle. 4. Drain the fuel tank . 5. If equipped, remove fuel tank skid plate rear retaining bolts. 6. If equipped, remove fuel tank skid plate front retaining bolts and the skid plate. 7. Disconnect the fuel filler pipe and the evaporative emissions ( EVAP ) tube. 8. Disconnect the fuel supply tube and the EVAP tube. 9. Use a suitable jack to support the fuel tank . 10. Remove the bolt and position the rear fuel tank support strap aside. 11. Remove the bolt and position the front fuel tank support strap aside. 12. Partially lower the fuel tank . 13. Disconnect the fuel pump electrical connector. 14. Lower and remove the fuel tank . INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
