2981.html,Axle Shaft Assembly: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Suspension,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;WARNING,"Axle Shaft Assembly: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Drive Axles, Bearings and Joints >> Axle Shaft Assembly >> Description and Operation Axle Shaft Assembly: Description and Operation Front Drive Halfshafts Front Drive Halfshaft and Joint Assembly ^ The inboard front wheel halfshaft joint and the outboard CV joint connect to a splined interconnecting shaft. A retainer circlip retains the inboard CV joint to the splined interconnecting shaft. ^ CAUTION: Always install the halfshaft assembly with a new retainer circlip. A retainer circlip retains the inboard CV joint housing to the front drive axle. ^ CAUTION: Always install the halfshaft with a new front axle wheel hub retainer. A front axle wheel hub retainer secures the side shaft assembly to the wheel hub. Halfshaft Handling CAUTION: Never pick up or hold the halfshaft assembly only by the inboard front wheel halfshaft joint or the outboard CV joint. Handle all halfshaft components carefully during removal and installation? and disassembly and assembly procedures. ^ To separate the outboard joint from the hub, press the joint from the hub. ^ To separate the inboard CV joint housing from the front drive axle, apply a load to the back face of the inboard CV joint housing to overcome the retainer circlip. ^ Do not over-angle the CV joints. ^ Damage will occur to an assembled inboard CV joint if it is over-plunged outward from the joint housing. ^ Never use a hammer to remove or install the halfshaft assembly. ^ Never use the halfshaft assembly as a lever to position other components. Always support the tree end of the halfshaft assembly. ^ Do not allow the front wheel halfshaft joint boots to contact sharp edges or hot exhaust components. ^ Handle the halfshaft assembly only by the interconnecting shaft to avoid pull-apart and potential damage to the CV joints. ^ Do not drop an assembled halfshaft. The impact will cut the boots from the inside without evidence of external damage. ^ Keep CV joints clean and maintain correct grease refill when installing new halfshaft components. ^ Inspect all machined surfaces and splines for damage. ^ The inboard front wheel halfshaft joint is repairable. ^ The side shaft assembly (interconnecting shaft and outboard CV joint) is not repairable, other than the boot. Install a new assembly if worn/damaged. Wheel and Tire Balancing, Rear WARNING: Do not balance the front wheels and tires while mounted on the vehicle. Possible tire disintegration, differential or halfshaft failure can result, causing personal injury or extensive component damage. Use an off-vehicle wheel and tire balanced only. Hoisting CAUTION: Use a frame-contact hoist only. Vehicle or component damage can result if other types of hoists are used. Never raise the vehicle using the halfshafts as lift points. Undercoating and Rustproofing During undercoating and rustproofing procedures, protect the boots from the coating materials. Foreign materials on the rubber boots will cause extreme advanced wear. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
