2983.html,Component Tests and General Diagnostics — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NOTE,"Component Tests and General Diagnostics — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Drive Axles, Bearings and Joints >> Axle Shaft Assembly >> Testing and Inspection >> Component Tests and General Diagnostics Component Tests and General Diagnostics Front Drive Halfshafts Halfshafts, Front Wheel NOTE: Do not make any repairs to the halfshaft assembly unless disassembly and inspection reveals wear/damage. NOTE: Inspect for, and remove, indentations (dimples) in the front wheel halfshaft joint boot convolutions. ^ Inspect the front wheel halfshaft joint boots for cracks tears and splits. ^ Inspect the vehicle underbody for grease splatter near the outboard and inboard front wheel halfshaft joint boots. This is an indication of boot/clamp damage. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2984.html,Removal and Installation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Suspension;Wiring;Interior,15,"tighten the front axle wheel hub retainer. NOTE: When installing either halfshaft assembly, turn the knuckle into a LH turn, and install the outboard CV joint into the",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE;WARNING,"Removal and Installation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Drive Axles, Bearings and Joints >> Axle Shaft Assembly >> Service and Repair >> Removal and Installation Removal and Installation Halfshaft Special Tool(s) Removal and Installation NOTE: Except where noted, this procedure applies to both front halfshaft assemblies. Use only the procedure steps necessary for the halfshaft requiring removal/installation. LH/RH halfshaft 1. Remove the center cap from the front wheel. 2. Loosen the front axle wheel hub retainer. 3. Raise and support the vehicle. 4. Remove the front wheel and tire assembly. 5. Remove and discard the front axle wheel hub retainer. 6. WARNING: Remove or tape the brake pads, to prevent them from falling out of the anchor plate. CAUTION: To prevent damage to the brake hose, do not allow the disc brake caliper to hang suspended from the hose. Remove the two bolts and position the disc brake caliper aside. 7. Remove the cotter pin and the nut. 8. CAUTION: Do not damage the tie-rod dust boot when installing the special tool. NOTE: Remove the adapter from the ball end of the special tool. Apply a small amount of grease to the tie-rod stud and to the ball of the special tool. Using the special tool, separate the tie-rod end from the knuckle. 9. Unclip the anti-lock sensor wiring harness from the locators. 10. Remove the bolt retaining the anti-lock sensor wiring harness to the knuckle. RH halfshaft only 11. Remove the nuts and disconnect the RH shock absorber from the front suspension lower arm. LH/RH halfshaft 12. CAUTION: Do not allow the knuckle to hang freely. It is possible to overextend and internally separate the inner CV joint from the housing. Remove the pinch bolt and disconnect the upper ball joint from the knuckle. 13. CAUTION: Do not use a hammer to separate the outboard CV joint from the hub. Damage to the threads and internal CV joint components may result. Using the special tool. press the outboard CV joint until it is loose in the hub. 14. NOTE: Due to a tight fit between the halfshaft assembly and the hub, to remove the LH outboard CV joint from the hub, turn the knuckle into a RH turn, and remove the joint from the hub from the RH side of the knuckle (as facing the knuckle). To remove the RH outboard CV joint from the hub, turn the knuckle into a LH turn, and remove the joint from the hub from the LH side of the knuckle (as facing the knuckle). Remove the outboard CV joint from the hub. 1. Rotate the knuckle. 2. Compress the outboard joint. 3. Remove the outboard joint from the hub. LH halfshaft only 15. CAUTION: Do not damage the axle shaft oil seal or the machined sealing surface on the inboard CV joint housing. NOTE: A circlip retains the inboard CV joint housing to the differential side gear in the axle. Using the special tool, disengage the LH inboard CV joint housing from the differential side gear. RH halfshaft only 16. CAUTION: Do not damage the axle shaft oil seal or the machined sealing surface on the inboard CV joint housing. NOTE: A circlip retains the inboard CV joint housing to the axle shaft in the axle tube. Using the special tool, disengage the RH inboard CV joint housing from the axle tube. 17. CAUTION: Do not damage the axle shaft oil seal, the machined sealing surface on the inboard CV joint housing, or the axle shaft splines. CAUTION: Install a new retainer circlip on the outboard splined end of the axle shaft before reseating the axle shaft in the differential side gear. Pull the knuckle, the halfshaft, and the axle shaft away from the axle tube, and separate the inboard CV joint housing from the axle shaft. LH/RH halfshaft 18. Remove the halfshaft assembly from the vehicle. 19. CAUTION: Always install the halfshaft with a new retainer circlip and a new front axle wheel hub retainer. CAUTION: On the RH side only, check the retainer circlip engagement after reseating the axle shaft and after installing the halfshaft in the axle. On the LH side only, check the retainer circlip engagement after installing the halfshaft in the axle. When seated, the retainer circlip will lock the axle shaft and the inboard CV joint housing to the axle. CAUTION: Never use power tools to tighten the front axle wheel hub retainer. NOTE: When installing either halfshaft assembly, turn the knuckle into a LH turn, and install the outboard CV joint into the hub from the LH side of the knuckle (as facing the knuckle). NOTE: Support the front suspension lower arm before attempting to connect the upper ball joint to the knuckle or the components will not be able to reach one another. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
2985.html,Disassembly and Assembly — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission,23,"Tighten the through-bolt until the special tool is in the closed position. Using the special tool, install the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 14. Install the || Tighten the through-bolt until the special tool is in the closed position. Using the special tool, install the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 4. Position the",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Disassembly and Assembly — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Drive Axles, Bearings and Joints >> Axle Shaft Assembly >> Service and Repair >> Disassembly and Assembly Disassembly and Assembly Halfshaft Special Tools: Special Tool(s) Disassembly 1. Remove the halfshaft assembly from the vehicle. 2. CAUTION: Do not damage the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. Remove the two front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 3. Slide the inboard front wheel halfshaft joint boot from the constant velocity (CV) joint housing. 4. Separate the CV joint housing from the CV joint. 5. Index-mark the interconnecting shaft and the inboard CV joint. 6. Remove the retainer circlip. 7. Remove the inboard CV joint. 8. Remove the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 9. Remove the two front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 10. Remove the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 11. CAUTION: Do not disassemble the side shaft assembly. Install a new assembly if worn or damaged. Thoroughly wipe all of the grease from the side shaft assembly and the boots. Inspect all of the components for wear and damage. Discard the components, as necessary. Assembly 1. Pack the outboard CV joint with grease. 1. Use 185 grams (4.35 ounces) of grease. 2. Spread any remaining grease evenly inside the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 2. NOTE: Clean the front wheel halfshaft joint boot mounting surfaces of excess grease before installing the boot. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot and the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 1. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 2. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 3. NOTE: Tighten the through-bolt until the special tool is in the closed position. Using the special tool, install the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 4. Position the inboard front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamp. 5. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 6. NOTE: Align the index marks. Install the inboard CV joint. 7. Install the retainer circlip. 8. Lubricate the inboard CV joint needle bearings. 9. Fill the CV joint housing with 200 grams (4.71 ounces) of grease. 10. Position the CV joint housing onto the inboard CV joint. 11. NOTE: Clean the front wheel halfshaft joint boot mounting surfaces of excess grease before installing the boot. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot and the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamp. 1. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot. 2. Position the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamp. 12. Set the halfshaft assembled length to specification. 1. Measure the entire assembly length. 2. Push in or pull out on the inner joint as necessary to adjust the halfshaft assembled length to specification. 3. Hold the inner joint to prevent the assembled length from changing, and insert a small flat blade screwdriver between the boot and the joint to equalize the pressure. 13. NOTE: Tighten the through-bolt until the special tool is in the closed position. Using the special tool, install the front wheel halfshaft joint boot clamps. 14. Install the halfshaft assembly in the vehicle. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
