3367.html,Suspension: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body,2,torque value must be used during assembly to make sure correct part retention. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Suspension: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Steering and Suspension >> Suspension >> Description and Operation Suspension: Description and Operation Rear Suspension Components Part 1 Of 2: Part 2 Of 2: Rear Axle Bumpers The rear axle bumpers are used to prevent metal-to-metal contact between the rear axle and the frame. Rear Spring Semi-elliptic, leaf-type rear springs are used for the rear suspension . Shock Absorbers The shock absorbers provide the necessary suspension dampening control. Stabilizer Bar The rear stabilizer bar transmits forces to control vehicle roll during cornering. Suspension Fasteners New fasteners must be installed if the old Fasteners are loosened or removed. New parts with the same part number or an equivalent part must be installed if installation is necessary. Do not use a part of lesser quality or substitute design. The specified torque value must be used during assembly to make sure correct part retention. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3368.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Steering and Suspension >> Suspension >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Inspection and Verification 1. Road test. - Verify the customer's concern by performing a road test on a smooth road. If any vibrations are apparent, refer to Noise, Vibration and Harshness Diagnosis. 2. Inspect tires . - Check the tire pressure with all normal loads in the vehicle and the tires cold. For additional information, refer to the vehicle certification (VC) label. - Verify that all tires are sized to specification. - Inspect the tires for incorrect wear and damage. 3. Inspect chassis and underbody. - Remove any excessive accumulation of mud, dirt or road deposits from the chassis and underbody. 4. Inspect for aftermarket equipment. - Check for aftermarket changes to the steering , suspension , wheel and tire components (such as competition, heavy duty, etc.) The specifications shown do not apply to vehicles equipped with aftermarket equipment. Visual Inspection Chart 5. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported condition is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 6. If the fault is not visually evident, determine the symptom and proceed to the symptom chart. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
