3535.html,Glossary of Terms Used While Performing Tests — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;GLOSSARY;LEMON,"Glossary of Terms Used While Performing Tests — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Glossary of Terms Used While Performing Tests Glossary of Terms Used While Performing Tests GLOSSARY Secondary Air Bag Warning The secondary air bag warning is an audible fault format that consists of five sets of five tone bursts, with each set of five tone bursts separated by a five second quiet period. One tone burst cycle will consist of one second ON and one second OFF . This series of five activations is repeated every 30 minutes . Air Bag /Pretensioner Restraint System Diagnostic Tools Air bag/pretensioner restraint system diagnostic tools are used to simulate the equivalent resistance of an air bag module or safety belt pretensioner during certain diagnostic procedures. Disconnect the Component Disconnect the component means disconnect the component vehicle harness connector, not to remove the component. Do not reconnect a disconnected component unless instructed to do so. Deactivate the System Deactivate the system means to carry out the deactivation procedure. Depower the System Depower the system means to disconnect the battery and remove the restraints control module (RCM) fuse. Prove Out the System Prove out the system means to turn the ignition switch from the OFF to the ON position, and to visually monitor the air bag indicator with the air bag modules and safety belt pretensioners or restraint system diagnostic tools installed. Reactivate the System Reactivate the system means to carry out the reactivation procedure. Repower the System Repower the system means to remove any restraint system diagnostic tools that may have been installed, turn the ignition ON, install the RCM fuse, and connect the battery ground cable. Reconnect the System Reconnect the system means to reconnect all system components. Install a New Component Install a new component means to remove the existing component and install a new authorized part obtained from Ford Customer Service Division. Verify the System Verify the system means to prove out the system with restraint system diagnostic tools installed in place of SRS components. Air Bag Reconnect Checklist The checklist below should be completed following diagnosis or repair of any air bag system concern: - All restraint system diagnostic tools removed? - All in-seat harness connectors connected? - All air bag modules connected? - Safety belt pretensioner connectors connected? - Restraints control module (RCM) connected? - All sensors (front and side impact sensors) connected? - Safety canopy modules connected? - Safety canopy bridge resistor(s) connected? - RCM fuse installed? - Battery connected? scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3536.html,Test A — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;A1-A3;A3-A5;A5-A7;BATTERY FEED;CONTINUOUSLY;GROUND;ILLUMINATED;INDICATOR IS;LEMON;LOSS OF;NO COMMUNICATION;OR INOPERATIVE;OR LOSS OF;PINPOINT TEST;RCM DISCONNECTED;SIGNAL;START;THE AIR BAG;WARNING,"Test A — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test A Test A PINPOINT TEST A: THE AIR BAG WARNING INDICATOR IS ILLUMINATED CONTINUOUSLY - RCM DISCONNECTED OR INOPERATIVE, LOSS OF BATTERY FEED, OR LOSS OF SIGNAL GROUND Test A1-A3: Test A3-A5: Test A5-A7: Normal Operation During normal operation, the air bag indicator will illuminate continuously for approximately six seconds and then go out after the ignition switch is placed in the ON or START position and no air bag fault exists. The air bag indicator will remain illuminated continuously after five cycles of a lamp fault code (LFC), if a fault exists. Be sure to cycle the ignition switch and look for an approximate 6 second indicator prove-out without LFCs. The restraints control module (RCM) will communicate diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs) to the scan tool through the data link connector (DLC). If the scan tool displays NO COMMUNICATION when retrieving continuous DTCs, GO to Pinpoint Test R to troubleshoot the system. Test R Possible Causes An air bag indicator that is illuminated continuously can be caused by one of the following: - RCM disconnected from the vehicle harness - a loss of RCM signal ground - a faulted RCM - wiring, terminals, or connectors - a loss of RCM ignition feed - a faulted instrument cluster module scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3537.html,Test B — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;B1-B2;B1869;B2-B5;B5-B7;CIRCUIT OPEN;DTC B1869;GROUND;INDICATOR;LAMP AIR BAG;LEMON;OR SHORT TO;PINPOINT TEST;START;WARNING,"Test B — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test B Test B PINPOINT TEST B: DTC B1869 - LAMP AIR BAG WARNING INDICATOR CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND Test B1-B2: Test B2-B5: Test B5-B7: Normal Operation During normal operation, the air bag indicator will illuminate continuously for approximately 6 seconds and then go out after the ignition switch is placed to the ON or START position and no air bag fault exists. The air bag indicator will remain illuminated continuously after five cycles of a lamp fault code (LFC), if a fault exists. If the restraints control module (RCM) detects an open or short to ground on the air bag warning indicator circuit, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B1869 in memory. Possible Causes An open air bag indicator circuit can be caused by: - wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulted RCM. - a faulted instrument cluster module. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3538.html,Test C — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIR BAG;B1870;C1-C2;C2-C5;CIRCUIT SHORT;DTC B1870;INDICATOR;LEMON;PINPOINT TEST;START;TO BATTERY;WARNING,"Test C — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test C Test C PINPOINT TEST C: DTC B1870 - AIR BAG WARNING INDICATOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY Test C1-C2: Test C2-C5: Normal Operation During normal operation, the air bag indicator will illuminate continuously for approximately 6 seconds and then go out after the ignition switch is placed to the ON or START and no air bag fault exists. The air bag indicator will remain illuminated continuously after five cycles of a lamp fault code (LFC), if a fault exists. If the restraints control module detects a short to battery on the air bag warning indicator circuit, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B1870 in memory. If any other DTCs are detected with this DTC active, the secondary air bag warning will be activated. Possible Causes An air bag indicator circuit short to battery can be caused by: - wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulted RCM. - a faulted instrument cluster module. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3539.html,Test D — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIR BAG TONE;B1891;CIRCUIT SHORT;D2-D5;DTC B1891;INDICATOR;LEMON;LFC 53;PINPOINT TEST;TO BATTERY;WARNING,"Test D — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test D Test D PINPOINT TEST D: LFC 53/DTC B1891 - AIR BAG TONE WARNING INDICATOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY Test D1: Test D2-D5: Normal Operation The connection between the instrument cluster module and RCM is used to signal a chime if the primary air bag indicator is inoperative and another SRS fault exists. The restraints control module (RCM) monitors this connection to the instrument cluster module at C2041a pin 22. If the RCM detects a circuit failure on the connection to the cluster, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B1891 in memory and flash lamp fault code (LFC) 53 (or a higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Possible Causes An air bag tone warning circuit short to battery or ignition can be caused by: - wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulted instrument cluster module. - a faulted RCM. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3540.html,Test E — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIR BAG TONE;B1892;CIRCUIT SHORT;DTC B1892;E2-E4;E4-E7;INDICATOR;LEMON;LFC 53;OPEN;PINPOINT TEST;TO GROUND OR;WARNING,"Test E — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test E Test E PINPOINT TEST E: LFC 53/DTC B1892 - AIR BAG TONE WARNING INDICATOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND OR OPEN Test E1: Test E2-E4: Test E4-E7: Normal Operation The connection between the instrument cluster module and RCM is used to signal a chime if the primary air bag indicator is inoperative and another SRS fault exists. The restraints control module (RCM) monitors this connection to the instrument cluster module at C2041a pin 22. If the RCM detects a circuit failure on the connection to the cluster, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B1892 in memory and flash lamp fault code (LFC) 53 (or a higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Possible Causes An air bag tone warning indicator circuit short to ground or open can be caused by: - wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulted instrument cluster module. - a faulted RCM. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3541.html,Test F — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,2,tightening torque of the restraints control module (RCM) retaining bolts is critical for correct air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) operation. Refer to Restra || torque values. NOTE: A resistance difference as low as 10 ohms can set the LFC. The restraints control module (RCM) monitors the resistance between the ground connect,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIR BAG;B1921;CIRCUIT OPEN;DIAGNOSTIC;DTC B1921;F1-F3;F4-F6;GROUND;LEMON;LFC 14;MONITOR;NOTE;PINPOINT TEST;WARNING,"Test F — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test F Test F PINPOINT TEST F: LFC 14/DTC B1921 - AIR BAG DIAGNOSTIC MONITOR GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN Test F1-F3: Test F4-F6: Normal Operation WARNING: The tightening torque of the restraints control module (RCM) retaining bolts is critical for correct air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) operation. Refer to Restraints Control Module (RCM) for correct torque values. NOTE: A resistance difference as low as 10 ohms can set the LFC. The restraints control module (RCM) monitors the resistance between the ground connections at the mounting bolts and the reference ground at C2041a pin 16, circuit 570 (BK/WH). If the RCM detects a difference in resistance, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B1921 in memory and flash lamp fault code (LFC) 14 (or higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Possible Causes A resistance difference between the RCM mounting bolts ground and harness ground can be caused by: - the RCM is not securely mounted to the RCM bracket. - damaged wiring, terminals, or connectors. - RCM is faulted. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3542.html,Test G — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,10,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;B2292;DTC B2292;G10-G11;G12-G13;G14-G15;G16-G17;G18-G19;G2-G3;G4-G6;G6-G8;G8-G10;LEMON;LFC 33 AND;PINPOINT TEST;PRETENSIONER;RESTRAINT;SAFETY BELT;STATUS;SYSTEM,"Test G — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test G Test G PINPOINT TEST G: LFC 33 AND 34/DTC B2292 - RESTRAINT SYSTEM SAFETY BELT PRETENSIONER STATUS Test G1: Test G2-G3: Test G4-G6: Test G6-G8: Test G8-G10: Test G10-G11: Test G12-G13: Test G14-G15: Test G16-G17: Test G18-G19: Normal Operation The restraints control module (RCM) checks all of the safety belt retractor pretensioners for faults. If the RCM detects one of the following faults on any of the safety belt retractor pretensioner circuits, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B2292 in memory and flash, depending on the fault indicator, either lamp fault code (LFC) 33 or 34 (or higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Fault Conditions The RCM monitors for the following fault conditions: - low resistance. - high resistance or circuit open. - circuit short to voltage. - circuit short to ground. Possible Causes A safety belt retractor pretensioner status fault can be caused by: - damaged wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulty pretensioner. - RCM is faulted. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3543.html,Test H — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Wiring,17,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIRBAG;B2293;DTC B2293;H11-H12;H13-H15;H15-H16;H17-H19;H19-H20;H2-H3;H20-H22;H22-H24;H24-H25;H3-H5;H5-H7;H7-H8;H9-H11;LEMON;LFC 19 AND;PINPOINT TEST;RESTRAINT;STATUS;SYSTEM,"Test H — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test H Test H PINPOINT TEST H: LFC 19 AND 21/DTC B2293 - RESTRAINT SYSTEM AIRBAG STATUS Test H1: Test H2-H3: Test H3-H5: Test H5-H7: Test H7-H8: Test H9-H11: Test H11-H12: Test H13-H15: Test H15-H16: Test H17-H19: Test H19-H20: Test H20-H22: Test H22-H24: Test H24-H25: Test H26: Test H27: Test H28: Normal Operation The restraints control module (RCM) checks all of the front air bag circuits for faults. If the RCM detects one of the following faults on any of the front air bag circuits, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B2293 in memory and, depending on the fault, flash either lamp fault code (LFC) 19 or 21 (or higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Fault Conditions The RCM monitors for the following fault conditions: - low resistance. - high resistance or circuit open. - circuit short to voltage. - circuit short to ground. Possible Causes A driver air bag status fault can be caused by: - damaged wiring, terminals, or connectors. - driver air bag sub-harness. - a faulty clockspring. - a faulty driver air bag module. - RCM is faulted. A passenger air bag status fault can be caused by: - damaged wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulty passenger air bag module. - faulted RCM. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3544.html,Test I — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,11,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;B2294;C367;CANOPY;DTC B2294;I11-I12;I13-I15;I15-I16;I17-I18;I3-I4;I5-I6;I7-I9;I9-I11;LEMON;LFC 24 AND;MODULE;NOTE;PINPOINT TEST;RESTRAINT;SAFETY;STATUS;SYSTEM,"Test I — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Pinpoint Tests >> Test I Test I PINPOINT TEST I: LFC 24 AND 25/DTC B2294 - RESTRAINT SYSTEM SAFETY CANOPY MODULE STATUS Test I1: Test I2: Test I3: Test I3-I4: Test I5-I6: Test I7-I9: Test I9-I11: Test I11-I12: Test I13-I15: Test I15-I16: Test I17-I18: Normal Operation NOTE: When installing a new restraints control module (RCM), always make sure the correct RCM is being installed. If an incorrect RCM is installed, erroneous DTCs will result. The restraints control module (RCM) checks all safety canopy module circuits for faults. If the RCM detects one of the following faults on any of the safety canopy module circuits, it will store diagnostic trouble code (DTC) B2294 in memory and flash, depending on the fault, either lamp fault code (LFC) 24 or 25 (or higher priority code if one exists) on the air bag indicator. Vehicles may be equipped with optional safety canopy modules. Vehicles not equipped with safety canopy modules will have a safety canopy bridge resistor present at the driver safety canopy module C367 with a cap at the passenger safety canopy module C367 (no connect, circuits are open). Fault Conditions The RCM monitors for the following fault conditions: - low resistance. - high resistance or circuit open. - circuit short to voltage. - circuit short to ground. Possible Causes A safety canopy module status fault can be caused by: - damaged wiring, terminals, or connectors. - a faulty safety canopy bridge resistor. - a faulty safety canopy module. - RCM is faulted. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
