3651.html,"Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals",Engine;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;EQUIPMENT;INTERFERENCE;LEMON;M100CDR;RADIO FREQUENCY;SUPPRESSION,"Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Accessories and Optional Equipment >> Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc >> Description and Operation Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc: Description and Operation RADIO FREQUENCY INTERFERENCE SUPPRESSION EQUIPMENT The audio system consists of the audio unit with digital audio compact disc player. There are 4 audio systems available: - M100CDR - DM100i - CD6 Audiophile in-dash multi-disc audio unit (includes a unique subwoofer) - Adrenaline audio (includes a unique subwoofer) Radio Frequency Interference Suppression Equipment: The radio suppression equipment reduces interference transmitted through the speakers by the engine ignition and electrical systems. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3652.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;VERIFICATION 1,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Accessories and Optional Equipment >> Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern. Visual Inspection Chart: 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of mechanical and electrical damage. 3. If the fault is not visually evident, proceed to Speaker Walk-Around Test and Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode. Speaker Walk-Around Test Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3653.html,Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AUDIO UNIT SELF;CARRY OUT;CLEAR;CLEARED;DIAGNOSTIC MODE;DISPLAY TEST;DOCUMENT;EJECT;FOUND;LEMON;NOTE;SELF FAIL;SELF PASS;SELF TEST;SIGNAL TEST;SOFT LEVELS;TUNE,"Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Accessories and Optional Equipment >> Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc >> Testing and Inspection >> Reading and Clearing Diagnostic Trouble Codes >> Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode Audio Unit Self-Diagnostic Mode AUDIO UNIT SELF-DIAGNOSTIC MODE NOTE: To enter the test or diagnostic mode, the audio unit must be turned on and in tuner mode (AM/FM). 1. The audio unit self-diagnostic mode has 5 tests available: - Preset Button 1 = Audio internal/external SELF TEST. This test is an on-demand self-test. If SELF FAIL is displayed, press TUNE > to scroll view the DTCs stored. Refer to the Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index. If the system is OK, SELF PASS will be displayed. Diagnostic Trouble Code Tests and Associated Procedures - Preset Button 2 = View/Clear continuous DTCs. NO DTCs is displayed if no DTCs are retrieved. If DTCs FOUND is displayed, press TUNE > to view the DTCs retrieved. Refer to the Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index. To clear all DTCs, press the EJECT button. DTCs CLEAR or DTCs CLEARED will be displayed. Diagnostic Trouble Code Tests and Associated Procedures - NOTE: Always DOCUMENT, CLEAR and CARRY OUT the CD6 On-Demand Self-Test again. Preset Button 3 = SIGNAL TEST. This test measures the average strength at the current tuner setting. - Preset Button 4 = Software configuration level. This test queries each radio system controller for its software configuration level. SOFT LEVELS will be displayed upon completion of the query. Press TUNE > to scroll view the software configuration version level. - Preset Button 5 = DISPLAY TEST. This test will light all the audio unit display segments for 5 seconds . When the test is complete, DISPLAY TEST is displayed on the bezel. 2. To enter these tests, press the desired preset button while in the speaker walk-around test or while in the audio unit self-diagnostic mode. 3. To exit the audio unit self-diagnostic mode, turn the ignition switch or the audio unit off. 4. If the concern remains and the fault is not detected, proceed to the Symptom Chart to continue diagnostics. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3654.html,Speaker Walk-Around Test — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AROUND TEST;LEMON;NO CDDJ;NO DJ;NOTE;SPEAKER WALK;SPKR SHORT;SUBWOOFER I;SUBWOOFER II,"Speaker Walk-Around Test — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Accessories and Optional Equipment >> Radio, Stereo, and Compact Disc >> Testing and Inspection >> Reading and Clearing Diagnostic Trouble Codes >> Speaker Walk-Around Test Speaker Walk-Around Test SPEAKER WALK-AROUND TEST NOTE: To enter the test or diagnostic mode, the audio unit must be turned on and in tuner mode (AM/FM). The audio unit self-diagnostic mode tests can only be entered while in the speaker walk-around test. 1. To enter the test, press preset buttons 3 and 6 simultaneously, hold for approximately 3 seconds and then release. 2. The test stops at each speaker and applies a tone to each speaker for approximately 1-2 seconds . Each speaker is tested and shown on the display in the following sequence: RF, LF, LR, RR, SUBWOOFER I, and SUBWOOFER II. 3. The test automatically continues and tests Subwoofer I and Subwoofer II for speaker short and CD/DJ. If a speaker short exists, SPKR SHORT will be displayed. If the vehicle is not equipped with CD/DJ or if the CD/DJ is not responding, NO CDDJ or NO DJ will be displayed. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
