3692.html,Initial Inspection — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;INSPECTION CHART;LEMON;VERIFICATION 1;VISUAL,"Initial Inspection — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Body Control Systems >> Testing and Inspection >> Vehicle Security Module >> Initial Inspection Initial Inspection INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern. 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of electrical damage: VISUAL INSPECTION CHART Electrical - Central junction box (CJB) fuse(s): - 9 (7.5A) - 14 (7.5A) - 15 (7.5A) - 19 (15A) 3. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported concern is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 4. If the cause is not visually evident, connect the diagnostic tool to the data link connector and select the vehicle to be tested from the diagnostic tool menu. If the diagnostic tool does not communicate with the vehicle: - check that the program card is correctly installed. - check the connections to the vehicle. - check the ignition switch position. 5. If the diagnostic tool still does not communicate with the vehicle, refer to the diagnostic tool operating manual. 6. Carry out the diagnostic tool data link test. If the diagnostic tool responds with: - ISO or SCP circuits fault; all electronic control units no response/not equipped, refer to Information Bus (Module Communications Network). - No response/not equipped for vehicle security module, GO to Pinpoint Test A. Pinpoint Tests - System passed, retrieve and record the continuous diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs), erase the continuous DTCs and carry out self-test diagnostics for the vehicle security module. 7. If the DTCs retrieved are related to the concern, go to the Diagnostic Trouble Code Chart to continue diagnostics. Multifunction Electronic Modules 8. If no DTCs related to the concern are retrieved, refer to the appropriate vehicle system to continue diagnostics. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
