3743.html,Drilling Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DRILLING;LEMON;PRECAUTIONS 1,"Drilling Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Frame >> Service Precautions >> Drilling Precautions Drilling Precautions DRILLING PRECAUTIONS 1. If a hole must be drilled in the frame , make sure the hole meets the following requirements: - The hole is at least the specified distance from the edge of the nearest hole. - The edge of the drilled hole is at least the specified distance from the edge or radius of the flange or web. - The hole is at least the specified distance above the frame centerline. - The drilled hole is at least the specified distance from any other existing bracket or component of the frame . scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3744.html,Frame Straightening — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;5D058;5D059;CAUTION;FRAME STRAIGHTENING;LEMON;NOTE;WARNING,"Frame Straightening — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Frame >> Service Precautions >> Frame Straightening Frame Straightening FRAME STRAIGHTENING 1. WARNING: Straightening of front frame rail convolute is prohibited. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. NOTE: A front rail repair kit (5D058 and 5D059) is available. When straightening the frame , make sure the following requirements are met: - CAUTION: Reposition and/or shield any fuel lines, brake lines, or wiring harness or component in the heated area. If heat is needed to straighten a frame member, keep the temperature below 650 °C (1,200 °F) (a dull red glow). A temperature sensitive thermal melt crayon should be used to monitor heat buildup. - Heat should be kept to a minimum area so that the hardness of the metal will not be affected. - Straightening should only be attempted on frames that fail to meet specifications of the diagonal checking method or where damage is apparent. - Straightening should be limited to parts which are not severely bent. - Reposition any fuel lines, brake lines, or wiring harnesses or components. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3745.html,Welding Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;14301;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;PRECAUTIONS 1;WELDING,"Welding Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Frame >> Service Precautions >> Welding Precautions Welding Precautions WELDING PRECAUTIONS 1. If welding must be done on a frame , make sure the following requirements are met: - If the frame is attached to the vehicle, the battery ground cable (14301) must be disconnected before using any electrical welding equipment. - Do not use gas welding equipment; arc welding is the only approved method. - Use a temperature-indicating crayon to make sure that the temperature does not exceed 750 °C (1,400 °F) . - Install new spot-welded components by spot welding where possible. If spot welding is not possible, use puddle welding. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3746.html,Frame: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;5005;5D058;5D059;FRAME AND BODY;LEMON;MOUNTING,"Frame: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Frame >> Description and Operation Frame: Description and Operation FRAME AND BODY MOUNTING Body Support - Radiator Support: Body Support - Number 1: Body Support - Number 3: The frame consists of two steel channel rails, a rear crossmember, additional support crossmembers and a front crossmember. The rails and crossmembers are not to be removed from the frame (5005) for repair except for the spare tire carrier plate. A front frame rail repair kit (5D058 and 5D059) is available if the front rail is to be repaired scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
