3778.html,"Handles, Locks, Latches and Entry Systems — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals",Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ENTRY SYSTEMS;HANDLES;LATCHES AND;LEMON;LOCKS;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF,"Handles, Locks, Latches and Entry Systems — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Locks >> Power Locks >> Description and Operation >> Handles, Locks, Latches and Entry Systems Handles, Locks, Latches and Entry Systems HANDLES, LOCKS, LATCHES AND ENTRY SYSTEMS The hood consists of the following components: - hood latch striker - hood latch - hood latch release handle and cable The front door consists of the following components: - front door latch push button rod - exterior door handle - front door latch - interior door handle - door lock actuator (if equipped) - door lock cylinder - door ajar switch The rear door consists of the following components: - rear door latch push button rod - push button rod remote control - exterior door handle - rear door latch - interior door handle - door lock actuator (if equipped) - door ajar switch For removal and installation of the front door lock actuator, refer to Front Door Latch. For removal and installation of the rear door lock actuator, refer to Rear Door Latch. The tailgate consists of the following components: - tailgate latches - tailgate cables - tailgate latch remote control - tailgate release handle - tailgate lock cylinder The tonneau cover consists of the following components: - bi-fold type cover - front lock cylinder - rear lock cylinder - front latch release cable - rear latch release cable - tonneau cover latches PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Power Door Locks The central security module controls the power door lock and keyless entry system. The lock and unlock operation is carried out by supplying ground to the central security module from the door lock control switch. The normal path of the actuators is to ground through the central security module. The door lock control switch will lock and unlock all doors by grounding the appropriate circuit to the central security module. The central security module then supplies power to the appropriate common actuator circuit to lock or unlock all doors. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3779.html,Autolock Enable/Disable — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Suspension;Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AUTOLOCK;DISABLE;ENABLE;LEMON;NOTE;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;REVERSE;START,"Autolock Enable/Disable — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Locks >> Power Locks >> Description and Operation >> Autolock Enable/Disable Autolock Enable/Disable AUTOLOCK ENABLE/DISABLE Autolock can be enabled/disabled using the following three methods: diagnostic tool, keyless entry keypad, ignition lock cylinder. A manual enable/disable mode allows the autolock feature to be turned off and on. PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Autolocks If the autolock feature is enabled all doors must be closed for the autolock feature to activate. The autolock feature will activate when the ignition switch is in the RUN or START position, the transmission is moved in and out of REVERSE and then the driver releases the brake pedal. After the initial lock, all doors will automatically relock when any door is opened and then closed followed by the release of the brake pedal. However, the doors will not relock if the key is OFF. NOTE: The door ajar state will be monitored continuously for 500 milliseconds after locking has occurred. If a door is opened again within 500 milliseconds , the driver door will unlock. The door may not automatically lock if the vehicle is shifted too quickly into gear after starting the engine. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3780.html,Initial Inspection - Module Controlled — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;VERIFICATION 1,"Initial Inspection - Module Controlled — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Locks >> Power Locks >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview >> Initial Inspection - Module Controlled Initial Inspection - Module Controlled INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern by operating the system. Visual Inspection Chart: 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of mechanical and electrical damage. Refer to the chart. 3. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported concern is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 4. If the concern remains after the inspection, connect the diagnostic tool to the data link connector (DLC) located beneath the instrument panel and select the vehicle to be tested from the diagnostic tool menu. If diagnostic tool does not communicate with the vehicle: - check that the program card is correctly installed. - check the connections to the vehicle. - check the ignition switch position. 5. If diagnostic tool still does not communicate with the vehicle, refer to the diagnostic tool manual. 6. Carry out the diagnostic tool data link test. If the diagnostic tool responds with: - CAN = all electronic control units, no response/not equipped, refer to Information Bus (Module Communications Network). - No response/not equipped for central security module, go to Body Control Systems (Multifunction Electronic Control Module). - System passed, retrieve and record the continuous diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs), erase the continuous DTCs and carry out self-test diagnostics for the central security module. 7. If the DTCs retrieved are related to the concern, go to the Central Security Module Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index to continue diagnostics. Diagnostic Trouble Code Tests and Associated Procedures 8. If DTCs are retrieved that are not found in the Central Security Module Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index, refer to the master Central Security Module Diagnostics Trouble Code (DTC) index in Body Control Systems (Multifunction Electronic Control Module). Multifunction Electronic Modules 9. If no DTCs related to the concern are retrieved, proceed to the Symptom Chart to continue diagnostics. Module Controlled scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
