3814.html,Mirrors: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;MIRRORS;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;REAR VIEW,"Mirrors: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Mirrors >> Description and Operation Mirrors: Description and Operation REAR VIEW MIRRORS The rear view mirrors consist of the following components: - interior rear view mirror - auto-dimming interior mirror (if equipped) - exterior rear view mirrors - exterior rear view mirror motors - exterior rear view mirror glass - exterior mirror control switch PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Exterior Mirrors The exterior mirrors are controlled by the exterior rear view mirror control switch. The switch supplies power and ground to the selected exterior rear view mirror motor in order to adjust the mirror to the desired position. Auto-Dimming Interior Rear View Mirrors The automatic dimming feature has two photoelectric sensors that detect forward and rear light conditions and adjusts the reflectance level of the mirror to eliminate unwanted glare. The reflectance level is variable and depends on the amount of rear glare in relation to ambient light conditions in front of the interior mirror. When the forward sensor detects daytime conditions, the rear sensor is inactive, and the mirror stays in a high reflectance mode. When the forward sensor detects night time conditions, the rear sensor is active and detects glare from the headlights of vehicles approaching from the rear, or other glare producing light sources. To provide increased visibility when backing up, the mirror will automatically return to a high reflectance mode whenever the shifter is placed in reverse. If the forward or rear sensors are blocked, the automatic dimming interior mirror might not work correctly. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
