3880.html,Vacuum/Pressure Pump: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ASSEMBLY;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;LUMBAR;REMOVAL 1,"Vacuum/Pressure Pump: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Vacuum/Pressure Pump >> Service and Repair Vacuum/Pressure Pump: Service and Repair LUMBAR ASSEMBLY REMOVAL 1. Remove the front seat backrest. 2. Unhook the seat backrest trim cover J-clip. 3. Remove the seat backrest trim cover swing rods. 1 Remove and discard the hog rings. 2 Remove the seat backrest trim cover swing rods. 4. Roll the seat backrest trim cover to the top row of hog rings. 5. Remove and discard the hog rings. 6. Finish inverting the seat backrest trim cover. 7. Removing power lumbar bladder assembly. 1 Cut the tie strap. 2 Release the lumbar bladder retaining clips. 3 Remove the lumbar bladder assembly. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3881.html,Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Service Precautions >> Technician Safety Information Technician Safety Information WARNING: - Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) vehicle and when handling an air bag module. This will reduce the risk of injury in the event of an accidental deployment. - Carry a live air bag module with the air bag and trim cover pointed away from your body. This will reduce the risk of injury in the event of an accidental deployment. - Do not set a live air bag module down with the trim cover face down. This will reduce the risk of injury in the event of an accidental deployment. - After deployment, the air bag surface can contain deposits of sodium hydroxide, a product of the gas generant combustion that is irritating to the skin. Wash your hands with soap and water afterwards. - Never probe the connectors on the air bag module. Doing so can result in air bag deployment, which can result in personal injury. - The safety belt pretensioner is a pyrotechnic device. Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag equipped vehicle and when handling a safety belt buckle pretensioner or safety belt retractor pretensioner. Never probe a pretensioner electrical connector. Doing so could result in pretensioner or air bag deployment and could result in personal injury. - Never probe the connectors on the safety canopy module. Doing so can result in safety canopy deployment. - Vehicle sensor orientation is critical for correct system operation. If a vehicle equipped with an air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) is involved in a collision, inspect the sensor mounting bracket and wiring pigtail for deformation. Correctly position and install a new sensor or new supplemental restraint system (SRS) components that are damaged whether or not the air bag is deployed. - The restraint system diagnostic tool is for restraint system service only. Remove from vehicle prior to road use. Failure to remove could result in injury and possible violation of vehicle safety standards. - To avoid accidental deployment and possible personal injury, the backup power supply must be depleted before repairing or installing any front or side air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) components and before servicing, installing, adjusting or striking components near the front or side air bag sensors, such as doors, instrument panel, console , door latches, strikers, seats and hood latches . The side impact sensors (if equipped) are located at or near the base of the B-pillars and C-pillars. To deplete the backup power supply energy, disconnect the battery ground cable and wait at least one minute. Be sure to disconnect auxiliary batteries and power supplies (if equipped). - The 60 percent latch foot is spring loaded. The seat should be in mid-travel position when removing the bolts. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury. - The 40 percent latch foot is spring loaded. The seat should be in load floor position when removing the bolts. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3882.html,Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Service Precautions >> Vehicle Damage Warnings Vehicle Damage Warnings CAUTION: - Use care when disconnecting the seat cushion side shield from the seat cushion frame so the tabs on the seat cushion side shield are not damaged. - When positioning the seat or separating the seat bottom from the back, be careful not to damage the seat back pivot and any of the wires or cables from the seat back to the seat bottom. This can cause damage to one of the seat components. - Use care when handling the seat and track assembly. Dropping the assembly or sitting on a seat not secured in the vehicle may result in damaged components. - Use care when separating the seat backrest trim cover from the hook and loop strip or the hook and loop strip can be torn from the seat backrest foam. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
3883.html,Seats: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;SEATS,"Seats: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Description and Operation Seats: Description and Operation SEATS Front Seats The front seats can be equipped with the following systems: - Manual seat tracks - Power seat tracks - Power lumbar - Heated seats - Cloth or leather seats - 2-way adjustable head restraints - Infinitely adjustable recline - Map pocket on the back of the seat The base seating package offers cloth low back seats. Both first row seats have a manual adjustment forward/backward. The cloth comfort group seating package offers cloth low back seats. The driver side has a six-way power seat adjustment. The passenger seat has a manual adjustment forward/backward. Both seats have a map pocket on the back of the seat. The leather comfort group seating package offers leather low back seats. Both front row seats have a driver and passenger power seat adjustment, heated seats, power lumbar support and a map pocket on the back of the seat. Heated Seats This system allows the electrical heating of the front seats on passenger demand. The components of the system are: - the seat heating elements located in the seat cushion and backrest. - the heated seat control switch, located on the seat side trim panel . - temperature sensors located in the seat cushion heating elements. - heated seat relay. Rear Seats Second Row Seating The following second row seating configurations and features are available: - 60/40 rear seat (cloth or leather) - 60/40 rear seat that folds down for more interior cargo space - a carpeted panel to complete load floor - 2-way adjustable head restraints - 3 point restraint scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
