4009.html,Conventional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CLUSTER;INSTALLATION 1;INSTRUMENT;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1,"Conventional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Instrument Cluster / Carrier >> Service and Repair >> Conventional Conventional INSTRUMENT CLUSTER REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery. 2. Remove the center instrument panel finish panel. - Remove the screws. - Disconnect the electrical connectors. 3. Remove the screws and position the hood release handle aside. 4. Remove the screws and remove the instrument panel steering column cover. 5. Remove the instrument panel steering column opening cover reinforcement. 6. Position the column-mounted transmission range selector lever aside. 7. Remove the screws and pull the instrument cluster finish panel out from the instrument panel. 8. Disconnect the headlamp and the dimmer switch electrical connectors and remove the instrument cluster finish panel. 9. NOTE: Illustration shows steering column removed for clarity. Remove the instrument cluster. 1 Remove the screws. 2 Remove the transmission range indicator 3 Disconnect the electrical connectors. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
