4026.html,"Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals",Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Service Precautions Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators: Service Precautions CAUTION: - Be careful when probing the BJB, CJB or any connectors. Damage will result to the connector receptacle if the probe or terminal being used is too large. - Electronic modules are sensitive to static discharges. If exposed to these charges, damage may result. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4027.html,Instrument Cluster — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1083;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;999999;BRAKE;CHECK ENGINE;CHECK FUEL CAP;CHECK GAUGE;CLUSTER;DC-AC-DC;INSTRUMENT;LEMON;LOW FUEL;NORMAL;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;SPEED CONT;THEFT,"Instrument Cluster — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Description and Operation >> Instrument Cluster Instrument Cluster INSTRUMENT CLUSTER Instrument Cluster Display: The instrument cluster consists of the components as shown in the illustration. PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION The instrument cluster contains indicator lamps, warning lamps and gauges that are designed to alert the driver that certain conditions exist in the vehicle. Indicator lamps provide information to the driver of conditions that exist in the vehicle. Warning indicator lamps provide information to the driver of conditions that could potentially alter vehicle performance. When installing a new instrument cluster, it is necessary to upload the module configuration to the diagnostic tool. Following installation of the instrument cluster, download the module configuration from the diagnostic tool into the new instrument cluster. The following item is configurable for the instrument cluster: - belt minder The instrument cluster carries a display prove-out to verify that all warning/indicator lamps and monitored systems are functioning correctly. When the ignition switch is in the ON position, engine off, the following instrument cluster warning indicators will prove out: - air bag indicator ( 6 second prove-out on, 2 seconds off) - safety belt indicator ( 6 second prove-out) - THEFT indicator ( 3 second prove-out) - 4x4 indicator ( 3 second prove-out) - 4x4 LOW indicator ( 3 second prove-out) - charge system indicator ( 3 second prove-out) - check engine indicator ( 3 second prove-out) - ABS warning indicator ( 3 second prove-out) Fuel Level Gauge The fuel level gauge informs the driver of the amount of fuel remaining in the tank. The instrument cluster is hardwired to the fuel sending unit, which is a variable resistor controlled by the action of a float arm. The fuel gauge receives its signal from the fuel level sensor, part of the fuel pump module. The fuel level sensor measures variable resistance in the fuel tank depending on the present fuel level. If the fuel level is low, the resistance of the fuel level sensor is low. If the fuel level is high, the resistance of the fuel level sensor is high. On flex-fuel vehicles, basic fuel level indication is the same as gasoline vehicles, except that the flex-fuel vehicles incorporate the use of a flex-fuel module. The flex-fuel module is a DC-AC-DC interface, used to prevent reactions created by the interaction of DC current with the fuel. The flex-fuel module is part of the fuel pump module and is installed as an assembly. Engine Coolant Temperature (ECT) Gauge The ECT gauge displays the engine coolant temperature, or the cylinder head temperature, received from the powertrain control module (PCM) via the SCP communication network. The ECT gauge also indicates when fail-safe cooling is active. When the engine temperature is low, the resistance of the ECT sending unit is high. When the engine temperature is high, the resistance of the ECT sending unit is low. Oil Pressure Gauge The oil pressure switch is installed in the engine block and consists of a diaphragm and contact points. With oil pressure, the contact points close causing the gauge to indicate NORMAL oil pressure. With no oil pressure, the contacts open and the gauge indicates low oil pressure. Battery Voltage Gauge The battery voltage gauge measures the voltage potential at the battery. Circuit 904 (LG/RD) is hardwired to the instrument cluster from the generator and is used to turn on the voltage regulator. This circuit is powered by the PCM after the engine is started. This circuit is also used to turn the charging system warning indicator on if there is a fault in the charging system operation. Speedometer The instrument cluster receives the vehicle speed sensor (VSS) signal from the powertrain control module (PCM) via the SCP communication network. The instrument cluster monitors the VSS input from the PCM and commands the speedometer with a corresponding movement of the pointer. Odometer/Trip Odometer The odometer and trip odometer displays are viewed through the message center in the integrated circuit display. The odometer is tamper-resistant. It accumulates and registers up to 999999 kilometers or miles , based upon rolling count data sent from the PCM via the SCP communication network. The resettable trip odometer accumulates and registers up to 1,608 kilometers (999 miles) . Tachometer The instrument cluster receives the tachometer data from the PCM via the SCP communication network and commands the tachometer pointer between 0 and 6,000 rpm , according to the data. Warning Indicators Air Bag Warning Indicator The instrument cluster is hardwired to the restraint control module. If an air bag system concern is detected, a DTC is logged and the restraint control module provides a ground path to the instrument cluster turning on the air bag indicator. Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Warning indicator The ABS warning indicator is used to indicate an ABS concern or deactivation of the ABS. The instrument cluster, upon receipt of the ABS message from the ABS module over circuit 603 (DG), turns on the ABS warning indicator. BRAKE Warning Indicator The red brake warning light (BRAKE) informs the driver of different conditions concerning the brakes. It indicates whether the parking brake is on, or if the brake fluid is low. Charging System Warning Indicator The charging system indicator informs the driver of the condition of the vehicle's charging system. When the charging system voltage is low, a ground is provided which turns on the charging system indicator. CHECK ENGINE The CHECK ENGINE/malfunction indicator lamp ( MIL ) will illuminate when any of the following conditions exist: - less than or equal to 1/10 tank of fuel remaining. - low oil pressure. - greater than or equal to 121°C (250°F) engine coolant temperature and the coolant gauge will be driven to the ""H"" position. Safety Belt Warning Indicator The restraint control module monitors the safety belt position through the safety belt switch (part of the buckle). When the safety belt is buckled, the restraint control module (RCM) receives a ground signal and sends an ISO message to the instrument cluster to turn off the safety belt warning indicator. When the safety belt is unbuckled, the ground to the RCM is removed and the RCM sends a safety belt warning message over circuit 1083 (LB/PK) to the instrument cluster to turn on the indicator. Low Fuel Warning Indicator When the fuel level drops to a predetermined level, the LOW FUEL warning illuminates. Door Ajar Warning Indicator The door ajar switches provide a ground signal to the vehicle security module. The vehicle security module, upon receipt of the door ajar ground data, supplies a door ajar status message to the instrument cluster over circuit 765 (YE/BK) and circuit 761 (GY/RD). The instrument cluster monitors the door ajar status and commands the door ajar indicator on or off according to the door ajar status message. High Beam Indicator The instrument cluster provides a ground for the high beam indicator. When the high beams are turned on, the multifunction switch provides a power signal to the instrument cluster through hardwired circuitry and illuminates the high beam indicator. Anti-Theft Warning Indicator The anti-theft system provides for vehicle security through an audible and visual notification if the vehicle's exterior is invaded with the system on. The system self-arms when the doors and hood are closed and the key is in the OFF position. Any open door or hood will prevent the system from arming. The hood ajar switch and the door ajar switches cause these circuits to register as normally closed circuits. The vehicle security module monitors the status of the hood ajar and door ajar switches. If these circuits indicate an open entry point, the switch opens the circuit to the vehicle security module, which energizes the horn and autolamp relays (causing the horn to sound and the lights to flash). The vehicle security module turns off the anti-theft system when it receives a command through the keyless entry keypad, remote keyless entry (RKE) transmitter, or anti-theft alarm inhibit switch. Once triggered, the anti-theft system flashes the low beam headlamps, the parking lamps, the THEFT indicator, and sounds the horn. Speed Control Indicator The speed control indicator (SPEED CONT) lamp will illuminate when the speed control is engaged. CHECK FUEL CAP Display The CHECK FUEL CAP display is used to indicate critical leaks in the fuel tank evaporative system due to a loose fuel cap. Fuel tank pressure is monitored by the PCM, and if a leak is detected, the PCM sends the instrument cluster a ground signal over the SCP communication network to illuminate the display. Overdrive (O/D) Off Display The O/D OFF warning will display to indicate to the driver that the transmission will not shift into overdrive. CHECK GAUGE Display The CHECK GAUGE display will illuminate if any of the following occur: - Engine oil pressure drops below approximately 42 kPa (6 psi) . - Engine temperature exceeds approximately 121°C (250°F) . - Less than 1/10 of fuel remaining in tank. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4028.html,Instrument Panel Illumination — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CLUSTER AND;INSTRUMENT;LEMON;PANEL ILLUMINATION;RICP,"Instrument Panel Illumination — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Description and Operation >> Instrument Panel Illumination Instrument Panel Illumination INSTRUMENT CLUSTER AND PANEL ILLUMINATION The instrument cluster and panel lighting system is powered through the headlamp switch and the panel dimmer switch. The instrument cluster illumination is controlled by the output of the panel dimmer switch. The instrument panel lighting circuit provides illumination for the: - climate control panel - rear integrated control panel (RICP) - instrument cluster - ashtray - audio unit - heated seat switch - steering wheel control switch(es) - rear window adjust switch - fog lamp switch - power door lock switch - power window switch - headlamp switch - 4WD control switch - overhead console For the removal and installation of the instrument cluster illumination bulbs, refer to Instrument Cluster. For the removal and installation of the climate control assembly bulb, refer to Heating and Air Conditioning. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4029.html,Warning Devices — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CHECK FUEL CAP;DEVICES;LEMON;LOCK;LOW FUEL;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;START;WARNING,"Warning Devices — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Description and Operation >> Warning Devices Warning Devices WARNING DEVICES Audible Warnings: The warning device system consists of the following components: - instrument cluster - key-in-ignition switch - door ajar switch - restraints control module (RCM) The instrument cluster controls the following warning chimes: - safety belt not fastened - airbag secondary - key-in-ignition - headlamp-on - generic warning - door ajar - safety belt minder For removal and installation of the instrument cluster, refer to Instrument Cluster. For removal and installation of the door ajar switch, refer to Locks. For removal and installation of the RCM, refer to Air Bag Systems. PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Safety Belt Warning Chime The safety belt warning chime alerts that the safety belt is not fastened. The safety belt chime will sound when the driver safety belt is not fastened and the ignition switch is turned from the OFF to the RUN or START position. The safety belt warning chime will stop when the safety belt is fastened, when the ignition is switched to the OFF position or after the chime has sounded for six seconds . The safety belt warning chime inputs are: - ignition switch position - driver safety belt switch The output for the safety belt warning chime is the instrument cluster. Belt Minder The belt minder feature is configurable. To configure without using a diagnostic tool, refer to Belt Minder Deactivating/Activating. The belt minder feature supplements the current safety belt warning function. The belt minder feature is enabled after the current safety belt warning is complete. The belt minder reminds the driver that their safety belt is unbuckled by intermittently sounding a chime and illuminating the safety belt warning lamp in the instrument cluster once the vehicle speed has exceeded 4.8 km/h (3 mph) . While activated, the belt minder alternates the chime and indicator from ON for 6 seconds to OFF for 30 seconds . With the Driver Toll Booth feature, during stop/go traffic (such as approaching a toll booth) an intentionally unbuckled driver has reasonable time to buckle without warning tone, until the vehicle speed has exceeded 4.8 km/h (3 mph) for 1 minute . The belt minder feature stops when: - the driver safety belt is buckled. - the ignition switch is turned to OFF or ACC. - five minutes have elapsed since the belt minder started. Airbag Secondary Warning Chime The airbag secondary warning chime alerts when there is a fault with the airbag indicator. The airbag secondary warning chime inputs are: - ignition switch - restraints control module (RCM) Key-in-ignition Warning Chime The key-in-ignition warning chime will sound when the key is in the OFF/LOCK or ACC position and the driver door is ajar. The key-in-ignition warning will stop sounding when the driver door is closed, the ignition switch is moved to RUN position, or the key is removed from the ignition. The key-in-ignition warning input is the key-in-ignition switch. Generic Warning Chime This warning chime brings the attention to the warning messages that are displayed on the message center. The chime will sound when any warning messages, such as LOW FUEL or CHECK FUEL CAP are displayed. The generic warning input is the instrument cluster Door Ajar Warning Chime The door ajar warning chime alerts when any door becomes ajar while the ignition is in the RUN position. The door ajar warning will stop when the door is closed or when the ignition switch is turned OFF. The door ajar warning chime inputs are: - the ignition switch in the RUN position - door ajar switches Headlamp On Warning Chime The headlamp on warning chime alerts that the headlamps are on with the driver door open and the ignition switch in the OFF position. The warning chime will stop when any of the above conditions are removed. The headlamp on warning chime inputs are: - ignition switch - Headlamp switch - driver door switch scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4030.html,Initial Inspection - Instrument Cluster — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;VERIFICATION 1,"Initial Inspection - Instrument Cluster — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview >> Initial Inspection - Instrument Cluster Initial Inspection - Instrument Cluster INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern. Visual Inspection Chart: 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of mechanical or electrical damage. 3. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported concern is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 4. If the concern remains after inspection, connect the diagnostic tool to the data link connector (DLC) located beneath the instrument panel and select the vehicle to be tested from the diagnostic tool menu. If the diagnostic tool does not communicate with the vehicle: - check that the program card is correctly installed. - check the connection of the data link connector to the vehicle. - check the ignition switch is in the RUN position. 5. If the diagnostic tool still does not communicate with the vehicle, refer to the diagnostic tool operating manual. 6. Carry out the diagnostic tool data link test. If the diagnostic tool responds with: - SCP or ISO circuit fault; all electronic control units no response/not equipped, refer to Information Bus (Module Communications Network). - No response/not equipped for the instrument cluster, GO to Pinpoint Test W. Test W - System passed, retrieve and record the continuous diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs), erase the continuous DTCs and carry out self-test diagnostics for the instrument cluster. 7. If the DTCs retrieved are related to the concern, go to the Instrument Cluster Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index to continue diagnostics. Trouble Code Diagnostic Charts - Instrument Cluster 8. If no DTCs related to the concern are retrieved, GO to Symptom Chart to continue diagnostics. Diagnosis By Symptom - Instrument Cluster scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
