4111.html,Courtesy Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;START,"Courtesy Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Lighting and Horns >> Courtesy Lamp >> Description and Operation Courtesy Lamp: Description and Operation PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Interior Lighting The instrument cluster illuminates the interior lamps when any door is opened. The following are inputs used for controlling the interior lamps: - all door ajar switches. - illuminated entry request (vehicle security module). All interior lamps are turned off when any of the following occur: - all the doors are closed and the illuminated entry feature is not active. - the ignition switch is turned to ON. - a power door lock command is received before the five seconds have elapsed for two-step unlock. The instrument cluster controls the interior lamps illuminated entry function with the interior lamp relay. The relay is activated when the instrument cluster applies ground to the relay coil, and is deactivated by removing the ground. The instrument panel dimmer switch controls the interior lamps by supplying a signal to the instrument cluster. The vehicle security module sends a signal to the instrument cluster to indicate a request to turn the illuminated entry feature ON or OFF. The instrument cluster illuminates the interior lamps when an unlock signal is received from the vehicle security module. The illuminated entry feature will be canceled when any of the following conditions are met: - 25 seconds have elapsed since the illuminated entry feature was activated and the interior lamp control is not activated. - the ignition is in the ON or START position. For additional vehicle security module information, refer to Locks. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4112.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;REFER;VERIFICATION 1,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Lighting and Horns >> Courtesy Lamp >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern. Visual Inspection Chart: 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of mechanical and electrical damage. 3. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported concern is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 4. If the cause is not visually evident, connect the diagnostic tool to the data link connector and select the vehicle to be tested from the diagnostic tool menu. If the diagnostic tool does not communicate with the vehicle: - check that the program card is correctly installed. - check the connections to the vehicle. - check the ignition switch position. 5. If the diagnostic tool still does not communicate with the vehicle, refer to the diagnostic tool operating manual. 6. Carry out the data link diagnostics test. If the diagnostic tool responds with: - SCP or CAN or UBP circuits fault; all electronic control units no response/not equipped, refer to Information Bus (Module Communications Network). - No response/not equipped for instrument cluster, REFER to Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators. - System passed, retrieve and record the continuous diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs), erase the continuous DTCs and carry out self-test diagnostics for the instrument cluster. 7. If the DTCs retrieved are related to the concern, go to the Instrument Cluster Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index to continue diagnostics. Diagnostic Trouble Code Tests and Associated Procedures 8. If no DTCs related to the concern are retrieved, GO to Symptom Chart. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures 9. If the DTCs are retrieved that are not found in the Instrument Cluster Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index, refer to the master Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Index in Body Control Systems (Multifunction Electronic Control Module). Multifunction Electronic Modules scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
