4135.html,Daytime Running Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;75-92;DAYTIME;LEMON;OPERATION;PRINCIPLES OF;RUNNING LAMPS,"Daytime Running Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Lighting and Horns >> Daytime Running Lamp >> Description and Operation Daytime Running Lamp: Description and Operation DAYTIME RUNNING LAMPS (DRL) The daytime running lamps (DRL) system consists of a DRL module that is located behind the front bumper. The module is mounted to the radiator support. PRINCIPLES OF OPERATION Daytime Running Lamps (DRL) The daytime running lamps (DRL) system operates the low beam headlamps at a reduced intensity. The DRL module supplies pulse width modulated (PWM) voltage, approximately 75-92% of battery voltage, to the low beam headlamps when the following conditions are met: - The high beam headlamps are disabled. - The ignition switch is in the RUN position. The DRL module remains enabled when the low beam headlamps are turned on. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4136.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;INSPECTION CHART;LEMON;VERIFICATION 1;VISUAL,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Lighting and Horns >> Daytime Running Lamp >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION 1. Verify the customer concern by operating the system. 2. Visually inspect for obvious signs of mechanical and electrical damage. VISUAL INSPECTION CHART Electrical - Daytime running lamps (DRL) module - Central junction box (CJB) fuse(s): - 27 (15A) - 33 (15A) - Battery junction box (BJB) fuse(s): - 33 (15A) Sport - 38 (10A) - 42 (10A) - 31 (15A) - Damaged wiring harness - Loose or corroded connection 3. Verify the headlamps are operating correctly. Correct any concerns before proceeding to the next step. 4. If an obvious cause for an observed or reported concern is found, correct the cause (if possible) before proceeding to the next step. 5. If the concern is not visually evident, verify the symptom and refer to the Symptom Chart. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
