4306.html,Window Regulator: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,13,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REAR WINDOW GLASS;REGULATOR;REMOVAL 1,"Window Regulator: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Regulator >> Service and Repair Window Regulator: Service and Repair REAR WINDOW GLASS - REGULATOR REMOVAL 1. Fold down the rear seat backs. 2. Fold the loadspace trim panels up and remove the luggage compartment lower screws and loadspace trim panel. 3. Remove the pin-type retainers from the luggage compartment trim panel. 4. Open the luggage compartment trim panel access doors and remove the four pin-type retainers and the luggage compartment trim panel. 5. Remove the spare tire jack and handle assembly. 6. If equipped, remove the sub-woofer assembly. 1 Disconnect the electrical connector. 2 Remove the bolts. 7. Remove the carpet pin-type retainers and pull the carpet back. 8. NOTE: The rear window glass water shield uses a reusable butyl rubber adhesive. A new water shield does not have to be installed unless it is damaged or if the butyl rubber adhesive does not adhere to a section of the sheet metal. Remove the water shield from the rear window glass motor. 9. Position the rear window glass regulator access panel aside. 1 Remove the screws. 2 Remove the nut. 3 Position the rear window glass regulator access panel aside. 10. Position the rear window glass to the 3/4 down position. 11. Disconnect the rear window glass regulator motor electrical connector. 12. Remove the rear window glass bolts. 13. Secure the rear window glass in the full closed position. 14. Remove the upper rear window glass regulator bolts. 15. Loosen the right and lower rear window glass regulator drum housing bolts, and remove the left rear window glass regulator drum housing bolt. 16. Remove the rear window glass regulator assembly. - Position the slider to the midway point. 17. If necessary, transfer the rear window glass motor. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: The rear window glass motor must be initialized after a repair has been carried out. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
