4361.html,Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Service Precautions >> Technician Safety Information Technician Safety Information WARNING: - Do not run the engine when jacking the vehicle. The wheels contacting the ground could cause the vehicle to move. - Make sure the jack and jack stands are correctly located to prevent the vehicle from falling. - A wheel chock should be used to prevent the vehicle from rolling and falling off the jack. - When one of the rear wheels is off the ground, the transmission alone will not prevent the vehicle from moving or slipping off the jack, even if the transmission is in P (park) (automatic transmission) or reverse (manual transmission). scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4362.html,Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Service Precautions >> Vehicle Damage Warnings Vehicle Damage Warnings CAUTION: - Do not use the differential housing as a lift point. Leaks or damage to the rear axle cover and adjoining differential housing surface can occur if a floor jack or any lifting device is allowed to contact the cover at any point where the cover joins the housing. - Damage to the suspension , fuel tank , exhaust or steering linkage components can occur if care is not exercised when positioning the hoist adapters prior to lifting the vehicle. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4363.html,Vehicle Identification Number — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension;Body;Interior,10,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;A00001-;CODES;F99999;GVWR;IDENTIFICATION;LEMON;SOHC,"Vehicle Identification Number — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Application and ID >> Vehicle Identification Number Vehicle Identification Number VIN Locator: IDENTIFICATION CODES The vehicle identification number (VIN) is a seventeen-digit combination of letters and numbers. The VIN is stamped on a metal tab riveted on the instrument panel, top upper left of the dash. The VIN number is also found on the vehicle certification (VC) label. Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) World Manufacturer Identifier: The first three vehicle identification number (VIN) positions are the world manufacturer identifier. - 1FM - Ford Motor Company, USA, multi-purpose vehicle Brake And Gross Vehicle Weight Rating (GVWR): The fourth VIN position is the vehicle brake type and gross vehicle weight rating (GVWR) code, all vehicles use hydraulic brakes. This code may also identify the vehicle safety restraint system. - D - 5,001-6,000 pounds GVWR, active safety belts (all positions) with driver and front passenger air bags and driver and front passenger side impact air bags - Z - 5,001-6,000 pounds GVWR, active safety belts (all positions) with driver and front passenger air bags Line, Series And Body Type: Positions five through seven indicate the vehicle line, series and body type. - U67 - Sport Trac, four-door, 4x2 - U77 - Sport Trac, four-door, 4x4 Engine Type: The eighth VIN position is the engine displacement and number of cylinders. - K - 4.0L, EFI, SOHC, six cylinder Check Digit: The ninth VIN position is a government assigned check digit. Model Year: The tenth VIN position is the model year code. - 4 - 2004 Assembly Plant: The eleventh VIN position is the assembly plant code. - U - Louisville (Louisville, Kentucky) Build Sequence: VIN positions twelve through seventeen are an alphanumeric code for the vehicle build sequence. This is also the vehicle serial number and warranty number. - A00001-F99999 scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
4364.html,Vehicle Certification (VC) Label — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Suspension;Body;Interior,13,,126 inch;200 mm,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2001;2002;2003;2004;2WD V6-4;3L54-5560-AA;3L54-5560-BA;5R44;A5LDE-NR;CAFE;CERTIFICATION;F67A-5B326-FA;F67A-5B327-FA;GVWR;HDGE;LABEL;LEMON;MACAA;NOTE;OASIS;VEHICLE,"Vehicle Certification (VC) Label — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Application and ID >> Vehicle Certification (VC) Label Vehicle Certification (VC) Label VC Label Locator: The vehicle certification (VC) label contains information on the manufacturer name, the month and year of manufacture, the certification statement, and the VIN. It also includes the gross vehicle weight rating (GVWR). VEHICLE CERTIFICATION (VC) LABEL Paint Codes: The first set of code numbers list the primary body color, the second set of code numbers list the lower body or two-tone paint code (if applicable). The following lists the exterior paint codes: Primary body color codes - CY - Competition Orange - DX - Dark Blue Pearl - FX - Merlot - G2 - Redfire - JP - Silver Birch Metallic - G3 - Pueblo Gold - P5 - Aspen Green Metallic - UA - Ebony - YZ - Oxford White Wheelbase Code: - 126 - 126 inch (3,200 mm) wheelbase Brake Code: All vehicles receive a four-wheel anti-lock brake system (ABS) as standard equipment. Interior Trim Code: Interior trim codes are listed as a two part code. The first code listed indicates the interior trim code. The second code listed indicates the interior trim color. The interior trim codes are: - Q - Captains cloth low back bucket seats - R - Static cloth low back bucket seats - S - Imola leather low back bucket seats - W - Static/embroidered cloth low back bucket seats - X - Imola leather/embossed low back bucket seats - Y - Captains cloth/embroidered low back bucket seats The interior trim colors are: - F - Medium/Dark Flint - W - Medium Pebble Tape/Paint Stripe Code: Tape or paint stripe codes do not apply. Radio Codes: - 1 - AM/FM electronic stereo with six disc compact disc (CD) changer (in dash) and clock - K - Premium electronic AM/FM stereo with cassette, compact disc (CD) player and clock - W - Premium electronic AM/FM stereo with cassette and compact disc (CD) player and clock - Z - Premium electronic AM/FM stereo with compact disc (CD) player and clock Axle Codes: - 42 - 4.10 ratio, non-limited slip - 46 - 3.73 ratio, non-limited slip - D2 - 4.10 ratio, limited slip - D4 - 3.73 ratio, limited slip Transmission Codes: The available transmissions are: - D - Five-speed automatic overdrive, A5LDE-NR/5R44/55E Spring Codes: Spring codes are listed as a two part code. The first code identifies the front springs. The second code identifies the rear springs. Front Springs The front suspension uses torsion bars . Torsion bar codes are: - 1 - F67A-5B326-FA (right-hand) - 1 - F67A-5B327-FA (left-hand) Rear Springs Rear spring codes are: - 4 - 3L54-5560-BA - 5 - 3L54-5560-AA Powertrain Calibration Information: Powertrain Calibration Information NOTE: Powertrain calibration information is limited to a maximum of five characters per line on the Vehicle Certification Label. Because of this, calibration identification consisting of more than five characters will wrap to the second line on the VC label. Powertrain calibration information is printed in the lower right corner of the Vehicle Certification Label. Only the base calibration information is printed. Revision levels will not appear, however, they can be found in On Line Automotive Service Information System (OASIS). Model Year Model year is as follows: - 1 - 2001 - 2 - 2002 - 3 - 2003 - 4 - 2004 Vehicle Code The vehicle code is as follows: - S1 - Sport Trac Transmission Code The transmission codes are as follows: - D - Automatic transmission Unique Calibration Unique calibration is explained in the following: The Emissions/CAFE/CO2 Compliance Department is responsible for assigning these calibration numbers. Unique calibration identifications are assigned to cover similar vehicles to differentiate tires , drive configurations, final drive ratios and other certification-significant factors. These two characters are chosen by the analyst to provide identifiable information unique to each calibration. For example, using the number 2 to denote a two-valve engine versus using the number 4 to denote a four-valve engine provides an easily identifiable difference. Fleet Code Fleet coding is as follows: - 0 - Certification (U.S. 4K, final sale in export markets) - 1 - HDGE/Dyno - 2 - Fast AMA, U.S. - 3 - ADP, U.S. - 4 - Not assigned - 5 - Not assigned - 6 - Evaporative emissions - 7 - MACAA - 8 - On-board diagnostics - 9 - Not assigned Certification Region Certification region (lead region where multiple regions are included) are as follows: - 5 - U.S. fifty states - A - U.S. Federal (including altitude, may include Canada or Mexico) - B - California Standard (includes U.S. green states) - C - Canada - G - Gulf Cooperative Council - H - Hong Kong - J - Japan - K - Korea - L - Malaysia - M - Mexico - N - New Zealand - P - Australia - Q - South America (Brazil) - S - Singapore - T - Taiwan - U - South America (unleaded fuel) - V - Vietnam - X - ROW (rest of world) - Y - Military - Z - Israel Revision Level Revision levels will advance as revisions occur. Not printed on label. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
