5451.html,Attachment II - Labor and Parts Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LABOR ALLOWANCES;LEMON;NOTE;SMOG,Attachment II - Labor and Parts Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Technical Service Bulletins >> All Technical Service Bulletins >> Campaign - In-Stock Vehicle Label SMOG Info Revised >> Attachment II - Labor and Parts Information Attachment II - Labor and Parts Information LABOR ALLOWANCES SMOG Emissions Information Labels Corrected SMOG Emissions Information labels are provided in Attachment III. Follow the instructions in Attachment Ill for printing and installing the corrected SMOG Emissions Information label. NOTE : For all affected in-stock units dealers are required to apply the revised SMOG Emissions Information label over the existing SMOG Emissions Information on the Vehicle Content Label which is located on the driver's side window. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
5452.html,Attachment III - Technical Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;PROCEDURE 1;SERVICE;SMOG;VECI,"Attachment III - Technical Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Technical Service Bulletins >> All Technical Service Bulletins >> Campaign - In-Stock Vehicle Label SMOG Info Revised >> Attachment III - Technical Information Attachment III - Technical Information The affected vehicles require installation of a corrected SMOG Emissions Information label. These labels are designed to be printed on a plain sheet of paper. Each sheet of paper contains five (5) revised SMOG Emissions Information labels. Table of Contents Service Procedure SMOG Index 0.51 Labels SMOG Index 1.00 Labels SMOG Index 1.44 Labels SMOG Index 1.45 Labels SMOG Index 1.51 Labels SMOG Index 1.65 Labels SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Locate the VECI label under the hood and identify the three-letter label suffix. 2. Refer to the chart to identify the correct SMOG Index based on the VECI label suffix for the vehicle being serviced. 3. Once identified, print the appropriate page and cut out one (1) SMOG Information label from the printed page. Retain the printed page for use on other affected vehicles which require the same SMOG Emissions Information. 4. Partially peel back the Parts Content Information label from the left side door glass. 5. Affix the new SMOG Emission Information label over the original using cellophane tape and reattach the Parts Content Information label to the window. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
