5686.html,Wiper Motor Linkage: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Wiper Motor Linkage: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Wiper and Washer Systems >> Wiper Motor Linkage >> Service Precautions Wiper Motor Linkage: Service Precautions CAUTION: To avoid possible damage to the windshield wiper adapter and connecting arm clip, be sure the clip is fully seated before installing the adapter and connecting arm clip on the windshield wiper motor crank pin. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5687.html,Wiper Motor Linkage: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Interior,6,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AND PIVOT SHAFT;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;WIPER MOUNTING ARM,"Wiper Motor Linkage: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Wiper and Washer Systems >> Wiper Motor Linkage >> Service and Repair Wiper Motor Linkage: Service and Repair WIPER MOUNTING ARM AND PIVOT SHAFT REMOVAL 1. Remove the cowl grilles. 2. Unsnap the wiper motor clip from the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft. 3. Disconnect the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft from the LH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft and move both away from the windshield wiper motor. 4. Remove the RH and LH wiper mounting arm and pivot shafts. 1 Remove the two nuts. 2 Remove the wiper mounting arm and pivot shafts. INSTALLATION 1. Install the RH and LH wiper mounting arms and pivot shafts. 1 Position the wiper mounting arm and pivot shafts into place. 2 Install the two nuts. 2. CAUTION: To avoid possible damage to the windshield wiper adapter and connecting arm clip, be sure the clip is fully seated before installing the adapter and connecting arm clip on the windshield wiper motor crank pin. If removed, install the clip onto the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft. 3. Install the wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft assemblies. 1 Install the LH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft onto the windshield wiper motor crank pin. 2 Install the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft onto the wiper motor crank pin. 3 Push the retaining clip until it snaps into place. 4. Install the cowl grilles. 5. Adjust the LH and RH wiper pivot arms. Refer to Windshield Wiper Blade and Pivot Arm Adjustment. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5688.html,Wiper Motor: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Wiper Motor: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Wiper and Washer Systems >> Wiper Motor >> Service Precautions Wiper Motor: Service Precautions CAUTION: The internal permanent magnets used in the windshield wiper motor are made of a glass-like material. To avoid damaging the magnets, do not strike the motor with a hammer or any other object. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5689.html,Wiper Motor: Locations — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,Wiper Motor: Locations — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Wiper and Washer Systems >> Wiper Motor >> Locations Wiper Motor: Locations View 151-1: scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
5690.html,Wiper Motor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,11,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;MOTOR REMOVAL 1;WINDSHIELD WIPER,"Wiper Motor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Wiper and Washer Systems >> Wiper Motor >> Service and Repair Wiper Motor: Service and Repair WINDSHIELD WIPER MOTOR REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the washer hose from the LH washer jet nozzle. 2. Remove the cowl grille. 3. Unsnap the wiper motor clip from the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft. 4. Disconnect the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft from the LH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft and move both away from the windshield wiper motor. 5. Disconnect the electrical connector. 6. Remove the ground strap nut and position the strap aside. 7. CAUTION: The internal permanent magnets used in the windshield wiper motor are made of a glass-like material. To avoid damaging the magnets, do not strike the motor with a hammer or any other object. Remove the windshield wiper motor. - Remove the stud bolts. - Remove the bolts. INSTALLATION 1. CAUTION: The internal permanent magnets used in the windshield wiper motor are made of a glass-like material. To avoid damaging the magnets, do not strike the motor with a hammer or any other object. Install the windshield wiper motor. 1 Install the windshield wiper motor. 2 Install the stud bolts. 3 Install the bolts. 2. Install the ground strap and nut. 3. Connect the electrical connector. 4. Install the wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft arms to the windshield wiper motor. 1 Install the LH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft onto the windshield wiper motor crank pin. 2 Install the RH wiper mounting arm and pivot shaft onto the wiper motor crank pin. 3 Push the retaining clip until it snaps into place. 5. Install the cowl grilles. 6. Connect the washer hose to the LH washer jet nozzle. 7. Install the LH wiper pivot arm. 8. Adjust the LH wiper pivot arm. Refer to Windshield Wiper Blade and Pivot Arm Adjustment. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
