5714.html,Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,0,,,0L VIN K;12-24;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windshield >> Service Precautions >> Vehicle Damage Warnings Vehicle Damage Warnings CAUTION: - The urethane adhesive must cure for a minimum of one hour before testing for air or water leaks. - After installing the urethane installed glass, the vehicle should not be driven until the urethane adhesive has cured. The curing times at temperatures above 13°C (55°F) and relative humidity above 50% is 12-24 hours (refer to Essex Drive Away Chart for cure times, as temperatures and humidity vary). Inadequate curing of the urethane adhesive may adversely affect the strength of the urethane bond. - Do not scratch the pinch weld area. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5715.html,Windshield: Service and Repair: General Procedures — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;400-HV;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE;RESEAL 1;WINDSHIELD,"Windshield: Service and Repair: General Procedures — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windshield >> Service and Repair >> General Procedures Windshield: Service and Repair: General Procedures WINDSHIELD RESEAL 1. Remove the windshield side garnish mouldings. 2. Remove the interior rear view mirror. 3. Remove the overhead console. 4. If equipped, remove the roof opening panel trim. 5. Remove the sun visors. 1 Remove the sun visor screws. 2 Remove the sun visors. - If equipped, disconnect the electrical connector. 6. Remove the sun visor clips. 1 Remove the sun visor clip screws. 2 Remove the sun visor clips. 7. Partially lower the front portion of the headliner near the windshield upper opening and block with a suitable material. 8. Remove the cowl grille. 9. Clean the edge formed by the existing urethane and the glass on the inside at the top and sides, and outside on the bottom of the windshield with an alcohol free cleaner. 10. Cut the urethane applicator tip to specification. 11. NOTE: Use either a high-ratio electric or battery-operated caulk gun that will apply the urethane with less effort and a continuous bead. Apply a bead of urethane adhesive essex 400-HV to the cleaned area. 12. NOTE: Make sure that all gaps in the urethane adhesive are smoothed into one continuous bead. Backfill the urethane application and clean the excess. 13. CAUTION: The urethane adhesive must cure for a minimum of one hour before testing for air or water leaks. After the urethane has cured, check the windshield seal for air or water leaks through the urethane adhesive bead and add urethane adhesive as necessary. 14. Install the cowl grille. 15. Install the front portion of the headliner. 16. Install the sun visor clips. 1 Position the sun visor clips. 2 Install the screws. 17. Install the sun visors. 1 Position the sun visors. - If equipped, connect the electrical connector. 2 Install the screws. 18. If equipped, install the roof opening panel trim. 19. Install the overhead console. 20. Install the interior rear view mirror. Make sure the interior rear view mirror is securely seated on the mounting tab. 21. Install the windshield side garnish. 22. Clean the interior and exterior of the windshield glass with an alcohol free cleaner. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5716.html,Removal and Installation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,15,,,0L VIN K;12-24;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;400-HV;CAUTION;ESB-M3G137-A;INSTALLATION;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;SPECIAL TOOL;WARNING;WINDSHIELD GLASS;WSB-M2G234-C;WSB-M2G314-B;WSB-M2G316-B;WSB-M5B280-C,"Removal and Installation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windshield >> Service and Repair >> Removal and Installation Removal and Installation WINDSHIELD GLASS Special Tool(s): SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL WARNING: To prevent glass splinters from entering the eyes or cutting hands, wear safety glasses and heavy gloves when cutting the glass from the vehicle. 1. Remove the windshield side garnish mouldings. 2. Remove the interior rear view mirror. 3. Remove the overhead console. 4. Remove the sun visors. 1 Remove the sun visor screws. 2 Remove the sun visors. - If equipped, disconnect the electrical connector. 5. Remove the sun visor clips. 1 Remove the sun visor clip screws. 2 Remove the sun visor clips. 6. Lower the front portion of the headliner. 7. Remove the cowl grille. 8. NOTE: Lubricate the urethane adhesive with water to aid the special tool when cutting. Using the special tool, cut the urethane adhesive from the windshield glass starting at the top center and work toward the bottom corners. 9. Using the special tool, distance the windshield from the body. 10. Using the special tool, cut the remaining urethane adhesive and remove the windshield glass. 11. Using a soft brush or vacuum, remove any foreign material or dirt from the pinch weld. INSTALLATION CAUTION: After installing the urethane installed glass, the vehicle should not be driven until the urethane adhesive has cured. The curing times at temperatures above 13°C (55°F) and relative humidity above 50% is 12-24 hours (refer to Essex Drive Away Chart for cure times, as temperatures and humidity vary). Inadequate curing of the urethane adhesive may adversely affect the strength of the urethane bond. 1. Dry fit the windshield . Make alignment marks on the glass and vehicle body with tape or non-staining grease pencil. 2. CAUTION: Do not scratch the pinch weld area. NOTE: After trimming the urethane, do not touch the exposed urethane bead. Trim the remaining urethane adhesive on the pinch weld to within the specification. - The existing urethane adhesive surface should be smooth and free of cuts and contamination. 3. Use a wool applicator to apply Urethane Metal Primer Essex U-413 meeting Ford specification WSB-M2G234-C to any exposed metal on the pinch weld. Allow six to ten minutes to dry. 4. If originally equipped, apply (A) Foam Dam meeting Ford specification ESB-M3G137-A to the (B) pinch weld. 5. If reinstalling original windshield , remove the excess urethane adhesive from the windshield glass. 6. Clean the inside of the glass surface with an alcohol-free cleaner making sure the ceramic coated area is clean. 7. NOTE: Wipe off the Glass Prep immediately after each application because it flash dries. If installing a new windshield glass, apply Urethane Glass Prep Essex U-401 meeting Ford specification WSB-M5B280-C twice around the glass surface to be urethaned. 8. If installing a new windshield glass, apply Glass Primer Essex U-402 meeting Ford specification WSB-M2G314-B to the same area that was prepped in the pervious step. Allow five minutes to dry. 9. Cut the urethane adhesive applicator tip to specification. 10. Apply a triangular bead of Urethane Adhesive Essex 400-HV, which meets Ford specification WSB-M2G316-B to the pinch weld just outside the foam dam, on top of the existing bead of urethane. 11. Install the windshield glass aligning it to the marks previously made. 12. After the windshield glass is set, check for water leaks and add urethane adhesive where needed. 13. If necessary, remove excess urethane adhesive from the outside surface of the windshield glass. 14. Install the cowl grille. 15. Install the overhead console. 16. Install the sun visor clips. 1 Position the sun visor clips. 2 Install the screws. 17. Install the sun visors. 1 Position the sun visors. - If equipped, connect the electrical connector. 2 Install the screws. 18. Install the front portion of the headliner. 19. Install the interior rear view mirror. Make sure the interior rear view mirror is securely seated on the mounting tab. 20. Install the windshield side garnish mouldings. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
