5729.html,Body - Power Rear Window Rattling Noise — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,13,,,03-19-4;031904A;031904B;0L VIN K;15-20;164-R4900;164-R4906;1960-2025;1L5Z-35422A08-AA;1L5Z-35422A08-M;2001-2004;2004;2WD V6-4;501-11;ACTION;ARTICLES;BODY;CODE 35422A08 33;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;DO NOT;EXPLORER SPORT;IF WINDOW;IN VENT;LEMON;NECESSARY;NOISE;NONE WARRANTY;OPERATION;OTHER APPLICABLE;PART NO;POSITION;POSITION FORD;POWER REAR;PROCEDURE NOTE;RATTLE WHEN;REGULATOR;REPLACE THE;REPLACEMENT IS;SERVICE;STATUS;TRAC ISSUE;TWICE;WINDOW;WINDOW MOTOR,"Body - Power Rear Window Rattling Noise — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Regulator >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> Body - Power Rear Window Rattling Noise Body - Power Rear Window Rattling Noise Article No. 03-19-4 09/29/03 ^ BODY - POWER REAR WINDOW RATTLE WHEN IN VENT POSITION ^ NOISE - POWER REAR WINDOW RATTLE WHEN IN VENT POSITION FORD: 2001-2004 EXPLORER SPORT TRAC ISSUE On some vehicles the power rear window may exhibit a rattle noise when in the vent position. This may be due to a stick/slip condition between the regulator rail and the plastic glide mechanism. ACTION To service this condition, an updated Power Rear Window Regulator (1L5Z-35422A08-AA) should only be installed if the following Service Procedure directs regulator replacement. SERVICE PROCEDURE NOTE IF WINDOW REGULATOR REPLACEMENT IS NECESSARY, DO NOT REPLACE THE POWER REAR WINDOW MOTOR. 1. Remove the Rear Window Glass-Regulator. Refer to Section 501-11 of the on-line Workshop Manual. 2. Pull the black plastic glider off of the power rear window regulator rail. 3. Apply Krytox grease (164-R4906) from the Rotunda Squeak & Raule Kit (164-R4900) to the areas of the glider that interface to the regulator rail. 4. Ensure that Krytox grease is applied into the notched areas of the plastic glider (Figure 11). 5. Reinstall the glider back onto the power rear window regulator rail and reassemble the power rear window. Initialize the power rear window. Refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10. 6. Cycle power rear window up and down 15-20 times to work in Krytox. 7. Re-initialize the power rear window motor. Refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10. 8. Road test to verify repair. Repeat Steps 1-7 if necessary. 9. If the condition is still present after following this procedure TWICE, then replace the Power Rear Window Regulator with an updated regulator (1L5Z-35422A08-M). Re-initialize, refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10, and road test to verify repair. (The updated service regulator less motor has a black powder coated rail and the old service regulator less motor has a galvanized coating). Parts Block OTHER APPLICABLE ARTICLES: NONE WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of The New Vehicle Limited Warranty. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 031904A Remove Rear Power 2.2 Hrs. Window Regulator Apply Grease (Includes Time To Perform Operation Twice And Test Drive) 031904B Remove Rear Power 3.2 Hrs. Window Regulator Apply Grease (Includes Time To Perform Operation Twice And Test Drive) If Condition Still Exists Replace Regulator DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 35422A08 33 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5730.html,Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,2,,,07 REAR POWER;072005A 2002;072005B 2002;072005C 2002;072005D 2002;072005E 2002;07200SF 2002;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2002-2005;2002-2006;2003-2005;2004;2005;2006;2006 0;2006 1;27406B;27406B8;27406B9;2WD V6-4;501-11;ACTION;CODE 7823394 07;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;IMPORTANT;INOPERATIVE;ISSUE;LEMON;LINCOLN;MERCURY;OPERATION;PART NO;PROCEDURE 1;SERVICE;STATUS;STUCK IN THE;TSB 07-16;TSB 07-20;UP POSITION FORD;WARRANTY;WINDOW MOTOR,"Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Regulator >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative TSB 07-20-5 10/15/07 REAR POWER WINDOW MOTOR INOPERATIVE/STUCK IN THE UP POSITION FORD: 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac 2002-2006 Explorer LINCOLN: 2003-2005 Aviator MERCURY: 2002-2006 Mountaineer This article supersedes TSB 07-16-14 to update the Part List. ISSUE Some 2002-2006 Explorer, Mountaineer and 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, and 2003-2005 Aviator vehicles built before 1/23/2006 may experience a rear power window that sticks in the up position. This condition can be intermittent and may be due to the power motor which temporarily locks up. ACTION Follow the Service Procedure steps to correct the condition. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Use the current Workshop Manual (WSM), Section 501-11 procedure to remove the door panel and inspect the window regulator for damaged parts. 2. If any damage part or parts are found replace the regulator assembly. 3. If no damaged parts are found on the regulator assembly, replace the window regulator motor using WSM, Section 501-11. Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage IMPORTANT : Warranty coverage limits/policies are not altered by a TSB. Warranty coverage limits are determined by the identified causal part. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 072005A 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 0.9 Hr. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005B 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 1.6 Hrs. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005C 2002-2006 0.4 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005D 2002-2006 0.7 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005E 2002-2006 0.6 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 07200SF 2002-2006 1.1 Hrs. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7823394 07 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
