5743.html,Body - Rear Bolt-In Glass Installation/Removal Tips — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,4,Torque the attaching nuts to: ^ 2001-2003 F-150 27 lb-in (3 N.m) ^ 2004 F-150 Heritage 27 lb-in (3 N.m) ^ 2004-2005 F-150 35 lb-in (4 N.m) ^ Explorer Sport Trac 27 lb,25 mm;8 mm,05 REMOVAL AND;0L VIN K;150 27;150 35;1960-2025;2001-2003 F;2001-2005;2004;2004 F;2004-2005 F;2006;2WD V6-4;ACTION;ATTEMPT TO;AUTOMOTIVE GLASS;BROKEN TO;BUTYL OR;CODE 70422B30 07;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;CREATE A;DEALER;DIFFICULT;EXTREMELY;FIGURE 1;FOAM CORE BUTYL;FORD;GLASS;GLASS INSTALLATION;GLASS MODULE FROM;GLASS REMOVAL;IN THE;INDUSTRY AS;INSTALLATION OF;ISSUE;IT WILL ALSO;LEAK;LEMON;MAKE IT ROUND;MAKE THE NEXT;MUST BE;NOTE DO NOT;NOTE THE BACK;NOTE TO BREAK;PART NO;PLACED ON;PLASTIC;PLASTIC TOOL;PROCEDURE GLASS;REAR BOLT-IN,"Body - Rear Bolt-In Glass Installation/Removal Tips — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Glass >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Body - Rear Bolt-In Glass Installation/Removal Tips Body - Rear Bolt-In Glass Installation/Removal Tips TSB 05-11-9 06/13/05 REMOVAL AND INSTALLATION OF REAR BOLT-IN GLASS - SERVICE TIP FORD: 2001-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, F-150, Ranger ISSUE Some 2001-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, Ranger, and F-150 vehicles may require replacement or re-sealing of the bolt-in rear glass. This TSB procedure supplements the Workshop Manual to prevent damage to the glass and body during removal, and leaks after installing glass. The 2006 Workshop Manual will be updated to incorporate these changes. ACTION Use only a plastic tool to break the foam core butyl seal when removing the glass. When installing glass use only 5/16"" (8 mm) foam core butyl for sealing. Refer to the following Service Procedure. SERVICE PROCEDURE GLASS REMOVAL 1. Begin glass removal by following the procedure in the Workshop Manual, up to and including removing the attachment nuts. NOTE THE BACK WINDOW GLASS HAS A FOAM CORE BUTYL PLACED ON THE RUBBER SEAL TO PREVENT LEAKS. THIS BUTYL SEAL MUST BE BROKEN TO REMOVE THE GLASS MODULE FROM THE BODY. NOTE TO BREAK THE BUTYL SEAL USE ONLY A PLASTIC TOOL, REFERRED TO IN THE AUTOMOTIVE GLASS INDUSTRY AS A ""PLASTIC"" WINDSHIELD SETTING TOOL (FIGURE 1). 2. Slide the plastic setting tool under the window glass outside rubber seal between the attaching studs at one of the corners, to cut through the foam butyl. At the same time apply light hand pressure to the glass from the inside of the vehicle, pressing outward (Figure 2). 3. Once the glass module begins to separate from the body, continue to apply constant hand pressure from within the vehicle while moving around the perimeter of the glass. This will continue to break the foam core butyl seal. Once the seal is completely broken, the glass module may be removed. 4. Remove any remaining foam butyl from the body and window rubber seal before glass installation. GLASS INSTALLATION NOTE DO NOT USE A ""SOLID TYPE"" BUTYL OR URETHANE AND ATTEMPT TO ROLL IT TO MAKE IT ROUND, THIS WILL CREATE A LEAK. IT WILL ALSO MAKE THE NEXT GLASS REMOVAL EXTREMELY DIFFICULT. 1. Apply the 5/16"" (8 mm) foam core butyl to the rear window glass rubber seal, starting at the bottom middle and working around. 2. Overlap the foam butyl by 1"" (25 mm) at the starting/finishing points. 3. Complete the installation by following the procedure in the Workshop Manual. 4. Torque the attaching nuts to: ^ 2001-2003 F-150 27 lb-in (3 N.m) ^ 2004 F-150 Heritage 27 lb-in (3 N.m) ^ 2004-2005 F-150 35 lb-in (4 N.m) ^ Explorer Sport Trac 27 lb-in (3 N.m) ^ Ranger 18 lb-in (2 N.m) WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 70422B30 07 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5744.html,Rear Door Window Glass: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REAR DOOR;REMOVAL 1;SPECIAL TOOL;WINDOW GLASS,"Rear Door Window Glass: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Glass >> Rear Door Window Glass >> Service and Repair Rear Door Window Glass: Service and Repair REAR DOOR WINDOW GLASS Heavy Duty Riveter: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL 1. Remove the rear door trim panel . 2. Remove the interior glass weatherstrip . 3. Remove the rear door belt line moulding nut. 4. CAUTION: Do not strike or force the rear door belt line moulding during the installation. The rear door belt line moulding is made of aluminum and will be damaged. NOTE: During installation, make sure that the rear door belt line moulding fits flush with the edge of the sheet metal and the door panel shelf. Remove the rear door belt line moulding. 5. Position aside the water shield. 6. Connect the power window switch. 7. Remove the rear door window glass rivets. - Lower the glass approximately two-inches to access the rivets through the holes. 8. Carefully lower the window regulator while holding the glass. - Lower the glass. 9. Separate the front of the window run/ weatherstrip from the door. 10. Remove the rear door window glass through the outboard side of the rear door. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Use the special tool to install the rivets. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5745.html,Front Door Window Glass: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;FRONT DOOR;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1;SPECIAL TOOL;WINDOW GLASS,"Front Door Window Glass: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Glass >> Front Door Window Glass >> Service and Repair Front Door Window Glass: Service and Repair FRONT DOOR WINDOW GLASS Heavy Duty Riveter: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL 1. Remove the front door trim panel . 2. CAUTION: Do not strike or force the front door belt line moulding during installation. The front door belt line moulding is made of aluminum and will be damaged. NOTE: During installation, make sure that the front door belt line moulding fits flush with the edge of the sheet metal and the door panel shelf. Remove the front door belt line moulding. 1 Remove the nut. 2 Remove the moulding. 3. Remove the interior glass weatherstrip . 4. NOTE: Lower the window glass to access the rivets. Remove the front door window glass rivets. 5. Remove the front door window glass through the outboard side of the front door. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Use the special tool to install the rivets. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5746.html,Rear Window Glass - Power — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,10,,0.23 in;6 mm,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ESB-M3G143-B;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;POWER REMOVAL 1;REAR WINDOW GLASS,"Rear Window Glass - Power — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Glass >> Back Window Glass >> Service and Repair >> Rear Window Glass - Power Rear Window Glass - Power REAR WINDOW GLASS - POWER REMOVAL 1. Remove the C-pillar trim panel. 2. Remove the spare tire and jack assembly. 3. Remove the roof trim panel. 4. If equipped, remove the sub-woofer assembly. 1 Disconnect the electronic connector. 2 Remove the bolts. 5. NOTE: Do not remove the power rear window motor water shield. Remove the carpet pin-type retainers and pull the carpet back. 6. Position the rear window glass regulator access panel aside. 1 Remove the screws. 2 Remove the nut. 3 Position the rear window glass regulator access panel aside. 7. Position the rear window glass to the 3/4 down position. 8. Remove the rear window weatherstrip moulding. 9. Remove the rear window glass bolts. 10. NOTE: When securing the rear window glass note that the rear window glass and module will be removed with the rear window glass in the secured position. Secure the rear window glass in the full up position. 11. Remove the 12 rear window glass module nuts. 12. Push the rear window glass module out at the top. 13. NOTE: In order for the rear window glass to function correctly the locating clip must engage the pinch weld at the rear of the cab during installation. Lift the rear window glass module from the rear of the cab to disengage the locating clip. 14. Remove the excess foam butyl from the window opening. 15. If necessary, remove the center rear window glass from the module. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Apply 6 mm (0.23 in) Foam Butyl or equivalent meeting Ford specification ESB-M3G143-B to the rear window glass module. - Start at the bottom and work around the module. 2. Reinitialize the rear window glass motor. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5747.html,Rear Window Positioning — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,6,,0.8 in;20 mm,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;CLOSE;DOWN;LEMON;NOTE;OPEN;POSITIONING;REAR WINDOW,"Rear Window Positioning — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Window Glass >> Back Window Glass >> Service and Repair >> Rear Window Positioning Rear Window Positioning REAR WINDOW POSITIONING CAUTION: - Make sure that no obstructions are present in the power rear window system when carrying out this procedure. - If the glass/regulator system is binding, the system must be diagnosed and a new component must be installed. Do not apply hand pressure to glass that does not move freely. NOTE: - Because the power rear window removal/installation position is approximately three-quarters down and the power rear window motor can only move the window to three positions, a special procedure is necessary to position the window to the removal/installation position. - If the power rear window motor does not respond to this procedure, refer to the diagnosis and testing for repair. If the window must be removed and the window motor does not respond to this procedure, remove the window motor. The window then can be moved by carefully applying hand pressure in the downward direction. - By only partially carrying out the power rear window motor initialization procedure, the window motor will enter error mode. In error mode, no window motor movement is possible and the window motor will have to be reinitialized. Refer to Rear Window Motor Initialization. - The key-in-ignition chime can cause the vent button to be pressed more or less than six times due to the distraction of the chime. 1. NOTE: Steps 1-6 must be completed within 30 seconds . Start with the ignition in the OFF position. Open the driver door. 2. Turn the ignition to the ON position. 3. Press the power rear window control switch vent button six times. 4. Turn the ignition to the OFF position. The driver door must be open. 5. Press the power rear window control switch vent button six times. 6. Turn the ignition to the ON position. The power rear window will move down-up-down-up approximately 20 mm (0.8 in) . This movement indicates that the window motor has entered initialization mode. 7. Rotate and hold the power rear window control switch to the CLOSE position until the window stalls into the upper header seal. 8. Momentarily rotate the power rear window control switch to the OPEN position and release. The window will carry out a one-touch down operation until the window stalls at the bottom of the travel stop designed into the window regulator . 9. Rotate and hold the power rear window control switch to the CLOSE position momentarily until the window regulator glass attach bolts are lined up with the sheet metal access holes. The window will be approximately in the three-quarter DOWN position when installed to the window regulator. 10. Repeat this procedure if the window regulator glass attach bolts are raised too far above the sheet metal access holes. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
