5765.html,Body - Power Rear Window Bounces Open When Closing — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,12,,8 lb-ft,03-19-5;031905A;031905B;0L VIN K;15-20;164-R4900;164-R4906;1960-2025;1L5Z-7823394-BA;2001-2004;2004;2WD V6-4;ACTION;ARTICLES;BODY;BOUNCES BACK;CLOSING;CLOSING FORD;CODE 7823394 42;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;DO NOT;ELECTRICAL;EXPLORER SPORT;IF MOTOR;LEMON;NECESSARY;NONE WARRANTY;OPEN WHEN;OPERATION;OTHER APPLICABLE;PART NO;POWER REAR;PROCEDURE NOTE;REGULATOR;REPLACE THE;REPLACEMENT IS;SERVICE;STATUS;TRAC ISSUE;TWICE;WINDOW,"Body - Power Rear Window Bounces Open When Closing — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Power Window Motor >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> Body - Power Rear Window Bounces Open When Closing Body - Power Rear Window Bounces Open When Closing Article No. 03-19-5 09/29/03 ^ BODY - POWER REAR WINDOW BOUNCES BACK OPEN WHEN CLOSING ^ ELECTRICAL - POWER REAR WINDOW BOUNCES BACK OPEN WHEN CLOSING FORD: 2001-2004 EXPLORER SPORT TRAC ISSUE Some vehicles upon closing the rear power window may exhibit a window bounce back to the fully: open position. The condition will typically occur when the window is almost to the top of the fully closed position. ACTION The updated Service Motor (1L5Z-7823394-BA) should only be installed it bounce back condition is verified, and replacement is directed per the following service procedure. SERVICE PROCEDURE NOTE IF MOTOR REPLACEMENT IS NECESSARY, DO NOT REPLACE THE WINDOW REGULATOR . 1. Inspect for damage to side run channels, especially near the reversal point. 2. With the power rear window glass down, loosen the two (2) glass attachment bolts. 3. With the bolts loose but still attached, operate the power rear window up/down twice. 4. Retighten the bolts to 11 N.m (8 lb-ft). 5. Apply Krytox grease (164-R4906) from Rotunda Squeak & Rattle Kit (164-R4900) to the glass runs and regulator rails and initialize the power rear window. Refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10. 6. Cycle the power rear window up and down 15-20 times to work in Krytox. 7. Re-initialize the power rear window motor. Refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10. 8. Verify repair. Repeat Steps 2-7 if necessary. 9. If the condition is still present after following this procedure TWICE, then replace the power rear window motor with the updated service motor (1L5Z-7823394-BA), re-initialize (refer to Quick Initialization Guide Figures 1-10), and verify the repair. Parts Block OTHER APPLICABLE ARTICLES: NONE WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of The New Vehicle Limited Warranty. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 031905A Apply Grease To Rear 0.9 Hr. Power Window Channel (Includes Time To Remove And Install Rear Trim Panel And To Perform Procedure Twice Then Verify Repair) 031905B Apply Grease To Rear 1.1 Hrs. Power Window Channel (Includes Time To Remove And Install Rear Trim Panel And To Perform Procedure Twice Then Verify Repair) If Concern Still Exists Replace Window Motor DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7823394 42 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5766.html,Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,2,,,07 REAR POWER;072005A 2002;072005B 2002;072005C 2002;072005D 2002;072005E 2002;07200SF 2002;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2002-2005;2002-2006;2003-2005;2004;2005;2006;2006 0;2006 1;27406B;27406B8;27406B9;2WD V6-4;501-11;ACTION;CODE 7823394 07;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;IMPORTANT;INOPERATIVE;ISSUE;LEMON;LINCOLN;MERCURY;OPERATION;PART NO;PROCEDURE 1;SERVICE;STATUS;STUCK IN THE;TSB 07-16;TSB 07-20;UP POSITION FORD;WARRANTY;WINDOW MOTOR,"Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Power Window Motor >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative TSB 07-20-5 10/15/07 REAR POWER WINDOW MOTOR INOPERATIVE/STUCK IN THE UP POSITION FORD: 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac 2002-2006 Explorer LINCOLN: 2003-2005 Aviator MERCURY: 2002-2006 Mountaineer This article supersedes TSB 07-16-14 to update the Part List. ISSUE Some 2002-2006 Explorer, Mountaineer and 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, and 2003-2005 Aviator vehicles built before 1/23/2006 may experience a rear power window that sticks in the up position. This condition can be intermittent and may be due to the power motor which temporarily locks up. ACTION Follow the Service Procedure steps to correct the condition. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Use the current Workshop Manual (WSM), Section 501-11 procedure to remove the door panel and inspect the window regulator for damaged parts. 2. If any damage part or parts are found replace the regulator assembly. 3. If no damaged parts are found on the regulator assembly, replace the window regulator motor using WSM, Section 501-11. Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage IMPORTANT : Warranty coverage limits/policies are not altered by a TSB. Warranty coverage limits are determined by the identified causal part. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 072005A 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 0.9 Hr. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005B 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 1.6 Hrs. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005C 2002-2006 0.4 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005D 2002-2006 0.7 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005E 2002-2006 0.6 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 07200SF 2002-2006 1.1 Hrs. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7823394 07 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
