5773.html,Rear Door Window Regulator Motor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REAR DOOR;REGULATOR MOTOR;REMOVAL 1;WINDOW,"Rear Door Window Regulator Motor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Power Window Motor >> Rear Door Window Motor >> Service and Repair >> Rear Door Window Regulator Motor Rear Door Window Regulator Motor REAR DOOR WINDOW REGULATOR MOTOR REMOVAL 1. Remove the rear door window regulator. 2. Remove the rear door window regulator motor. 1 Remove the bolts. 2 Remove the rear door window regulator motor. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Cycle the door glass to make sure of engagement of the drive mechanism. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
5774.html,Rear Window Glass Motor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,4,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;MOTOR REMOVAL NOTE;NOTE;REAR WINDOW GLASS,"Rear Window Glass Motor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Windows and Glass >> Windows >> Power Window Motor >> Rear Door Window Motor >> Service and Repair >> Rear Window Glass Motor Rear Window Glass Motor REAR WINDOW GLASS - MOTOR REMOVAL NOTE: - The power rear window motor can be removed and a new one installed without removing the seat or trim panel . - When the power rear window motor is removed and installed, the motor must be initialized. 1. Fold down the passenger rear seat back . 2. Open the luggage compartment trim panel access door. 3. Remove the spare tire jack and handle assembly. 4. NOTE: The rear window glass water shield uses a reusable butyl rubber adhesive. A new water shield does not have to be installed unless it is damaged or if the butyl rubber adhesive does not adhere to a section of the sheet metal. Position the carpet aside and position the water shield back from the rear window glass motor to access bolts. 5. CAUTION: Use care not to damage the drum housing when removing the rear window glass motor. NOTE: Apply pressure to the drum while removing the rear window motor to avoid extraction of the drum with the motor. Remove the rear window motor. 1 Disconnect the electrical connector. 2 Remove the bolts. 3 Remove the rear window glass motor. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: The rear window motor must be initialized after a repair is carried out. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
