 BIAS THE MIDDLE OF THE TAPE TOWARD THE TAB OVER APPROXIMATELY 25.5 MM (1"") BEFORE REACHING THE TAB. COVER THE TAB, THEN TRANSITION BACK TO EVENLY APPLYING THE TAPE TO BOTH LENS AND HOUSING. INSPECT THE TABS TO MAKE SURE THE TAPE COMPLETELY SEALS THE LENS AND HOUSING. 10. While peeling backing paper off the tape, approximately 8-15 cm (3-6"") at a time, apply the tape to the seam between the lens and housing, starting at bottom center of lamp (Figure 3). Position the middle of tape over glue track (seam), so tape is evenly applied to both lens and housing. Stretch tape slightly when applying, particularly around the corners. This is important to minimize tape bunching around the corners. It is recommended that tape be applied first to the chrome body, then wrapped over onto the lens to minimize trapping air bubbles. Continue applying tape around entire edge of lamp until reaching the starting point. Overlap tape about 25.5 mm (1""), and trim off excess tape. 11. Press down tape securely around entire edge to assure adhesion along entire repair area, particularly at the final overlap joint. A finger or small blunt tool should be used. A good tape seal is essential to a lasting repair. 12. Reinstall the four (4) lens retaining clips over the tape repair. If excess tape thickness prevents clip installation, carefully trim back edge of tape on housing side ONLY to permit clip installation (Figure 1). 13. Reinstall the light bulbs. 14. Reinstall headlamp assembly. PARTS BLOCK WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 041303A Reseal One 04.Hr. Headlamp Assembly (Includes Time To Remove And Install Headlamp ) 041303B Reseal Both 0.7Hr. Headlamp Assemblies (Includes Time To Remove And Install Head lamps) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 13007 63 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
