5813.html,Turn Signal Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension;Wiring,4,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Turn Signal Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Lighting and Horns >> Turn Signals >> Turn Signal Switch >> Service and Repair Turn Signal Switch: Service and Repair Multifunction Switch Removal and Installation 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. Remove the ignition switch lock cylinder . 1. Insert the ignition key into the ignition switch lock cylinder and turn to RUN position. 2. Push the ignition switch lock cylinder release tab with a punch while pulling out the ignition switch lock cylinder. 3. If equipped, twist the tilt wheel handle and shank counterclockwise and remove. 4. Remove the upper and lower steering column shrouds. 1. Remove the screws. 2. Remove the upper and lower steering column shrouds. 5. Remove the multifunction switch. 1. Remove the screws. 2. Disconnect the electrical connectors. 3. Remove the multifunction switch. 6. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
