6152.html,Dimmer Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DIMMER;INSTALLATION 1;INSTRUMENT PANEL;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;SWITCH,"Dimmer Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Sensors and Switches - Instrument Panel >> Dimmer Switch >> Service and Repair Dimmer Switch: Service and Repair INSTRUMENT PANEL DIMMER SWITCH REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery. 2. Remove the center instrument panel finish panel. - Remove the screws. - Disconnect the electrical connectors. 3. Remove the screws and position the hood latch release handle aside. 4. Remove the screws and remove the instrument panel steering column cover. 5. Remove the instrument panel steering column opening cover reinforcement. 6. Position the column-mounted transmission range selector lever aside. 7. Remove the screws and pull the instrument cluster finish panel out from the instrument panel. 8. Disconnect the headlamp and the dimmer switch electrical connectors and remove the instrument cluster finish panel. 9. Remove the screws and the instrument panel dimmer switch. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6153.html,Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BELT MINDER;CHIME;INDICATOR AND;LEMON;SAFETY BELT;WARNING,"Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Seat Belt Reminder Lamp >> Description and Operation Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation SAFETY BELT WARNING INDICATOR AND CHIME The safety belt warning indicator illuminates and a chime sounds to remind the occupants to fasten their safety belts. The conditions of operation for the safety belt waring indicator and chime are as follows: - If the driver safety belt is not buckled before the ignition switch is turned to RUN, the safety belt warning indicator illuminates for 1-2 minutes and the warning chime sounds for 4-8 seconds . - If the driver safety belt is buckled while the warning indicator is illuminated and the reminder chime is sounding, the safety belt warning indicator and reminder chime will turn off. - If the driver safety belt is buckled before the ignition switch is turned to the ON position, the safety belt warning indicator and reminder chime will remain off. BELT MINDER The Belt Minder feature is a supplemental warning to the safety belt warning function. This feature provides an additional reminder to the driver and/or passenger that the safety belt is unbuckled by intermittently sounding a chime and illuminating the safety belt warning lamp in the instrument cluster. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
