6166.html,Key Reminder Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension;Interior,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;IGNITION;INSTALLATION 1;KEY-IN-;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;SWITCH;WARNING,"Key Reminder Switch: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Instrument Panel, Gauges and Warning Indicators >> Key Reminder Switch >> Service and Repair Key Reminder Switch: Service and Repair SWITCH - KEY-IN-IGNITION WARNING REMOVAL 1. Remove the ignition switch lock cylinder . 1 Insert the ignition key and turn to the RUN position. 2 Insert a punch in the access hole of the steering column and press the release tab while pulling out the ignition switch lock cylinder . 2. Remove the key-in-ignition warning switch. 1 Pry the clip down. 2 Push the key-in-ignition warning switch off the rear of the ignition switch lock cylinder . INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Verify ignition switch lock cylinder operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
