6267.html,Brake Switch (Cruise Control): Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Wiring,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;DEACTIVATOR;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;SPEED CONTROL;SWITCH;WARNING,"Brake Switch (Cruise Control): Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Cruise Control >> Brake Switch (Cruise Control) >> Service and Repair Brake Switch (Cruise Control): Service and Repair SPEED CONTROL DEACTIVATOR SWITCH REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. Disconnect the speed control deactivator switch electrical connector. 3. WARNING: Brake fluid contains polyglycol ethers and polyglycols. Avoid contact with eyes. Wash hands thoroughly after handling. If brake fluid contacts eyes, flush eyes with running water for 15 minutes. Get medical attention if irritation persists. If taken internally, drink water and induce vomiting. Get medical attention immediately. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. CAUTION: Brake fluid is harmful to painted and plastic surfaces. If brake fluid is spilled onto a painted or plastic surface, immediately wash it with water. Remove the speed control deactivator switch. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Bleed the brake system. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
