ited Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 051008A 2001-2003 Explorer Sport 0.3 Hr. (2Dr), 2001-2004 Explorer Sport Trac, 2003-2004 Ranger, Replace The Center Finish Panel (Do Not Use With 18805B, 18805C) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7004302 42 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6278.html,Body - Moonroof Squeak or Rattle Noise — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,6,,,05 MOONROOF;050304A 2001;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2001-2003;2001-2005;2002-2005;2003;2003-2005;2004;2WD V6-4;ACTION;CODE 78502B36 01;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;CORNER;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;INSERT;ISSUE;LEMON;LINCOLN;MERCURY;OPERATION;OR RATTLE NOISE;PART NO;PROCEDURE 1;REPAIR FORD;SERVICE;SQUEAK AND;STATUS;TSB 05-3;WARRANTY,"Body - Moonroof Squeak or Rattle Noise — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Technical Service Bulletins >> By Symptom >> Customer Interest >> Body - Moonroof Squeak or Rattle Noise Body - Moonroof Squeak or Rattle Noise TSB 05-3-4 02/21/05 MOONROOF SQUEAK AND/OR RATTLE NOISE - CORNER INSERT REPAIR FORD: 2001-2003 Explorer Sport 2001-2005 Explorer Sport Trac 2002-2005 Explorer LINCOLN: 2003-2005 Aviator MERCURY: 2002-2005 Mountaineer ISSUE Some 2001-2003 Explorer Sport, 2001-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, 2002-2005 Explorer 4dr/Mountaineer, and 2003-2005 Lincoln Aviator vehicles may exhibit a squeak and/or rattle noise coming from the moonroof area. It is no longer necessary to replace the entire moonroof rail assembly. A new corner insert is now available to correct the condition (Figure 2). ACTION The corner inserts are located in both front corners of the moonroof track and can be accessed by cycling the moonroof glass to the full open position. The original corner insert design had snap tabs that may break off during installation, creating a rattle condition. Replace both of the original inserts and remove any broken tabs left in the track. Refer to the following Service Procedure. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Open the moonroof to the full open position. 2. To determine if the corner inserts have broken snap tabs, pull up on the part with a screwdriver and inspect the snap tabs (Figures 1 and 2). 3. Remove both the inserts from the moonroof. Also, examine the track and remove any loose debris (Figure 3). 4. Install a new corner insert on both sides (Figure 4). Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 050304A 2001-2003 Explorer Sport, 0.3Hr. 2001-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, 2002-2005 Explorer 4dr/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Lincoln Aviator: Replace Both Of The Moonroof Corner Inserts DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 78502B36 01 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6279.html,Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,6,,,04 POWER;041606A;041606B;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2003;2003-2004;2004;2WD V6-4;ACTION;BE NOTICEABLE;BEFORE;BLADDER;BOARD IS;CODE 7064842 42;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;CORRECTLY IT;CRITICAL;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;EXPANDING;INSTALLING ZIP;IS INSTALLED;ISSUE;LEMON;LOWER SEAT FRAME;LUMBAR;LUMBER BOARD;MATERIAL IS;NOTE IF THE;NOTE POSITION OF;OF SEAT FORD;ONCE THE SEAT;OPERATION;PART NO;POSITION;PROCEDURE 1;REINSTALLED;SERVICE;SHOULD NOT;STATUS;THROUGH BACK;TIES ONTO THE;TSB 04-16;VERIFY BOARD;WARRANTY,"Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Technical Service Bulletins >> By Symptom >> Customer Interest >> Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back TSB 04-16-6 08/23/04 POWER LUMBAR BLADDER EXPANDING THROUGH BACK OF SEAT FORD: 2003 Explorer Sport 2003-2004 Explorer Sport Trac ISSUE Some 2003-2004 Explorer Sport Trac and 2003 Explorer Sport 2dr vehicles may exhibit a power lumbar bladder pushing out the back of the seat when inflated. ACTION To service, install a lumbar support board in the rear of the seat back between the metal cross member on the frame and the lumbar bladder. The board must be installed exactly as outlined in the following Service Procedure to be completely effective. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Cycle seat track to full forward position in vehicle to access back of seat assembly. 2. Set seat to full upright position. 3. Release air from bladder using the lumbar switch (fully deflate lumbar support). 4. Using flathead screw driver, pry the ""J""-retainer apart on the bottom of seat back cover (Figure 1). 5. While pulling bottom of trim cover away from frame , slide board (with holes down and foam facing toward the rear of the seat) up into seat back (Figure 2). 6. Sandwich the board between the metal cross member on frame and lumbar bladder (Figure 3). 7. Secure board with two (2) zip ties thorough holes in board and around lower cross member on frame (Figure 4). NOTE POSITION OF BOARD IS CRITICAL. VERIFY BOARD POSITION BEFORE INSTALLING ZIP TIES ONTO THE LOWER SEAT FRAME . 8. Re-secure ""J""-retainer on bottom of trim cover. 9. Test Lumbar Support for correct operation. NOTE IF THE LUMBER BOARD IS INSTALLED CORRECTLY IT SHOULD NOT BE NOTICEABLE ONCE THE SEAT MATERIAL IS REINSTALLED. Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 041606A Install Lumbar Support 0.3 Hr. Board One Seat 041606B Install Lumbar Support 0.5 Hr. Board Both Seats DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7064842 42 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6280.html,Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,2,,,07 REAR POWER;072005A 2002;072005B 2002;072005C 2002;072005D 2002;072005E 2002;07200SF 2002;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2002-2005;2002-2006;2003-2005;2004;2005;2006;2006 0;2006 1;27406B;27406B8;27406B9;2WD V6-4;501-11;ACTION;CODE 7823394 07;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;IMPORTANT;INOPERATIVE;ISSUE;LEMON;LINCOLN;MERCURY;OPERATION;PART NO;PROCEDURE 1;SERVICE;STATUS;STUCK IN THE;TSB 07-16;TSB 07-20;UP POSITION FORD;WARRANTY;WINDOW MOTOR,"Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Technical Service Bulletins >> By Symptom >> Customer Interest >> Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative Body - Rear Door Window Stuck In Up Position/Inoperative TSB 07-20-5 10/15/07 REAR POWER WINDOW MOTOR INOPERATIVE/STUCK IN THE UP POSITION FORD: 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac 2002-2006 Explorer LINCOLN: 2003-2005 Aviator MERCURY: 2002-2006 Mountaineer This article supersedes TSB 07-16-14 to update the Part List. ISSUE Some 2002-2006 Explorer, Mountaineer and 2002-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, and 2003-2005 Aviator vehicles built before 1/23/2006 may experience a rear power window that sticks in the up position. This condition can be intermittent and may be due to the power motor which temporarily locks up. ACTION Follow the Service Procedure steps to correct the condition. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Use the current Workshop Manual (WSM), Section 501-11 procedure to remove the door panel and inspect the window regulator for damaged parts. 2. If any damage part or parts are found replace the regulator assembly. 3. If no damaged parts are found on the regulator assembly, replace the window regulator motor using WSM, Section 501-11. Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage IMPORTANT : Warranty coverage limits/policies are not altered by a TSB. Warranty coverage limits are determined by the identified causal part. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 072005A 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 0.9 Hr. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005B 2002-2005 Explorer Sport 1.6 Hrs. Trac: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor Or Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005C 2002-2006 0.4 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005D 2002-2006 0.7 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Motor, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel: Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 072005E 2002-2006 0.6 Hr. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : One Rear Door (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) 07200SF 2002-2006 1.1 Hrs. Explorer/Mountaineer, 2003-2005 Aviator: Replace The Rear Door Window Regulator, Includes Time To Remove And Install Interior Door Trim Panel : Both Rear Doors (Do Not Use With 27406B, 27406B8, 27406B9) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7823394 07 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6281.html,Body - Rattle Noise From Tailgate — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,2,Torque the new tailgate striker to 30 lb-ft +/- 4 lb-ft (40 N.m +/- 6 N.m). WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage IMPORT,30 lb-ft;4 lb-ft,07 TAILGATE;072502A 2004;072502B 2004;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2004-2005;2004-2008 F;2006-2008;2007-2008;2008 F;2WD V6-4;40442A;ACTION;CODE 99404A42 30;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;IMPORTANT;LEMON;LINCOLN;LT ISSUE;NOISE;OPERATION;PART NO;PROCEDURE 1;RATTLE FORD;SERVICE;STATUS;STRIKER;TSB 07-25;WARRANTY,"Body - Rattle Noise From Tailgate — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Technical Service Bulletins >> By Symptom >> Customer Interest >> Body - Rattle Noise From Tailgate Body - Rattle Noise From Tailgate TSB 07-25-2 12/24/07 TAILGATE STRIKER - NOISE/RATTLE FORD: 2004-2005 Explorer Sport Trac 2004-2008 F-150, F-Super Duty 2007-2008 Explorer Sport Trac LINCOLN: 2006-2008 Mark LT ISSUE Some 2004-2008 F-Super Duty and F-150, 2006-2008 Mark LT, and 2004-2005 and 2007-2008 Explorer Sport Trac vehicles with a customer complaint of a noise or rattle in the tailgate may have worn tailgate striker sleeves. This condition may be found on vehicles used in severe conditions such as fleet applications or repetitive rough road/off-road applications. ACTION Follow the Service Procedure steps to correct the condition. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Remove the tailgate striker bolt using a T50 Torx bit. 2. Replace the tailgate striker with a new striker. 3. Align the tailgate striker up/down to the tailgate latch and adjust in/out for margin flushness. 4. Torque the new tailgate striker to 30 lb-ft +/- 4 lb-ft (40 N.m +/- 6 N.m). WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage IMPORTANT : Warranty coverage limits/policies are not altered by a TSB. Warranty coverage limits are determined by the identified causal part. OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 072502A 2004-2008 F-150, F-Super 0.2 Hr. Duty, 2006-2008 Mark LT and 2004-2005 and 2007-2008 Explorer Sport Trac: Replace One Tailgate Striker , Includes Time To Align Tailgate (Do Not Use With 40442A) 072502B 2004-2008 F-150, F-Super 0.3 Hr. Duty, 2006-2008 Mark LT and 2004-2005 and 2007-2008 Explorer Sport Trac: Replace Both Tailgate Strikers , Includes Time To Align Tailgate (Do Not Use With 40442A) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 99404A42 30 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
