6309.html,Tonneau Cover Latch Release Cable — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSTALLATION 1;LATCH RELEASE CABLE;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL NOTE;TONNEAU COVER,"Tonneau Cover Latch Release Cable — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Truck Bed >> Truck Bed Cover >> Service and Repair >> Tonneau Cover Latch Release Cable Tonneau Cover Latch Release Cable TONNEAU COVER LATCH RELEASE CABLE REMOVAL NOTE: Front tonneau cover latch release cable shown, rear tonneau cover latch release cable similar. 1. NOTE: Mark location of bolts to latch bracket. Remove the four bolts (two each side) and position the LH and RH tonneau cover latches aside. 2. NOTE: Tonneau cover release cables are not reuseable. Discard cables once removed. Disconnect the tonneau cover cables from the LH and RH latches. 1 Disconnect the cable conduit. 2 Remove the cable end from the lever arm. 3. Disconnect the lock actuator housing from the lock cylinder and remove the tonneau cover latch release cable. - Twist and pull upward. INSTALLATION 1. Route the new tonneau cover latch release cable through the tonneau cover. 2. NOTE: Install the lock actuator housing into place with the molded line facing outward. Install the lock actuator housing. - Twist and push downward.The lock actuator housing will snap into place. 3. Connect the tonneau cover latch release cables to the LH and RH latches. 1 Insert the cable end through the lever arm. 2 Snap the cable conduit into the opening. 4. Position the tonneau cover latches and Install the four bolts. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
