6383.html,Front Manual — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,6,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FRONT MANUAL;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;SEAT TRACK,Front Manual — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Track >> Service and Repair >> Front Manual Front Manual SEAT TRACK - FRONT MANUAL REMOVAL 1. Remove the front seat and depower the supplemental restraint system (SRS). 2. Remove the safety belt buckle support. 1 Remove the nut. 2 Remove the bolt. 3 Remove the safety belt buckle support. 3. Remove the seat track to seat cushion front bolts. 4. Remove the front seat track . 1 Remove the seat track to seat cushion rear bolts. 2 Remove the front seat track . INSTALLATION 1. Install the front seat track front bolts. 1 Position the front seat track . 2 Install the inboard bolt. 3 Install the outboard bolt. 2. Install the front seat track rear bolts. 1 Install the inboard bolt. 2 Install the outboard bolt. 3. Install the safety belt buckle slide bar onto the seat. 1 Position the safety belt buckle slide bar to the seat. 2 Install the nut and bolt. 4. Install the front seat and repower the SRS. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
6384.html,Front Power — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,6,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FRONT POWER;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL NOTE;SEAT TRACK,"Front Power — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Track >> Service and Repair >> Front Power Front Power SEAT TRACK - FRONT POWER REMOVAL NOTE: The driver side shown, passenger side similar. 1. Remove the front seat and depower the supplemental restraint system (SRS). 2. Remove the safety belt buckle support. 1 Remove the nut. 2 Remove the bolt. 3 Remove the safety belt buckle support. 3. Disconnect the seat track wiring harness electrical connector. 4. Remove the seat track . 1 Remove the bolts. 2 Remove the seat track . INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: When installing the power seat track, start at the corner with the round hole and work around the seat base in a horseshoe pattern. Install the seat track . 2. Connect the seat track wiring harness electrical connectors. 3. Install the safety belt buckle slide bar onto the seat. 1 Position the safety belt buckle slide bar to the seat. 2 Install the nut and bolt. 4. Install the front seat and repower the SRS. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
