6408.html,Front Seat Cushion — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Wiring;Interior,23,Tighten until the screws are fully seated. 16. Install the seat cushion . scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ASSEMBLY;CUSHION;DISASSEMBLY;FRONT SEAT;LEMON;NOTE,"Front Seat Cushion — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Cushion >> Service and Repair >> Disassembly and Assembly >> Front Seat Cushion Front Seat Cushion FRONT SEAT CUSHION DISASSEMBLY All vehicles 1. Remove the seat cushion . 2. Disconnect the seat backrest recliner actuator. 1 Remove the screws. 2 Disconnect the seat backrest recliner actuator. Vehicles with heated seats 3. Disconnect the cushion heated seat element electrical connector. Vehicles with power lumbar 4. Release the rear J-clip and remove the power lumbar motor screw. 5. Remove the power lumbar motor. 1 Disconnect the power lumbar motor electrical connector. 2 Remove the power lumbar bladder hose. 3 Remove the power lumbar motor. All vehicles 6. Remove the seat cushion frame from the seat cushion foam. 1 Unhook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 2 Remove the seat cushion frame from the seat cushion foam. 7. Invert the seat cushion trim cover. 8. Remove the swing rod to tie-down wire hog rings from the side swing rods (one on each side). 9. NOTE: The hog rings along the front of the seat are shown, the hog rings along either side are similar. Remove and discard the hog rings. 1 Fold back the seat cushion trim cover to expose the hog rings. 2 Remove and discard the hog rings on the front and side. 10. Remove the swing rods. Vehicles with heated seats 11. Remove the cushion heated seat element. Vehicles with power seats 12. NOTE: Some component connectors may not exist due to vehicle options. Remove the power seat wiring harness. 1 Disconnect the pin-type retainers. 2 Remove the power seat wiring harness. All vehicles 13. Remove the flexilator. 1 Remove the flexilator springs. 2 Remove the flexilator. 14. Remove the seat backrest recliner roll pins and remove the seat backrest recliners. 15. Disconnect the seat backrest recliners from the seat backrest recliner actuator. 1 Disconnect the seat backrest recliner actuator cable housings from the seat backrest recliners. 2 Unhook the seat backrest recliner actuator cables from the seat backrest recliners. ASSEMBLY All vehicles 1. Connect the seat backrest recliners to the seat backrest recliner actuator. 1 Hook the seat backrest recliner actuator cables to the seat backrest recliners. 2 Connect the seat backrest recliner actuator cable housings to the seat backrest recliners. 2. Install the seat backrest recliner roll pins. 3. Install the flexilator. 1 Position the flexilator. 2 Install the flexilator springs. Vehicles with power seats 4. Install the power seat wiring harness. 1 Position the power seat wiring harness. 2 Install the pin-type retainers. Vehicles with heated seats 5. Install the heated seat element onto the cushion foam pad. All vehicles 6. Install the front swing rod. 7. NOTE: Make sure the swing rods are seated under the boarder wire in the foam near the back of the seat cushion . Install the swing rods. 8. NOTE: The hog rings along the front of the seat are shown; the hog-rings along either side are similar. Install the hog rings. 1 Fold back the seat cushion trim cover for the hog ring installation. 2 Install the hog ring to the center of the front swing rod to tie-down the rod in the seat cushion . 3 Install the hog ring to the front swing rod to tie-down the wire on the outboard sides. 9. Install the hog ring to the side swing rods (one on each side) to the tie-down the wire. 10. Invert the seat cushion trim cover. 11. Install the seat cushion foam to the seat cushion frame . Vehicles with power lumbar 12. Install the power lumbar motor. 1 Install the power lumbar motor. 2 Connect the power lumbar hose on the power lumbar motor. 3 Connect the power lumbar motor electrical connector. 13. Install the screw into the power lumbar motor and install the J-clip. All vehicles 14. Install the seat cushion frame . 1 Position the seat cushion frame . 2 Hook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 15. Connect the seat backrest recliner actuator. 1 Connect the seat backrest recliner actuator. 2 Install the screws. - Tighten until the screws are fully seated. 16. Install the seat cushion . scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6409.html,40 Percent — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;40 PERCENT;ASSEMBLY 1;CAUTION;CUSHION;DISASSEMBLY 1;LEMON;NOTE;REAR SEAT,40 Percent — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Cushion >> Service and Repair >> Disassembly and Assembly >> Rear Seat Cushion >> 40 Percent 40 Percent REAR SEAT CUSHION - 40 PERCENT DISASSEMBLY 1. Remove the rear seat. 2. Remove the rear seat legs. 1 Remove the pivot bolts. 2 Remove the rear seat legs. 3. Unhook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 4. CAUTION: Use care when separating the seat cushion trim cover from the hook and loop strip or the hook and loop strip may be torn from the seat cushion foam. Remove the seat cushion trim cover. - Separate the seat cushion trim cover from the hook and loop strip. 5. NOTE: Use the brackets on the seat cushion frame to obtain the necessary leverage to unhook the rear flex mat J-clip. Remove the seat cushion flex mat. 1 Unhook the rear flex mat J-clip. 2 Unhook the front flex mat J-clip. 3 Remove the seat cushion flex mat. ASSEMBLY 1. CAUTION: The flex mat J-clips must be installed with the openings facing down or the seat cushion may be damaged. NOTE: Use the brackets on the seat cushion frame to obtain the necessary leverage to hook the rear flex mat J-clip. Install the seat cushion flex mat. 1 Position the seat cushion flex mat. 2 Hook the front flex mat J-clip. 3 Hook the rear flex mat J-clip. 2. Position the seat cushion trim cover on the seat cushion hook and loop strips. 3. Hook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 4. Install the rear seat riser pivot bolts. 1 Position the rear seat legs. 2 Install the rear seat riser pivot bolts. 5. Install the rear seat. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
6410.html,60 Percent — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;60 PERCENT;ASSEMBLY 1;CAUTION;CUSHION;DISASSEMBLY 1;LEMON;NOTE;REAR SEAT,60 Percent — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Cushion >> Service and Repair >> Disassembly and Assembly >> Rear Seat Cushion >> 60 Percent 60 Percent REAR SEAT CUSHION - 60 PERCENT DISASSEMBLY 1. Remove the rear seat backrest. 2. Remove the seat cushion legs. 1 Remove the pivot bolts. 2 Remove the seat cushion legs. 3. Remove the seat cushion frame from the seat cushion foam. 1 Unhook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 2 Remove the seat cushion frame from the seat cushion foam. 4. Invert the seat cushion trim cover. 5. CAUTION: Use care when separating the seat cushion trim cover from the hook and loop strip or the hook and loop strip may be torn from the seat cushion foam. Remove the seat cushion trim cover. - Separate the seat cushion trim cover from the hook and loop strip. 6. NOTE: Use the brackets on the seat cushion frame to obtain the necessary leverage to unhook the rear flex mat J-clip. Remove the seat cushion flex mats. 1 Unhook the rear flex mat J-clips. 2 Unhook the front flex mat J-clips. 3 Remove the seat cushion flex mats. ASSEMBLY 1. CAUTION: The flex mat J-clips must be installed with the openings facing down or the seat cushion foam may be damaged. NOTE: Use the brackets on the seat cushion frame to obtain the necessary leverage to hook the rear flex mat clip. Install the seat cushion flex mats. 1 Position the seat cushion flex mats. 2 Hook the front flex mat J-clips. 3 Hook the rear flex mat J-clips. 2. Position the seat cushion trim cover on the seat cushion hook and loop strips. 3. Install the seat cushion frame into the seat cushion foam. 1 Position the seat cushion frame . 2 Hook the seat cushion trim cover J-clips. 4. Install the seat cushion legs. 1 Position the seat cushion legs. 2 Install the rear seat riser pivot bolts. 5. Install the rear seat backrest. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
