6412.html,Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,6,,,04 POWER;041606A;041606B;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2003;2003-2004;2004;2WD V6-4;ACTION;BE NOTICEABLE;BEFORE;BLADDER;BOARD IS;CODE 7064842 42;CODING;CONDITION BASIC;CORRECTLY IT;CRITICAL;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;EXPANDING;INSTALLING ZIP;IS INSTALLED;ISSUE;LEMON;LOWER SEAT FRAME;LUMBAR;LUMBER BOARD;MATERIAL IS;NOTE IF THE;NOTE POSITION OF;OF SEAT FORD;ONCE THE SEAT;OPERATION;PART NO;POSITION;PROCEDURE 1;REINSTALLED;SERVICE;SHOULD NOT;STATUS;THROUGH BACK;TIES ONTO THE;TSB 04-16;VERIFY BOARD;WARRANTY,"Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Seats >> Seat Back >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back Interior - Seat Lumber Bladder Pushes Out Seat Back TSB 04-16-6 08/23/04 POWER LUMBAR BLADDER EXPANDING THROUGH BACK OF SEAT FORD: 2003 Explorer Sport 2003-2004 Explorer Sport Trac ISSUE Some 2003-2004 Explorer Sport Trac and 2003 Explorer Sport 2dr vehicles may exhibit a power lumbar bladder pushing out the back of the seat when inflated. ACTION To service, install a lumbar support board in the rear of the seat back between the metal cross member on the frame and the lumbar bladder. The board must be installed exactly as outlined in the following Service Procedure to be completely effective. SERVICE PROCEDURE 1. Cycle seat track to full forward position in vehicle to access back of seat assembly. 2. Set seat to full upright position. 3. Release air from bladder using the lumbar switch (fully deflate lumbar support). 4. Using flathead screw driver, pry the ""J""-retainer apart on the bottom of seat back cover (Figure 1). 5. While pulling bottom of trim cover away from frame , slide board (with holes down and foam facing toward the rear of the seat) up into seat back (Figure 2). 6. Sandwich the board between the metal cross member on frame and lumbar bladder (Figure 3). 7. Secure board with two (2) zip ties thorough holes in board and around lower cross member on frame (Figure 4). NOTE POSITION OF BOARD IS CRITICAL. VERIFY BOARD POSITION BEFORE INSTALLING ZIP TIES ONTO THE LOWER SEAT FRAME . 8. Re-secure ""J""-retainer on bottom of trim cover. 9. Test Lumbar Support for correct operation. NOTE IF THE LUMBER BOARD IS INSTALLED CORRECTLY IT SHOULD NOT BE NOTICEABLE ONCE THE SEAT MATERIAL IS REINSTALLED. Parts Block WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 041606A Install Lumbar Support 0.3 Hr. Board One Seat 041606B Install Lumbar Support 0.5 Hr. Board Both Seats DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7064842 42 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
