6547.html,Air Bag System Reconnect Checklist — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AIR BAG;CHECKLIST;LEMON;RECONNECT,Air Bag System Reconnect Checklist — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Interior Moulding / Trim >> Dashboard / Instrument Panel >> Air Bag(s) Arming and Disarming >> Service and Repair >> Air Bag System Reconnect Checklist Air Bag System Reconnect Checklist AIR BAG RECONNECT CHECKLIST The checklist below should be completed following diagnosis or repair of any air bag system concern: - All restraint system diagnostic tools removed? - All in-seat harness connectors connected? - All air bag modules connected? - Safety belt pretensioner connectors connected? - Restraints control module (RCM) connected? - All sensors (front and side impact sensors) connected? - Safety canopy modules connected? - Safety canopy bridge resistor(s) connected? - RCM fuse installed? - Battery connected? scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
6548.html,Prove Out Procedure — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;PROCEDURE;PROVE OUT,"Prove Out Procedure — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Interior Moulding / Trim >> Dashboard / Instrument Panel >> Air Bag(s) Arming and Disarming >> Service and Repair >> Prove Out Procedure Prove Out Procedure PROVE OUT PROCEDURE Turn the ignition switch from the OFF to the ON position and visually monitor the air bag indicator with all SRS components connected or restraint system diagnostic tools installed. The air bag indicator will light continuously for approximately six seconds and then turn off. If an SRS fault is present, the air bag indicator will either: - fail to light. - remain lit continuously. - flash. The flashing might not occur until approximately 30 seconds after the ignition switch has been turned from the OFF to the ON position. This is the time required for the restraints control module (RCM) to complete the testing of the SRS. If the air bag indicator is inoperative and an SRS fault exists, a chime will sound in a pattern of five sets of five beeps. If this occurs, the air bag indicator will need to be repaired before diagnosis can continue. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
