6553.html,Console - Floor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CONSOLE;FLOOR;LEMON,"Console - Floor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Interior Moulding / Trim >> Console >> Description and Operation >> Instrument Panel and Console >> Console - Floor Console - Floor CONSOLE - FLOOR The high series floor console consists of the following components: - armrest - ashcup - bin mat - console finish panel - coin holder - power point - cup holder insert - storage compartment - rear cup holders - rear integrated control panel The base floor console consists of the following components: - arm rest - carry bag - front cup holders - rear cup holders If the vehicle is equipped with manual transmission, there will be a consolette at the base of the gearshift lever. The consolette contains two cupholders, covers the restraint control module (RCM) and is attached by two screws. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6554.html,High Series — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;FLOOR CONSOLE;HIGH SERIES;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1,"High Series — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Body and Frame >> Interior Moulding / Trim >> Console >> Service and Repair >> Floor Console >> High Series High Series FLOOR CONSOLE - HIGH SERIES REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. CAUTION: To prevent the front tabs from breaking apply slight inward pressure when lifting upward, to release the tabs on the console tray. Remove the floor console tray. - Lift upward at the rear first. 3. Disconnect the floor console electrical connectors. 4. Remove the floor console front bolts. 5. Remove the floor console center bolts. 6. NOTE: The console must be moved rearward to disengage the rear mounting bracket. Remove the floor console. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
