6799.html,Customer Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Customer Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service Precautions >> Customer Safety Information Customer Safety Information WARNING: After any vehicle collision, the safety belt system at all outboard seating positions (except driver, which has no ""automatic locking retractor"" feature) must be checked by a qualified technician to verify that the ""automatic locking retractor"" feature for child seats is still functioning correctly, in addition to other checks for proper safety belt system function. A Belt and retractor assembly must be replaced if the safety belt assembly's ""automatic locking retractor"" feature or any other safety belt function is not operating properly when checked according to the procedures. Failure to install the Belt and Retractor assembly could increase the risk of injury in collisions. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6800.html,Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service Precautions >> Technician Safety Information Technician Safety Information WARNING: - The safety belt pretensioner is a pyrotechnic device. Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag equipped vehicle and when handling a safety belt buckle pretensioner or safety belt retractor pretensioner. Never probe a pretensioner electrical connector. Doing so could result in pretensioner or air bag deployment and could result in personal injury. - To reduce the risk of personal injury, do not use any memory saver devices. - All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters, child safety seat tether attachments if equipped, and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. New belt assemblies should be installed unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate correctly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and installed new if either damage or incorrect operation is noted. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6801.html,Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Vehicle Damage Warnings — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service Precautions >> Vehicle Damage Warnings Vehicle Damage Warnings CAUTION: Use care when separating the seat backrest trim cover from the hook-and-loop strip, or the hook-and-loop strip can be torn from the seat backrest foam. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6802.html,Seat Belt Retractor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Interior,0,"tightening the webbing around the occupant. For diagnostic information, refer to Air Bag Systems . For safety belt pretensioner disposal information, refer to Air Bag",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DUAL LOCKING MODE;ENERGY;LEMON;MANAGEMENT;NOTE;PRETENSIONER;RETRACTOR;RETRACTOR AND;RETRACTORS;SAFETY BELT;WARNING,"Seat Belt Retractor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Description and Operation Seat Belt Retractor: Description and Operation SAFETY BELT RETRACTOR AND PRETENSIONER All vehicles have a retractor pretensioner system for the front outboard occupants. This works in conjunction with the front air bag system mounted in the steering wheel and instrument panel. If the vehicle is involved in a collision that results in deployment of the front air bags and safety belt pretensioners, a new driver and front passenger seat belt system (including safety belt retractor and pretensioners, safety belt buckles and height adjusters), must be installed. When the air bag system is deployed, the pretensioner in the retractor deploys, causing the retractor spool to rotate. The rotating spool action removes excess webbing from the safety belt assembly, tightening the webbing around the occupant. For diagnostic information, refer to Air Bag Systems . For safety belt pretensioner disposal information, refer to Air Bag Systems . DUAL LOCKING MODE RETRACTORS WARNING: After any vehicle collision, the safety belt system at all outboard seating positions (except driver, which has no ""automatic locking retractor"" feature) must be checked by a qualified technician to verify that the ""automatic locking retractor"" feature for child seats is still functioning correctly, in addition to other checks for proper safety belt system function. A Belt and retractor assembly must be replaced if the safety belt assembly's ""automatic locking retractor"" feature or any other safety belt function is not operating properly when checked according to the procedures. Failure to install the Belt and Retractor assembly could increase the risk of injury in collisions. NOTE: When installing a dual locking mode retractor, the retractor should be checked to make sure it is not in the automatic locking retractor (ALR) mode after installation in the stowed position. All outboard continuous-loop, three-point retractor systems, except the driver position, are equipped with the dual locking mode system. The emergency locking retractor (ELR) mode will allow the occupant freedom of movement, locking tight only on hard braking, hard cornering, or an impact of approximately 8 km/h (5 mph) . The ELR mode helps to reduce the forward movement of the driver and passengers. The ELR mode is continuously in operation at all seating positions. The ALR portion of this system does not allow the occupant freedom of movement. The ALR mode is used when locking a child seat in an outboard seating position or when a tight belt fit is desired. The ALR mode is disengaged when the webbing is free to move in or out of the retractor. The ALR mode is automatically engaged when the webbing is fully extracted from the retractor and then allowed to retract. As the webbing is retracted back onto the spool, an audible clicking sound is made, indicating that the retractor is in ALR mode. The ALR mode is automatically disengaged when most of the webbing is retracted back onto the spool. The automatic locking mode must be used when installing a child safety seat in the front or rear passenger seating positions where dual locking mode retractors are provided. ENERGY MANAGEMENT RETRACTOR This vehicle has a safety belt system with an energy management feature at the front seating positions to help further reduce the risk of injury in the event of a head-on collision. The energy management retractor feature is designed to pay out webbing in a controlled manner. This feature is designed to help reduce the belt force acting on an occupant's chest. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6803.html,Rear Safety Belt Retractor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,2,"tighten nuts and bolts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 4. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · Abo",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSTALLATION 3;LEMON;NOTE;REAR SAFETY BELT;REMOVAL;RETRACTOR;SPECIAL TOOL;WARNING,"Rear Safety Belt Retractor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service and Repair >> Rear Safety Belt Retractor Rear Safety Belt Retractor REAR SAFETY BELT RETRACTOR Seat Belt Bolt Bit: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL WARNING: All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters, child safety seat tether attachments if equipped, and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. New belt assemblies should be installed unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate correctly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and installed new if either damage or incorrect operation is noted. NOTE: The driver side is shown, the passenger side is similar. 1. Remove the C-pillar trim panel. 2. Remove the bolt and the safety belt retractor. INSTALLATION 3. NOTE: - Make sure the safety belt webbing is not twisted prior to installation. - Make sure to tighten nuts and bolts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 4. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6804.html,Rear Center Safety Belt Retractor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,15,"tighten all nuts and bolts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet ·",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REAR CENTER;REMOVAL;RETRACTOR;SAFETY BELT;SPECIAL TOOL;WARNING,"Rear Center Safety Belt Retractor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service and Repair >> Rear Center Safety Belt Retractor Rear Center Safety Belt Retractor REAR CENTER SAFETY BELT RETRACTOR Seat Belt Bolt Bit: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL WARNING: All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters (if so equipped) child safety seat tether attachments and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. All belt assemblies should be installed unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate properly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and installed if either damage or improper operation is noted. 1. Remove the second row 60 percent seat. 2. Separate the J-clips at the bottom of the seat backrest trim cover. 3. Remove the staples and release the trim cover. 4. Remove the safety belt bezel. 5. Remove the latch bezel. 6. Pressing the head restraint release, remove the head restraint. 7. Release the hook-and-loop strip at the side of the seat. 8. CAUTION: Use care when separating the seat backrest trim cover from the hook-and-loop strip, or the hook-and-loop strip can be torn from the seat backrest foam. Separate the hook-and-loop strips and invert the trim cover. 9. Remove the screws and the backrest panel. 10. Squeeze the bottom of the head restraint guide together and pull it out. 11. Remove the backrest foam pad. 12. Remove the three screws (one shown), route the safety belt through and remove the safety belt retractor cover. 13. Remove the bolts and the safety belt guide. 14. Remove the safety belt sleeve screw. 15. Remove the two pin type retainers (one shown) and separate the safety belt sleeve. 16. Remove the bolt and the safety belt retractor. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: - Make sure the safety belt webbing is not twisted prior to installation. - Make sure to tighten all nuts and bolts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6805.html,Safety Belt Retractor and Pretensioner — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring;Interior,14,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;PRETENSIONER;REMOVAL;RETRACTOR AND;SAFETY BELT;SPECIAL TOOL;WARNING,"Safety Belt Retractor and Pretensioner — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Retractor >> Service and Repair >> Safety Belt Retractor and Pretensioner Safety Belt Retractor and Pretensioner SAFETY BELT RETRACTOR AND PRETENSIONER Seat Belt Bolt Bit: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL WARNING: - The safety belt pretensioner is a pyrotechnic device. Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag equipped vehicle and when handling a safety belt buckle pretensioner or safety belt retractor pretensioner. Never probe a pretensioner electrical connector. Doing so could result in pretensioner or air bag deployment and could result in personal injury. - To reduce the risk of personal injury, do not use any memory saver devices. NOTE: - The air bag warning lamp illuminates when the RCM fuse is removed and the ignition switch is ON. This is normal operation and does not indicate a supplemental restraint system (SRS) fault. - The SRS must be fully operational and free of faults before releasing the vehicle to the customer. - The driver side is shown, the passenger side is similar. 1. Depower the SRS. 2. Remove the driver side lower B-pillar trim panel. 1 Remove the rear door scuff plate. 2 Separate the front door scuff plate at the B-pillar trim panel. 3 Pull out where the B-pillar trim panel meets the B-pillar weatherstripping and remove the B-pillar trim panel. 3. NOTE: If the safety belt guide cover is damaged or if it does not remain closed, install a new cover. From behind the front safety belt guide cover, release the retaining tabs and open the cover. 4. Remove the nut and safety belt guide. 5. Remove the screw and the secondary safety belt guide. - Slide the secondary guide forward to remove. 6. Position the mat back, remove the bolt and the front row safety belt anchor. 7. Disconnect the driver side safety belt retractor pretensioner electrical connector. 8. Remove the safety belt retractor and pretensioner. 1 Remove the bolt. 2 Remove the bolt. 3 Remove the safety belt retractor and pretensioner. INSTALLATION 1. Install the safety belt retractor and pretensioner. 1 Position the safety belt retractor and pretensioner so the tabs align to the sheet metal holes. 2 Install the bolt. 3 Install the bolt. 2. Connect the driver side safety belt retractor pretensioner electrical connector. 3. NOTE: Make sure the safety belt webbing is not twisted prior to installation. Position the secondary safety belt guide and install the screw. 4. NOTE: - Make sure the safety belt webbing is not twisted prior to installation. - Inspect the shoulder safety belt guide cover for damage. If the shoulder safety belt guide cover is damaged or if it does not remain closed, install a new shoulder safety belt guide cover. Install the safety belt guide. 1 Position the safety belt guide. 2 Install the safety belt guide nut. 3 Close the safety belt guide cover. 5. NOTE: Make sure the safety belt webbing is not twisted prior to installation. Position the front row safety belt anchor, install the bolt and reposition the mat. 6. Install the driver side lower B-pillar trim panel. 1 Position the B-pillar trim panel to the B-pillar and install it around the weather stripping. 2 Install the rear door scuff plate. 3 Reposition the front door scuff plate at the B-pillar trim panel. 7. Repower the SRS. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
