6810.html,Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Interior,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BELT MINDER;CHIME;INDICATOR AND;LEMON;SAFETY BELT;WARNING,"Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Reminder Lamp >> Description and Operation Seat Belt Reminder Lamp: Description and Operation SAFETY BELT WARNING INDICATOR AND CHIME The safety belt warning indicator illuminates and a chime sounds to remind the occupants to fasten their safety belts. The conditions of operation for the safety belt waring indicator and chime are as follows: - If the driver safety belt is not buckled before the ignition switch is turned to RUN, the safety belt warning indicator illuminates for 1-2 minutes and the warning chime sounds for 4-8 seconds . - If the driver safety belt is buckled while the warning indicator is illuminated and the reminder chime is sounding, the safety belt warning indicator and reminder chime will turn off. - If the driver safety belt is buckled before the ignition switch is turned to the ON position, the safety belt warning indicator and reminder chime will remain off. BELT MINDER The Belt Minder feature is a supplemental warning to the safety belt warning function. This feature provides an additional reminder to the driver and/or passenger that the safety belt is unbuckled by intermittently sounding a chime and illuminating the safety belt warning lamp in the instrument cluster. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
