6823.html,Seat Belt Buckle: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Seat Belt Buckle: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Buckle >> Service Precautions Seat Belt Buckle: Service Precautions WARNING: All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters (if so equipped), child safety seat tether attachments, and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. All belt assemblies should be installed unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate properly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and installed if either damage or improper operation is noted. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6824.html,Front Safety Belt Buckle — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,3,"tighten all retainers to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · Abou",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BUCKLE;FRONT SAFETY BELT;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;SPECIAL TOOL;WARNING,"Front Safety Belt Buckle — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Buckle >> Service and Repair >> Front Safety Belt Buckle Front Safety Belt Buckle FRONT SAFETY BELT BUCKLE Seat Belt Bolt Bit: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL WARNING: All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters (if so equipped), child safety seat tether attachments, and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. All belt assemblies should be replaced unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate properly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and replaced if either damage or improper operation is noted. NOTE: Driver side is shown, passenger side is similar. 1. Remove the front driver or passenger seat from the vehicle. 2. Remove the safety belt buckle support assembly. 1 Remove the nut and bolt. 2 Remove the safety belt buckle support assembly. 3. NOTE: Clamp the safety belt buckle support assembly collar in a vise along the break line only. Remove the safety belt buckle. 1 Clamp the safety belt buckle support assembly in a suitable vise. 2 Using the special tool, remove the safety belt buckle bolt. 3 Remove the safety belt buckle. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: Make sure to tighten all retainers to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6825.html,Center and LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,1,"tighten all retainers to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · Abou",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BUCKLE;CENTER AND;INSTALLATION 1;LATCH;LEMON;LH REAR;LH REMOVAL;NOTE;SAFETY BELT;WARNING,"Center and LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Systems >> Seat Belt Buckle >> Service and Repair >> Rear Safety Belt Buckle >> Center and LH Center and LH REAR SAFETY BELT BUCKLE - CENTER AND LH REMOVAL WARNING: All safety belt assemblies including retractors, buckles, front seat belt buckle support assemblies (slide bar), shoulder belt height adjusters (if so equipped), child safety seat tether attachments, and attaching hardware should be inspected after any collision. All belt assemblies should be installed unless a qualified technician finds the assemblies show no damage and operate properly. Belt assemblies not in use during a collision should also be inspected and installed if either damage or improper operation is noted. 1. Remove the second row 60 percent and 40 percent rear seats. 2. Remove the safety belt buckle and the lower anchors and tethers for children (LATCH) assembly. 1 Remove the nut. 2 Remove the nuts. 3 Remove the safety belt buckle and LATCH assembly. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: Make sure to tighten all retainers to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Check the active restraint system for correct operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
