6911.html,Air Bag Resistor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BRIDGE;CANOPY;LEMON;RESISTOR NOTE;SAFETY,"Air Bag Resistor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Air Bag Resistor >> Description and Operation Air Bag Resistor: Description and Operation SAFETY CANOPY BRIDGE RESISTOR NOTE: - The vehicles may be equipped with optional safety canopy modules. Vehicles not equipped with safety canopy modules will have a safety canopy bridge resistor present at the driver safety canopy module connector with a cap at the passenger safety canopy module connector (no connect, circuits are open). - Do not deactivate the safety canopy module circuit by removing the bridge resistor from the electrical connector. If the safety canopy bridge resistor is removed. an open circuit fault will be generated by the restraints control module (RCM). If a restraint system diagnostic tool is installed at the safety canopy electrical connector. a low-resistance fault will be generated. The safety canopy bridge resistor: - is equipped on vehicles without safety canopy modules. - must not be removed during deactivation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6912.html,Air Bag Resistor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BRIDGE;CANOPY;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;RESISTOR;SAFETY;WARNING,"Air Bag Resistor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Air Bag Resistor >> Service and Repair Air Bag Resistor: Service and Repair SAFETY CANOPY BRIDGE RESISTOR REMOVAL WARNING: - Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) vehicle and when handling an air bag module. This will reduce the risk of injury in the event of an accidental deployment. - To reduce the risk of personal injury, do not use any memory saver devices. NOTE: - The air bag warning lamp illuminates when the RCM fuse is removed and the ignition switch is ON. This is normal operation and does not indicate a supplemental restraint system (SRS) fault. - The SRS must be fully operational and free of faults before releasing the vehicle to the customer. - There is only one safety canopy bridge resistor. The bridge resistor can be accessed on the headliner at the LH C-pillar. - Repair is made by installing a new part only. If the new part does not correct the condition, install the original part and carry out the diagnostic procedure again. 1. Depower the SRS. 2. From the back of the safety belt guide cover, release the retainer and open the safety belt guide cover. 3. Remove the bolt and the safety belt guide. 4. Separate the lower C-pillar trim panel at the weatherstrip, separate the weatherstrip at the C-pillar and separate the upper C-pillar trim panel at the pinch weld. 5. With the upper and lower C-pillar trim panels pulled back, disconnect and remove the safety canopy bridge resistor. INSTALLATION 1. Connect and install the safety canopy bridge resistor. 2. Attach the upper C-pillar trim panel, weatherstrip and lower C-pillar trim panel. 3. Align the safety belt guide and install the bolt. 4. NOTE: If the safety belt guide cover is damaged or if it does not remain closed, install a new cover. Close the safety belt guide cover. 5. Repower the SRS scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6913.html,Customer Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Customer Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Air Bag Control Module >> Service Precautions >> Customer Safety Information Customer Safety Information WARNING: - Do not handle, move or change the original horizontal mounting position of the restraints control module (RCM) while the RCM is connected and the ignition switch is ON. Failure to follow these instructions may result in the inadvertent deployment of the safety canopy and risk of personal injury. - The restraints control module (RCM) orientation is critical for correct system operation. If a vehicle equipped with an air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) has been involved in a collision in which the center tunnel area has been damaged, inspect the mounting surface for deformation. If damaged, the RCM must be replaced whether or not the air bags have deployed. In addition, make sure the area of the RCM mounting surface is restored to its original condition. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6914.html,Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,0,tightening torque of the air bag restraint control module (RCM) retaining bolts is critical for correct system operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;WARNING,"Technician Safety Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Restraints and Safety Systems >> Air Bag Systems >> Air Bag Control Module >> Service Precautions >> Technician Safety Information Technician Safety Information WARNING: - Do not handle, move or change the original horizontal mounting position of the restraints control module (RCM) while the RCM is connected and the ignition switch is ON. Failure to follow these instructions may result in the inadvertent deployment of the safety canopy and risk of personal injury. - The restraints control module (RCM) orientation is critical for proper air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) operation. If a vehicle equipped with an SRS system has been involved in a collision in which the center tunnel area has been damaged, inspect the mounting and bracket for deformation. If damaged, the RCM must be replaced whether or not the air bags have deployed. In addition, make sure the area of the RCM mounting is restored to its original condition. - Always wear safety glasses when repairing an air bag supplemental restraint system (SRS) vehicle and when handling an air bag module. This will reduce the risk of injury in the event of an accidental deployment. - To reduce the risk of personal injury, do not use any memory saver devices. - The tightening torque of the air bag restraint control module (RCM) retaining bolts is critical for correct system operation. 