6991.html,Vacuum Reservoir HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring;Interior,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;HVAC;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1;RESERVOIR;VACUUM,"Vacuum Reservoir HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Vacuum Reservoir HVAC >> Service and Repair Vacuum Reservoir HVAC: Service and Repair VACUUM RESERVOIR REMOVAL 1. Prepare the vehicle for vacuum reservoir removal. 1 Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2 Remove the air cleaner assembly. 2. Remove the screws. Position the air cleaner housing mounting bracket out of the way. 3. Raise and support the vehicle. 4. Remove the screws. 5. Lower the vehicle. 6. NOTE: The vacuum hoses to the vacuum reservoir are not interchangeable. Note the location of each vacuum hose to make sure of correct installation. Label and disconnect the vacuum hoses. Remove the vacuum reservoir. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
6992.html,Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;HVAC;LEMON;WARNING,Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service Precautions — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Vacuum Harness HVAC >> Service Precautions Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service Precautions WARNING: Read the warning information on the product label to prevent possible personal injury. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
6993.html,Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Interior,2,,1 inch;25 mm;8 inch;9 mm,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;HVAC;LEMON;MINI-TUBE;REPAIR;SPECIAL TOOL;VACUUM HOSE;WARNING,Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Vacuum Harness HVAC >> Service and Repair Vacuum Harness HVAC: Service and Repair VACUUM HOSE REPAIR - MINI-TUBE Vacuum Pump Kit: SPECIAL TOOL(S) 1. Measure the length of the damaged area of the mini-tube vacuum hose. 2. Cut a piece of standard 1/8 inch inner diameter vacuum hose approximately 25 mm ( 1 inch longer than the damaged area of the mini-tube vacuum hose). 3. Cut off the mini-tube vacuum hose on each side of the damaged area. 4. WARNING: Read the warning information on the product label to prevent possible personal injury. Dip the mini-tube hose ends in commercially available paint thinner containing methyl ethyl ketone (MEK). This solvent will seal the mini-tube in the vacuum hose. 5. Insert the ends of the mini-tube vacuum hose approximately 9 mm (3/8 inch) into the ends of the standard 1/8 inch repair vacuum hose section. 6. Shake the repair joint after assembly to make sure the solvent is dispersed and the vacuum line is not plugged. 7. Test the system for a vacuum leak in the repair area. - Use the Vacuum Pump or equivalent. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
