7032.html,Housing Assembly HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring;Interior,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CHAMBER;HVAC;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;PLENUM;REMOVAL 1,"Housing Assembly HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Housing Assembly HVAC >> Service and Repair Housing Assembly HVAC: Service and Repair PLENUM CHAMBER REMOVAL 1. Prepare the vehicle for plenum chamber removal. 1 Remove the instrument panel. Refer to: Body and Frame, Interior Trim, Dashboard/Instrument Panel, Service and Repair, Removal and Installation, Service and Repair 2 Remove the A/C evaporator housing. 3 Remove the powertrain control module (PCM). 2. Remove the PCM heat sink. 1 Remove the ground strap screw. 2 Remove the PCM heat sink. 3. NOTE: To ease the removal of the plenum chamber, first remove the nut located at the center of the dash panel behind the engine cylinder block. Remove the four nuts and the plenum chamber. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
7034.html,Hose/Line HVAC: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;HVAC;LEMON;NOTE;REFRIGERANT LINES,"Hose/Line HVAC: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Hose/Line HVAC >> Description and Operation Hose/Line HVAC: Description and Operation REFRIGERANT LINES NOTE: Installation of a new suction accumulator is not required when repairing the air conditioning system except when there is physical evidence of system contamination from a failed A/C compressor or damage to the suction accumulator. The condenser to evaporator tube contains high pressure liquid refrigerant upstream of the A/C evaporator core orifice. The A/C manifold and tube is attached to the A/C compressor, is sealed with O-ring seals, and has the following features: - The upstream side contains low pressure refrigerant gas. - The downstream side contains high pressure refrigerant gas and a fitting used to mount a serviceable high-pressure A/C charge port valve. - The downstream side also contains a fitting used to mount the A/C pressure cutoff switch. A long-travel Schrader-type valve stem core is installed in the fitting so that the A/C pressure cutoff switch can be removed without discharging the A/C system. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
7035.html,Hose/Line HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring;Interior,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CONDENSER TO;EVAPORATOR LINE;F7AZ-19589-DA;HVAC;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;WSH-M1C231-B;YN-12-C,"Hose/Line HVAC: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Heating and Air Conditioning >> Hose/Line HVAC >> Service and Repair Hose/Line HVAC: Service and Repair CONDENSER TO EVAPORATOR LINE REMOVAL 1. Prepare the vehicle for condenser to evaporator tube removal. 1 Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2 Recover the refrigerant . 3 Remove the air cleaner assembly. 2. Disconnect the condenser to evaporator tube from the A/C condenser core. Remove and discard the O-ring seal. - During installation, install a new O-ring seal lubricated with PAG Refrigerant Compressor Oil (R-134a Systems) F7AZ-19589-DA (Motorcraft YN-12-C) or equivalent meeting Ford specification WSH-M1C231-B. 3. Disconnect and remove the condenser to evaporator tube. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. 2. Evacuate, leak test, and charge the A/C system. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
