7200.html,Rear — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;19A508-AA;2004;2WD V6-4;ES-3W4W-;ESA-M1C75-B;FEHP;LEMON;SAE 75W-90;SAE 80W-90;WSP-M2C197-A;XY-75W90-QFEHP;XY-80W90-QL,Rear — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Steering and Suspension >> Suspension >> Wheel Bearing >> Specifications >> Rear Rear Lubricate the new rear wheel bearing - Conventional Axle Only Use SAE 80W-90 Premium Rear Axle Lubricant XY-80W90-QL or equivalent meeting Ford specification WSP-M2C197-A. - Traction-Lok Axle Only Use SAE 75W-90 FEHP Fuel Efficient High Performance Synthetic Rear Axle Lubricant XY-75W90-QFEHP or equivalent meeting Ford specification ES-3W4W-19A508-AA Lubricate the lip of the new wheel bearing oil seal - Use Premium Long-Life Grease XG-1-C or equivalent meeting Ford specification ESA-M1C75-B. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
7201.html,Torsion Bar: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension,7,Tighten the special tool until the torsion bar adjuster lifts off the adjustment bolt. 5. CAUTION: The torsion bar adjustment bolt is coated with dry adhesive. A new b,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Torsion Bar: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Steering and Suspension >> Suspension >> Torsion Bar >> Service and Repair Torsion Bar: Service and Repair Special Tool(s) Removal and Installation 1. Raise and support the vehicle. 2. Remove the bolts and the torsion bar cover plate. 3. NOTE: Before relieving the torsion bar tension, measure and record the measurement of the torsion bar adjustment bolt. This measurement will be used as the preset depth for the new torsion bar adjustment bolt during installation. Make preliminary adjustment references. ^ Measure and record the length where indicated. 4. Relieve the torsion bar tension. 1 Position the special tool and adapters. 2 Tighten the special tool until the torsion bar adjuster lifts off the adjustment bolt. 5. CAUTION: The torsion bar adjustment bolt is coated with dry adhesive. A new bolt must be installed if it is backed off or removed. Failure to do so can cause the adjustment bolt to loosen during operation and cause a loss of vehicle alignment. Remove the torsion bar adjustment bolt and nut. 6. Loosen the special tool until the tension is removed from the torsion bar . 7. Remove the torsion bar . 1 Mark the torsion bar and the adjuster for reference during installation. 2 Remove the torsion bar insulator. 3 Grasp the torsion bar , and pull it free from the lower arm. 8. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
