7216.html,Spindle: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Wiring,7,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON,"Spindle: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Steering and Suspension >> Suspension >> Spindle >> Service and Repair Spindle: Service and Repair Wheel Spindle Special Tool(s): Special Tool(s) Removal and Installation 1. Remove the brake disc and hub. 2. Remove the front brake anti-lock sensor. ^ Remove the anti-lock sensor electrical wire from the clamp. ^ Remove the bolt and position the sensor aside. 3. Remove the cotter pin and nut. 4. Using the special tool, separate the tie-rod end from the spindle . 5. Use a suitable jack stand to support the lower arm. 6. CAUTION: To avoid possible damage to the front wheel spindle , secure the spindle to keep it from tilting before removing the pinch bolt and nut. Remove the nut and pinch bolt. 7. Remove the cotter pin and nut. 8. Using the special tool separate the ball joint and remove the spindle . 9. To install, reverse the removal procedure. ^ Install the cotter pin into the lower ball joint from outboard to inboard with the fingers bent together at a right angle. Failure to do so can cause damage to the wheel and tire assembly. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
