7527.html,Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CYLINDER;F85Z-11582-AA;IGNITION LOCK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NON FUNCTIONAL;NOTE;REMOVAL 1;WARNING,"Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Starting and Charging >> Starting System >> Ignition Lock >> Service and Repair >> Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional IGNITION LOCK CYLINDER - NON FUNCTIONAL REMOVAL 1. WARNING: To reduce the risk of serious personal injury, read and follow all warnings, notes and instructions in the steering wheel removal and installation procedure. NOTE: Make sure the front wheels are in the straight-ahead position. Remove the steering wheel assembly. 2. Twist off the cap from the ignition switch cylinder. 3. NOTE: The lock cylinder is repaired by discarding the inoperative lock cylinder and building a new lock cylinder using the appropriate lock repair package (F85Z-11582-AA). The lock repair package includes a detailed instruction sheet to build the new lock cylinder to the current key code of the vehicle. Remove the ignition switch lock cylinder . - Use a 1/8-inch diameter drill bit to drill out the lock cylinder retaining pin. - Use a 3/8-inch drill bit to drill down the middle of the ignition lock key slot until the ignition switch lock cylinder breaks loose. - Remove and discard the ignition switch lock cylinder and clean the drill shavings from the steering column. 4. Remove the bearing retainer. 5. Remove the bearing and gear. - Thoroughly clean all drill shavings from the steering column and inspect it for damage. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Install a new ignition switch lock cylinder . - Verify ignition switch lock cylinder operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
