7617.html,Compensator Port Check — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,Compensator Port Check — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Brakes and Traction Control >> Hydraulic System >> Brake Master Cylinder >> Testing and Inspection >> Compensator Port Check Compensator Port Check The purpose of the compensator ports in the brake master cylinder is to supply any additional brake fluid required by the system due to brake pad wear and to allow brake fluid returning from the brake lines to the brake master cylinder to enter the brake master cylinder reservoir. The returning brake fluid will cause a slight turbulence in the brake master cylinder reservoir. Turbulence seen in the brake master cylinder reservoir upon release of the brake pedal is normal and shows that the compensating ports are not plugged. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
7618.html,Brake Master Cylinder: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Wiring,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;WARNING,"Brake Master Cylinder: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Brakes and Traction Control >> Hydraulic System >> Brake Master Cylinder >> Service and Repair Brake Master Cylinder: Service and Repair Master Cylinder Removal and Installation WARNING: Use of any other brake fluid than approved DOT 3 will cause permanent damage to brake components and will render the brakes inoperative. Brake fluid contains polyglycol ethers and polyglycols. Avoid contact with eyes. Wash hands thoroughly after handling. If brake fluid contacts eyes, flush eyes with running water for 15 minutes. Get medical attention if irritation persists. If taken internally, drink water and induce vomiting. Get medical attention immediately. CAUTION: Brake fluid is harmful to painted or plastic surfaces. If brake fluid is spilled onto a painted or plastic surface, immediately wash it with water. 1. On cruise control equipped vehicles, disconnect the brake pressure switch. 2. Disconnect the brake fluid level warning switch. 3. Disconnect the two brake lines, and plug the lines and the brake master cylinder ports. 4. Remove the wiring retainer clip from the master cylinder. 5. Remove the nuts and the brake master cylinder . 6. To install, reverse the removal procedure. ^ Bleed the brake master cylinder before installation. ^ Bleed the brake system. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
