7710.html,Output Shaft Speed (OSS) Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Transmission;Wiring,4,Tighten OSS sensor screw. 2. Connect OSS sensor electrical connector. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NEUTRAL,"Output Shaft Speed (OSS) Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Transmission Control Systems >> Sensors and Switches - Transmission and Drivetrain >> Sensors and Switches - A/T >> Transmission Speed Sensor >> Service and Repair >> Output Shaft Speed (OSS) Sensor Output Shaft Speed (OSS) Sensor Output Shaft Speed (OSS) Sensor Removal 1. With the vehicle in NEUTRAL, position it on a hoist. 2. Disconnect output shaft speed (OSS) sensor electrical connector. 3. Remove OSS sensor. 1. Remove the OSS sensor screw. 2. Remove the OSS sensor from the transmission. ^ Inspect the OSS sensor O-ring for damage. If damaged, install a new O-ring. Installation 1. Inspect and lubricate O-ring with petroleum jelly. 1. Install the OSS sensor into the transmission. 2. Tighten OSS sensor screw. 2. Connect OSS sensor electrical connector. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
