7964.html,A/T - No 3rd Gear/TCIL Flashing/DTC P0733 — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission,4,,90 degree,04B22;05 NO 3RD;05-15-3;051503A 2004;0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2004 FORD;2004-2005;2005;2WD V6-4;3RD GEAR;5R44E;5R5551E;7000A11;7000A43;7000F;7191A;7191A5;7191AXQ;7A098;7A100;7B155;ACTION;ADDRESSED BY;ALSO;AND FLASHING TCIL;ASSEMBLY;ATTEMPTING TO;BASED ON;BE AWARE THE;CODE 7G383 42;CODING;CONDITION;CONDITION BASIC;CONTAMINATION IS;COOLER;COOLER LINES;DEALER;DESCRIPTION TIME;DO NOT;DTC P0733;DTC P0733 A;DTC P0733 TSB;FEATURES TWO;FILTER;FLUID PAN;FLUSH THE;GEAR;GREATER THAN,"A/T - No 3rd Gear/TCIL Flashing/DTC P0733 — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Transmission and Drivetrain >> Automatic Transmission/Transaxle >> Actuators and Solenoids - A/T >> Pressure Regulating Solenoid >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Customer Interest >> A/T - No 3rd Gear/TCIL Flashing/DTC P0733 A/T - No 3rd Gear/TCIL Flashing/DTC P0733 TSB 05-15-3 08/08/05 NO 3RD GEAR, DTC P0733 (3RD GEAR INCORRECT RATIO) AND FLASHING TCIL - VEHICLES BUILT PRIOR TO 9/23/2004 FORD: 2004-2005 Explorer Sport Trac, Ranger This article supersedes TSB 05-06-11 to update the Service Procedure. ISSUE Some 2004-2005 Ranger and Explorer Sport Trac vehicles built prior to 09/23/2004 may exhibit symptoms of no 3rd gear along with a diagnostic trouble code (DTC) P0733 (3rd Gear Ratio Incorrect), and a flashing transmission control indicator lamp (ICIL). This may be due to improper pressure control. In addition, other shift concerns and transmission DTCs may be present. ACTION It may be necessary to replace the electronic pressure control solenoid (EPC). Refer to the following Service Procedure. SERVICE PROCEDURE NOTE CONTAMINATION IS NOT THE CAUSE OF THE CONDITION ADDRESSED BY THIS TSB. IT IS NOT NECESSARY TO FLUSH THE TRANSMISSION COOLER/COOLER LINES OR REPLACE THE FLUID PAN FILTER (7A098). ALSO, DO NOT REPROGRAM THE PCM, REPLACE THE MAIN CONTROL ASSEMBLY (7A100) OR INSTALL AN IN-LINE SERVICE FILTER (7B155). 1. Verify whether Customer Satisfaction Program 04B22 has already been performed. If it has not, add 5R5551E & 5R44E Transmission Additive as directed, close out 04B22 and proceed to Step 2. If 04B22 has been performed, DO NOT install additional Transmission Additive, proceed directly to Step 2. Installing Transmission Additive will prevent the symptom on solenoids that do not yet exhibit the condition but will not resolve the condition if it already exists. 2. Remove pressure tap plug at EPC port (Figure 1). 3. Install a pressure gauge into the EPC port to check EPC pressure, using a nipple and a 90 degree fitting (Figure 2). NOTE WHEN ATTEMPTING TO VERIFY A SHIFT IS OCCURRING INTO 3RD GEAR, BE AWARE THE RANGER FEATURES TWO (2) SHIFT STRATEGIES BASED ON THROTTLE POSITION. AT 1/3 THROTTLE OR LESS, THE TRANSMISSION SHIFT SEQUENCE WILL BE 1-3-4-5. WHEN THROTTLE POSITION IS GREATER THAN 1/3, THE SHIFT SEQUENCE WILL BE 1-2-3-4-5. 4. Drive the vehicle at normal operating temperature while monitoring the EPC pressure during shifts. Attempt to perform five (5) upshifts into 3rd gear and five (5) downshifts from 3rd gear. If EPC pressure becomes erratic when the shifting concern is present replace the EPC solenoid . Refer to the Workshop Manual. 5. Adjust the transmission fluid to the proper level using only packaged/bottled (not bulk) reformulated MERCON(R) V. 6. Clear DTCs, verity that KAM has been cleared. WARRANTY STATUS: Eligible Under Provisions Of New Vehicle Limited Warranty Coverage And Emissions Warranty Coverage OPERATION DESCRIPTION TIME 051503A 2004-2005 Ranger/Explorer 1.8 Hrs. Sport Trac: Replace The EPC Solenoid (Includes Time To Check DTCs, Install Pressure Gauge, Road Test, Reset Fluid Level, Clear Codes And KAM (Do Not Use With 7000F, 7000A11, 7000A43, 7191A, 7191AXQ, 7191A5) DEALER CODING CONDITION BASIC PART NO. CODE 7G383 42 Disclaimer scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
