8088.html,Spark Plug: Application and ID — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;AGSF22PP;LEMON,Spark Plug: Application and ID — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Spark Plug >> Application and ID Spark Plug: Application and ID Spark plug type AGSF22PP scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
8089.html,Spark Plug: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,6,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1;SPARK PLUG;SPECIAL TOOL,"Spark Plug: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Spark Plug >> Service and Repair Spark Plug: Service and Repair SPARK PLUG Spark Plug Wire Remover: SPECIAL TOOL(S) REMOVAL 1. Remove the right front tire and wheel. 2. Remove the right front fenderwell splash shield. 3. CAUTION: - Spark plug wires must be connected correctly. Mark the spark plug wires before removing them. - It is important to twist the spark plug wire boots while pulling upward to avoid possible damage to the spark plug wire. With a twisting motion, use the special tool to pull the spark plug wires from the right side of the engine. 4. NOTE: - Use compressed air to remove any foreign material in the spark plug well before removing the spark plugs. - If an original spark plug is reused, make sure it is installed in the same cylinder it was taken from. New spark plugs can be used in any cylinder. Remove the RH spark plugs . 5. Lower the vehicle. 6. CAUTION: - Spark plug wires must be connected correctly. Mark the spark plug wires before removing them. - It is important to twist the spark plug wire boots while pulling upward to avoid possible damage to the spark plug wire. With a twisting motion, use the special tool to pull the spark plug wires from the left side of the engine. 7. NOTE: - Use compressed air to remove any foreign material in the spark plug well before removing the spark plugs. - If an original spark plug is reused, make sure it is installed in the same cylinder it was taken from. New spark plugs can be used in any cylinder. Remove the LH spark plugs . 8. Inspect the spark plugs . 9. Use a suitable spark plug gap tool to check and adjust the spark plug gap. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Apply silicone dielectric compound to the inside of the spark plug wire boots. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
