8104.html,Crankshaft Position Sensor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CRANKSHAFT;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NEUTRAL;NOTE;POSITION;REMOVAL 1;SENSOR,"Crankshaft Position Sensor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Sensors and Switches - Ignition System >> Crankshaft Position Sensor >> Service and Repair Crankshaft Position Sensor: Service and Repair CRANKSHAFT POSITION (CKP) SENSOR REMOVAL 1. With the vehicle in NEUTRAL, position it on a hoist. 2. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 3. Remove the crankshaft position (CKP) sensor. 1 Disconnect the electrical connector. 2 Remove the bolt. 3 Remove the sensor. INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: - The new CKP sensor needs to be touching the damper. The new sensor has wear tabs that will wear off after several engine revolutions. - Be sure the sensor wiring is routed away from the battery cable. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
