8114.html,Coil On Plug (COP) — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;COIL ON PLUG;FMEM;LEMON,"Coil On Plug (COP) — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Ignition Coil >> Description and Operation >> Coil On Plug (COP) Coil On Plug (COP) COIL ON PLUG Coil On Plug: The coil on plug (COP) (Figure 65) ignition operates similar to standard coil pack ignition except each plug has one coil per plug. COP has three different modes of operation: engine crank, engine running, and CMP Failure Mode Effects Management (FMEM). scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8115.html,Coil Pack — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,4,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;COIL PACK;LEMON,"Coil Pack — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Ignition Coil >> Description and Operation >> Coil Pack Coil Pack COIL PACK Horizontal Connector Six Tower Coil Pack: Series 5 Six Tower Coil Pack: Four-Tower Coil Packs: Series 5 Four Tower Coil Pack: Coil packs come in four tower, Series 5 four tower, six-tower horizontal connector and Series 5 Six tower models. Two adjacent coil towers share a common coil and are called a matched pair. For six-tower coil pack (six cylinder) applications the matched pairs are 1 and 5, 2 and 6, and 3 and 4 (Figure 61) and (Figure 62). For four-tower coil pack (four cylinder) applications the matched pairs are 1 and 4, and 2 and 3 (Figure 63) and (Figure 64). When the coil is fired by the PCM, spark is delivered through the matched pair towers to their respective spark plugs . The spark plugs are fired simultaneously and are paired so that as one fires on the compression stroke, the other spark plug fires on the exhaust stroke. The next time the coil is fired the situation is reversed. The next pair of spark plugs fire according to the engine firing order . scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8116.html,Ignition Coil: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;IGNITION COIL;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL 1,"Ignition Coil: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Ignition System >> Ignition Coil >> Service and Repair Ignition Coil: Service and Repair IGNITION COIL REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 2. Disconnect the ignition coil electrical connector. 3. CAUTION: It is important to twist the spark plug wire boots while pulling upward to avoid possible damage to the spark plug wire. NOTE: Spark plug wires must be connected to the correct ignition coil terminal. Mark spark plug wire locations before removing them. Squeeze the locking tabs and twist while pulling upward to disconnect the six spark plug wires. 4. Remove the bolts and the ignition coil . INSTALLATION 1. NOTE: Apply silicone dielectric compound to the inside of the spark plug wire coil boots. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
