8149.html,Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCS;CUT-OFF;EATC;LEMON;THROTTLE A;WIDE OPEN,"Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Throttle Full Open Switch >> Description and Operation Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation WIDE OPEN THROTTLE A/C CUT-OFF (WAC) The wide open throttle A/C cutoff relay (may be referred to as the A/C clutch relay) is wired normally open (normally closed for Aviator). There is no direct electrical connection between the A/C switch or EATC Module and the A/C clutch. The PCM will receive a signal indicating that A/C is requested (for some applications, this message is sent through the BUS + and BUS - circuits). When A/C is requested, the PCM will check other A/C related inputs that are available (such as ACP (SW), ACCS). If these inputs indicate A/C operation is OK, and the engine conditions are OK (such as coolant temperature, engine rpm, throttle position), the PCM will ground the WAC output (unground for Aviator), closing the relay contacts and sending voltage to the A/C clutch. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8150.html,Throttle Cable/Linkage: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCELERATION;CONTROL;LEMON,"Throttle Cable/Linkage: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Throttle Cable/Linkage >> Description and Operation Throttle Cable/Linkage: Description and Operation ACCELERATION CONTROL The throttle is controlled by an accelerator cable attached to the accelerator pedal and shaft assembly. The accelerator pedal and shaft should travel smoothly from the idle position to the wide open throttle position. Hesitation or binding should not be experienced at any portion of the accelerator pedal and shaft travel. Surrounding components such as wiring, hoses, sound insulator and floor carpet must not contact the sliding inner member of the accelerator cable or interfere with the accelerator pedal and shaft. The acceleration control consists of an accelerator pedal and cable. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8151.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;VERIFICATION NOTE,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Throttle Cable/Linkage >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION NOTE: Care should be exercised when carrying out repair on or around the accelerator pedal linkage and controls. 1. Inspect the accelerator pedal and shaft and attaching linkage for damage or distortion which would bind or limit accelerator travel. 2. Inspect the accelerator cable for kinks or fraying which may cause binding. 3. Inspect the engine idle speed adjustment to make sure of the correct idle speed specification after any accelerator linkage adjustment or repair. 4. Inspect throttle body for excessive wear or damage. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
