8196.html,Fuel Tank Mounting Straps: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FUEL TANK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1;STRAPS;SUPPORT,"Fuel Tank Mounting Straps: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Tank >> Fuel Tank Mounting Straps >> Service and Repair Fuel Tank Mounting Straps: Service and Repair FUEL TANK SUPPORT STRAPS REMOVAL 1. Raise and support the vehicle. 2. If equipped, remove the fuel tank skid plate rear retaining bolts. 3. If equipped, remove the fuel tank skid plate front retaining bolts and the skid plate. 4. Use a suitable jack to support the fuel tank . 5. Remove the bolt and the rear fuel tank support strap. 6. Remove the bolt and the front fuel tank support strap. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8197.html,Fuel Gauge Sender: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,4,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FUEL PUMP;LEMON;MODULE,"Fuel Gauge Sender: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Tank >> Fuel Gauge Sender >> Description and Operation Fuel Gauge Sender: Description and Operation FUEL PUMP MODULE Fuel Pump Module: Fuel Pump Module (For Returnable Fuel Systems): Mechanical Returnless Fuel Pump Module (FPM): Electronic Returnless Fuel Pump Module (FPM): The fuel pump (FP) module (Figure 71),(Figure 72) and(Figure 73) is a device that contains the fuel pump and sender assembly. The fuel pump is located inside the FP module reservoir and supplies fuel through the FP module manifold to the engine and FP module jet pump. The jet pump continuously refills the reservoir with fuel, and a check valve located in the manifold outlet maintains system pressure when the fuel pump is not energized. A flapper valve located in the bottom of the reservoir allows fuel to enter the reservoir and prime the fuel pump during the initial fill. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8198.html,Fuel Filler Hose: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FILLER PIPE;FUEL TANK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NOTE;REMOVAL;WARNING,"Fuel Filler Hose: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Tank >> Fuel Filler Hose >> Service and Repair Fuel Filler Hose: Service and Repair FUEL TANK FILLER PIPE REMOVAL WARNING: Do not smoke, carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related component. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and may be ignited, resulting in possible personal injury. 1. NOTE: Fuel tank filler pipe may contain fuel. Remove the fuel tank filler cap. 2. Remove the screws. 3. Disconnect the fuel vapor vent tube from the inner fenderwell. 4. Working through the fenderwell, remove the tie strap and disconnect the fuel vapor hose. 5. Remove the ground strap and disconnect the fuel vapor tube. 6. Remove the fuel filler pipe through the wheelwell. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8199.html,Fuel Supply Line: Tools and Equipment — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;800-525-2943;8013;8100;8107;8110;LEMON,"Fuel Supply Line: Tools and Equipment — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Supply Line >> Tools and Equipment Fuel Supply Line: Tools and Equipment 3/8"" Fuel Line Remover AST tool# 8013 Used for removing 3/8"" fuel lines and feed lines from the fuel pump -sending unit. - For R and R of Fuel and Feed Lines - Quick line removal - Gold-Anodized Aluminum Construction - See Application Chart - Included in the 8100, 8107 and #8110 Line Disconnect Sets. Contact AST for pricing. Assenmacher Specialty Tools 1-800-525-2943 This Tool is also available in the following kits: 8110 - 10-Pc. Line Disconnect Set 8107 - 7-Piece Line Disconnect Set scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8200.html,Fuel Shut-off Solenoid: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;LOW PRESSURE;OFF VALVE;SOLENOID SHUT,Fuel Shut-off Solenoid: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Shut-off Solenoid >> Description and Operation Fuel Shut-off Solenoid: Description and Operation LOW PRESSURE SOLENOID SHUT-OFF VALVE Low pressure solenoid shut-off valve which isolates the fuel rail from the upstream fuel system when the engine is OFF. This minimizes the amount of fuel available to flow through the fuel injectors when the engine is off or leak from a damaged fuel rail during and after a crash. The valve is controlled by the PCM fuel shut-off valve circuit and contains an inertia switch. The valve is only on for one second after a key-on or whenever CKP signals are being received by the PCM. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
8201.html,Fuel Receptacle (CNG): Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension;Body;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NGVP1,"Fuel Receptacle (CNG): Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Receptacle (CNG) >> Description and Operation Fuel Receptacle (CNG): Description and Operation Fueling Connector Flange Assembly-Fuel Tank Fill Flange Assembly: The flange assembly (Figure 85) is designed for 20,685 kPa (3,000 psi) service pressure and is the refueling connection to fill the vehicle. The assembly is mounted behind the fuel filler door and attached to the fuel filler housing, similar to a gasoline vehicle. This assembly consists of an NGVP1 type receptacle with a 150 micron filter (which can be serviced), a spring loaded check valve to allow filling of the vehicle and a manually opened bypass to provide safe venting of the fuel system. The vehicle is refueled by attaching the fuel station fill nozzle to the receptacle and locking into place. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8202.html,Fuel Rail: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,Fuel Rail: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Rail >> Description and Operation Fuel Rail: Description and Operation Fuel Rail Fuel Rail Components: The fuel rail (Figure 80) distributes low pressure fuel from the chassis supply line to each fuel injector . Fuel pressure at the top of each fuel injector is maintained within 1% of the other fuel injectors at all times; this is done with nearly symmetric flow paths. The fuel rail is also designed to have minimal flow restriction by increasing the cross-sectional flow area and reducing the flow path length. The fuel rail contains several other parts in assembly (PIA) components that perform crucial functions. These include: - Injection pressure sensor which measures the pressure of the fuel near the fuel injectors. This signal is used by the PCM to adjust the fuel injector pulsewidth and meter fuel to each engine combustion cylinder. - Engine fuel temperature sensor which measures the pressure of the fuel near the fuel injectors. This signal is used by the PCM to adjust the fuel injector pulsewidth and meter fuel to each engine combustion cylinder. - Low pressure solenoid shut-off valve which isolates the fuel rail from the upstream fuel system when the engine is OFF. This minimizes the amount of fuel available to flow through the fuel injectors when the engine is off or leak from a damaged fuel rail during and after a crash. The valve is controlled by the PCM fuel shut-off valve circuit and contains an inertia switch. The valve is only on for one second after a key-on or whenever CKP signals are being received by the PCM. - schrader/service valve (if equipped) provides a service port to the low pressure fuel system. This valve is needed to relieve the pressure in the system before and during service. This valve could also be used to monitor the pressure near the injectors during diagnostic procedures. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
8203.html,Fuel Rail: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension;Wiring,4,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;FUEL INJECTOR;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;MANIFOLD;NOTE;REMOVAL;SUPPLY;WARNING,"Fuel Rail: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Rail >> Service and Repair Fuel Rail: Service and Repair FUEL INJECTOR SUPPLY MANIFOLD REMOVAL WARNING: - Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related components. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and may be ignited. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. - Fuel in the fuel system remains under high pressure even when the engine is not running. Before working on or disconnecting any of the fuel lines or fuel system components, the fuel system pressure must be relieved. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. CAUTION: If the supply manifold is used as a leverage device, damage may occur to the supply manifold. Care must be taken when working around the supply manifold. 1. Remove the intake manifold. 2. Disconnect the fuel tube spring lock coupling. 3. Remove the fuel supply tube bracket bolt from the LH valve cover. 4. Disconnect the following. - Fuel pressure /temperature sensor electrical and vacuum connections. - Fuel pulse damper vacuum hose. 5. NOTE: One connector is shown, the other five are similar. Disconnect the six fuel injector electrical connectors. 6. Remove the fuel injection supply manifold. 1 Remove the fuel supply tube. 2 Remove the fuel injection supply manifold and the fuel injectors as an assembly. 7. Remove the fuel injectors. INSTALLATION 1. CAUTION: Use O-ring seals that are made of special fuel-resistant material. Use of ordinary O-ring seals can cause the fuel system to leak. Do not reuse O-ring seals. NOTE: - Lubricate the new O-ring seals with clean engine oil. - Use new fasteners to attach the fuel line. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8205.html,Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,0,,,0L VIN K;134-R0087 OR;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;EQUIPPED WITH;EQUIVALENT;HANDLING;LEMON;ON VEHICLES NOT;POINT;PRESSURE TEST;SCHRADER VALVE;USE ROTUNDA FUEL;WARNING,"Gasoline Fuel System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Fuel Pump >> Fuel Pressure >> Fuel Pressure Test Port >> Description and Operation >> Gasoline Fuel System Gasoline Fuel System PRESSURE TEST POINT There is a pressure test point with a schrader fitting in the fuel rail that relieves fuel pressure and measures the fuel injector supply pressure for service and diagnostic procedures. Before servicing or testing the fuel system, read any CAUTION, WARNING, and HANDLING information. ON VEHICLES NOT EQUIPPED WITH A SCHRADER VALVE, USE ROTUNDA FUEL PRESSURE TEST KIT #134-R0087 OR EQUIVALENT. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
