8231.html,Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;MASS AIR FLOW;REMOVAL 1;SENSOR,"Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Air Flow Meter/Sensor >> Service and Repair Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Service and Repair MASS AIR FLOW (MAF) SENSOR REMOVAL 1. Loosen the air cleaner outlet tube clamp and position the tube aside. 2. Disconnect the mass air flow (MAF) sensor electrical connector. 3. CAUTION: The MAF sensor electronics module and body are calibrated as a unit and must be replaced as a unit. Do not tamper with the sensing elements located in the air flow bypass of the MAF body. Remove the four bolts and the MAF sensor. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
