8234.html,Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Wiring,1,"torque based strategy. Electronic Throttle Body And Accelerator Pedal Assembly: 4. The three pedal position signals ensure a correct input to the PCM, if any one sign",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCELERATOR PEDAL;APP1;APP2;APP3;APPS;LEMON;POSITION;SENSORS;VREF,"Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor >> Description and Operation Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor: Description and Operation ACCELERATOR PEDAL POSITION SENSORS (APPS) The ETC strategy uses pedal position sensors as an input to determine the driver demand. 1. There are three pedal position sensors required for system monitoring. APP1 has a negative slope (increasing angle, decreasing voltage) and APP2 & APP3 both have a positive slope (increasing angle, increasing voltage). During normal operation APP1 is used as the indication of pedal position by the strategy. 2. There are two VREF wires, two signal return wires and three signal wires (total of seven wires and pins) between the PCM and APPS assembly. - 2-5 V Reference Voltage - 2- Signal Return (ground) - APP1 voltage with negative voltage slope (5-0) - APP2 voltage with positive voltage slope (0-5) - APP3 voltage with positive voltage slope (0-5) 3. The pedal position signal is converted to pedal travel degrees (rotary angle) by the PCM. The software then converts these degrees to counts, which is the input to the torque based strategy. Electronic Throttle Body And Accelerator Pedal Assembly: 4. The three pedal position signals ensure a correct input to the PCM, if any one signal has a fault. The PCM knows if a signal is wrong by calculating where it should be, inferred by the other signals. A value will be substituted for a faulty signal if two out of the three signals are bad. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8235.html,Accelerator Pedal: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Wiring;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCELERATION;CONTROL;LEMON,"Accelerator Pedal: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Accelerator Pedal >> Description and Operation Accelerator Pedal: Description and Operation ACCELERATION CONTROL The throttle is controlled by an accelerator cable attached to the accelerator pedal and shaft assembly. The accelerator pedal and shaft should travel smoothly from the idle position to the wide open throttle position. Hesitation or binding should not be experienced at any portion of the accelerator pedal and shaft travel. Surrounding components such as wiring, hoses, sound insulator and floor carpet must not contact the sliding inner member of the accelerator cable or interfere with the accelerator pedal and shaft. The acceleration control consists of an accelerator pedal and cable. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8236.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;INSPECTION AND;LEMON;VERIFICATION NOTE,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Accelerator Pedal >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview INSPECTION AND VERIFICATION NOTE: Care should be exercised when carrying out repair on or around the accelerator pedal linkage and controls. 1. Inspect the accelerator pedal and shaft and attaching linkage for damage or distortion which would bind or limit accelerator travel. 2. Inspect the accelerator cable for kinks or fraying which may cause binding. 3. Inspect the engine idle speed adjustment to make sure of the correct idle speed specification after any accelerator linkage adjustment or repair. 4. Inspect throttle body for excessive wear or damage. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
