8399.html,Throttle Position Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;POSITION;SENSOR;THROTTLE,"Throttle Position Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Computers and Control Systems >> Throttle Position Sensor >> Description and Operation Throttle Position Sensor: Description and Operation THROTTLE POSITION SENSOR The TP sensor monitors throttle position and provides an electrical signal to the PCM. It is monitored by the OBD system for component integrity, system functionality, and faults that can cause emissions levels to exceed standards set in government regulations. For additional information on the TP sensor, refer to Electronic EC System Hardware-PCM Inputs. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
