8403.html,Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCS;CUT-OFF;EATC;LEMON;THROTTLE A;WIDE OPEN,"Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Computers and Control Systems >> Throttle Full Open Switch >> Description and Operation Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation WIDE OPEN THROTTLE A/C CUT-OFF (WAC) The wide open throttle A/C cutoff relay (may be referred to as the A/C clutch relay) is wired normally open (normally closed for Aviator). There is no direct electrical connection between the A/C switch or EATC Module and the A/C clutch. The PCM will receive a signal indicating that A/C is requested (for some applications, this message is sent through the BUS + and BUS - circuits). When A/C is requested, the PCM will check other A/C related inputs that are available (such as ACP (SW), ACCS). If these inputs indicate A/C operation is OK, and the engine conditions are OK (such as coolant temperature, engine rpm, throttle position), the PCM will ground the WAC output (unground for Aviator), closing the relay contacts and sending voltage to the A/C clutch. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8404.html,Output Shaft Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;OUTPUT SHAFT;SPEED SENSOR,"Output Shaft Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Computers and Control Systems >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Vehicle Speed Sensor >> Description and Operation >> Output Shaft Speed Sensor Output Shaft Speed Sensor OUTPUT SHAFT SPEED SENSOR The Output Shaft Speed Sensor (OSS), provides the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) with information about the rotational speed of an output shaft.The (PCM) uses the information to control and diagnose powertrain behavior. In some applications, the sensor is also used as the source of vehicle speed. The sensor may be physically located in different places on the vehicle, depending upon the specific application. The design of each speed sensor is unique and depends on which powertrain control feature uses the information generated. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8405.html,Vehicle Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission,1,torque converter clutch scheduling. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;SENSOR;VEHICLE SPEED,"Vehicle Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Computers and Control Systems >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Vehicle Speed Sensor >> Description and Operation >> Vehicle Speed Sensor Vehicle Speed Sensor VEHICLE SPEED SENSOR Typical Vehicle Speed Sensor (VSS): The vehicle speed sensor (VSS) (Figure 52) is a variable reluctance or Hall-effect sensor that generates a waveform with a frequency that is proportional to the speed of the vehicle. If the vehicle is moving at a relatively low velocity, the sensor produces a signal with a low frequency. As the vehicle velocity increases, the sensor generates a signal with a higher frequency. The PCM uses the frequency signal generated by the VSS (and other inputs) to control such parameters as fuel injection, ignition control, transmission/transaxle shift scheduling and torque converter clutch scheduling. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
