8645.html,Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Body,3,torque converter clutch scheduling. Most MAF sensors have integrated bypass technology (IBT) with an integrated intake air temperature (IAT) sensor. The MAF sensor is,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;MASS AIR FLOW;SENSOR,"Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Fuel Delivery and Air Induction >> Air Flow Meter/Sensor >> Description and Operation Air Flow Meter/Sensor: Description and Operation MASS AIR FLOW SENSOR Diagram Of Air Flow Through Throttle Body Contacting MAF Sensor Hot And Cold Wire Terminals: Typical Mass Air Flow (MAF) Sensor: Typical ""Drop-in"" Mass Air Flow (MAF) Sensor: The mass air flow (MAF) sensor uses a hot wire sensing element to measure the amount of air entering the engine. Air passing over the hot wire causes it to cool. This hot wire is maintained at 200°C (392°F) above ambient temperature as measured by a constant cold wire (Figure 42). If the hot wire electronic sensing element must be replaced, then the entire assembly must be replaced. Replacing only the element may change the air flow calibration. The current required to maintain the temperature of the hot wire is proportional to the air mass flow. The MAF sensor then outputs an analog voltage signal to the PCM proportional to the intake air mass. The PCM calculates the required fuel injector pulse width in order to provide the desired air/fuel ratio. This input is also used in determining transmission electronic pressure control (EPC), shift and torque converter clutch scheduling. Most MAF sensors have integrated bypass technology (IBT) with an integrated intake air temperature (IAT) sensor. The MAF sensor is located between the air cleaner and the throttle body or inside the air cleaner assembly. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
