8665.html,Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;ACCS;CUT-OFF;EATC;LEMON;THROTTLE A;WIDE OPEN,"Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Throttle Full Open Switch >> Description and Operation Throttle Full Open Switch: Description and Operation WIDE OPEN THROTTLE A/C CUT-OFF (WAC) The wide open throttle A/C cutoff relay (may be referred to as the A/C clutch relay) is wired normally open (normally closed for Aviator). There is no direct electrical connection between the A/C switch or EATC Module and the A/C clutch. The PCM will receive a signal indicating that A/C is requested (for some applications, this message is sent through the BUS + and BUS - circuits). When A/C is requested, the PCM will check other A/C related inputs that are available (such as ACP (SW), ACCS). If these inputs indicate A/C operation is OK, and the engine conditions are OK (such as coolant temperature, engine rpm, throttle position), the PCM will ground the WAC output (unground for Aviator), closing the relay contacts and sending voltage to the A/C clutch. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8666.html,Differential Pressure Feedback EGR System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,1,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DIFFERENTIAL;FEEDBACK EGR;HI SIGNAL;LEMON;PRESSURE;REF SIGNAL;SENSOR,"Differential Pressure Feedback EGR System — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Pressure Feedback Exhaust Sensor >> Description and Operation >> Differential Pressure Feedback EGR System Differential Pressure Feedback EGR System DIFFERENTIAL PRESSURE FEEDBACK EGR SENSOR Differential Pressure Feedback EGR Sensor: The differential pressure feedback EGR sensor (Figure 90) is a ceramic, capacitive-type pressure transducer that monitors the differential pressure across a metering orifice located in the orifice tube assembly. The differential pressure feedback sensor receives this signal through two hoses referred to as the downstream pressure hose (REF SIGNAL) and upstream pressure hose (HI SIGNAL). The HI and REF hose connections are marked on the differential pressure feedback EGR sensor housing for identification (note that the HI signal uses a larger diameter hose). The differential pressure feedback EGR sensor outputs a voltage proportional to the pressure drop across the metering orifice and supplies it to the PCM as EGR flow rate feedback. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
