8747.html,Muffler: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension;Interior,6,"tighten the nuts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NEUTRAL;NOTE,"Muffler: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Exhaust System >> Muffler >> Service and Repair Muffler: Service and Repair Muffler and Tailpipe Removal and Installation CAUTION: Do not use oil or grease-based lubricants on isolators as they deteriorate the rubber. 1. With the vehicle in NEUTRAL, position it on a hoist. 2. Remove the muffler -to-converter flag nuts, bolts and springs. Discard the flag nuts and bolts. 3. Remove the shock absorber bolt, then position the shock absorber out of the way. 4. Remove the stabilizer bar link nut, then position the RH stabilizer bar link out of the way. 5. Detach the tailpipe from the isolator. 6. Detach the muffler from the isolators and remove the muffler and tailpipe. 7. Remove and discard the converter outlet pipe gasket. 8. NOTE: Clean the mating surfaces of the catalytic converter and the inlet pipe. NOTE: Install a new outlet pipe gasket. NOTE: Use new exhaust fasteners. To correctly seat the catalytic converter to the inlet pipe, alternately tighten the nuts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
