8751.html,Dual Converter Y-Pipe — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring;Interior,5,"tighten the nuts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. ^ Check and, if necessary, align the exhaust system . scientia non olet · About LEMON Man || tightened after the three-way catalytic converter is installed. NOTE: Make sure to apply anti-seize lubricant to the threads of the sensors before installation. NOTE:",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Dual Converter Y-Pipe — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Exhaust System >> Exhaust Pipe >> Service and Repair >> Dual Converter Y-Pipe Dual Converter Y-Pipe Dual Converter Y-Pipe Material Removal and Installation 1. Remove the dual three-way catalytic converter. 2. Disconnect the heated oxygen sensor electrical connectors. 3. Remove the LH converter-to-manifold nuts. 4. Remove the RH converter-to-manifold nuts, then remove the dual converter Y-pipe. 5. Remove and discard the converter inlet gasket. If necessary, remove the heated oxygen sensors. 6. CAUTION: Make sure that the dual converter Y-pipe to exhaust manifold nuts are tightened after the three-way catalytic converter is installed. NOTE: Make sure to apply anti-seize lubricant to the threads of the sensors before installation. NOTE: Clean the mating surfaces of the catalytic converters . NOTE: Install a new converter inlet gasket. NOTE: Use new exhaust fasteners. To correctly seat the catalytic converters , alternately tighten the nuts to specification. To install, reverse the removal procedure. ^ Check and, if necessary, align the exhaust system . scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
