8780.html,Radiator: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NOTE,"Radiator: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Cooling System >> Radiator >> Service and Repair Radiator: Service and Repair Radiator Removal and Installation 1. Drain the cooling system . 2. Remove the air cleaner outlet tube. 3. Disconnect and remove the overflow hose. 4. Remove the cooling fan shroud. 5. Disconnect the upper radiator hose from the radiator. 6. Disconnect the lower radiator hose from the radiator. 7. NOTE: To avoid disturbing the transmission oil cooler fittings, use a backup wrench. Disconnect the two transmission cooling lines. 8. Remove the two bolts and the radiator. 9. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
