8895.html,Drive Belt: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Drive Belt: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Drive Belts, Mounts, Brackets and Accessories >> Drive Belt >> Description and Operation Drive Belt: Description and Operation Accessory Drive Component Locations The accessory drive system consists of the following: ^ drive belt ^ generator pulley ^ power steering pump pulley ^ A/C compressor pulley ^ water pump pulley ^ drive belt tensioner ^ belt idler pulley ^ crankshaft pulley The accessory drive: ^ has a single serpentine drive belt (six ribs) ^ has an automatic tensioner. ^ is not adjustable. 4. If the concerns remain after inspection determine the symptoms. GO to Symptom Chart. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8896.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Drive Belts, Mounts, Brackets and Accessories >> Drive Belt >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Accessory Drive Inspection and Verification 1. Verify the customer's concern by operating the engine to duplicate the condition. 2. Inspect to determine if any of the mechanical concerns apply. Visual Inspection Chart 3. Inspect for drive belt cracking/chunking/wear 4. If the concerns remain after inspection, determine the symptoms. Go to Symptom Chart. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures Under severe operating conditions (high temperature, low humidity), drive belt rib cracking can occur at less than 96,000 km (60,000 miles) . Drive belt rib cracking (cracks across grooves): ^ is not a reason for concern ^ has no detrimental effect on drive shaft performance. Cracks parallel to grooves are acceptable. The drive belt is still perfectly functional until rib chunking occurs. Drive belt chunking is where the rubber material actually chunks out between the cracks. A new drive belt should he installed if chunking occurs. V-Ribbed Serpentine Drive with Cracks Across Backing V-Ribbed Serpentine Drive with Chunks of Ribs Missing 5. If the concern(s) remains after inspection, determine the symptoms. GO to Symptom Chart. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
