8906.html,Valve Cover RH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission;Wiring;Interior,15,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Valve Cover RH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Cylinder Head Assembly >> Valve Cover >> Service and Repair >> Valve Cover RH Valve Cover RH Valve Cover RH Removal and Installation 1. Drain the cooling system . 2. Remove the air cleaner outlet pipe. 3. Remove the upper radiator hose. 4. Remove the crankcase breather hose and disconnect the vacuum hose. 5. Remove the transmission fluid indicator tube retaining nut and position the indicator tube aside. 6. Disconnect the coolant hoses. 7. Disconnect the coolant hose. 8. Remove the coolant tube bracket retaining bolts. 9. Disconnect the coolant hoses. 10. Detach the wiring harness retainer and remove the coolant tube and bracket assembly. 11. Disconnect the heater hose and position the hose aside. 12. Disconnect mass air flow (MAF) sensor electrical connector and wiring pin-type retainer. Position the wiring aside. 13. CAUTION: It is important to twist the spark plug wire boots while pulling upward to avoid possible damage to the spark plug wire. NOTE: Spark plug wires must be connected to the correct ignition coil terminal. Mark the spark plug wire locations before removing them. Position the spark plug wires aside. 1 Disconnect the spark plug wires. 2 Disconnect the spark plug wire retainer and position the wires aside. 14. Remove the wiring harness anchor from the valve cover stud. 15. Disconnect the fuel injector electrical connectors. Position the wiring aside. 16. Remove the bolts and the valve cover . 17. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8907.html,Valve Cover LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Body;Wiring,18,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Valve Cover LH — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Cylinder Head Assembly >> Valve Cover >> Service and Repair >> Valve Cover LH Valve Cover LH Valve Cover LH Removal and Installation 1. Disconnect the battery negative cable. 2. Detach the accelerator cable from the throttle body and the accelerator cable bracket. 3. Loosen the bolt and disconnect the electrical connector. 4. Disconnect the vapor hose end from the intake manifold . 5. Disconnect the vapor hose end and the pin-type retainer. Remove the vapor hose. 6. Disconnect the camshaft position (CMP) sensor electrical connector. Remove the differential pressure feedback exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) system. 7. Remove the EGR vacuum regulator solenoid. 1 Disconnect the electrical connector. 2 Disconnect the vacuum connection. 3 Remove the retaining bolts and the solenoid. 8. Disconnect the fuel tube push connect coupling. 9. Remove the fuel supply tube bracket bolt and position the supply tube aside. 10. Remove the bolt and position the fuel supply tube aside. 11. Disconnect the EGR vacuum hose and the EGR tube from the valve. 12. Remove the bolt and position the electrical connector aside. Disconnect the radio interference capacitor electrical connector. 13. Carry out the following: ^ Detach the two spark plug wire retainers. ^ CAUTION: It is important to twist the spark plug wire boots while pulling upward to avoid possible damage to the spark plug wire. NOTE: Spark plug wires must be connected to the correct ignition coil terminal. Mark spark plug wire locations before removing them. Disconnect the LH spark plug wires from the ignition coil. 14. Disconnect the ignition coil electrical connector. 15. Remove the ignition coil bracket lower bolts. 16. Remove the ignition coil bracket upper bolts and position the ignition coil aside. 17. Disconnect the positive crankcase ventilation (PCV) hose. 18. Unscrew the PCV valve. 19. Disconnect the LH fuel injector electrical connectors and detach the wire harness pin-type retainer on the valve cover stud. 20. Remove the bolts and the valve cover . 21. To install, reverse removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8909.html,Rocker Arm Assembly: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;NOTE,"Rocker Arm Assembly: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Cylinder Head Assembly >> Rocker Arm Assembly >> Service and Repair Rocker Arm Assembly: Service and Repair Roller Followers Special Tool(s) Material Removal 1. Remove the LH valve cover. 2. Remove the RH valve cover. 3. Remove the fuel injection supply manifold. 4. NOTE: Mark each camshaft roller follower to ensure its original position during reassembly. Using the special tool, remove the camshaft roller followers. 5. NOTE: Lubricate the parts with clean engine oil prior to installing. To install, reverse the removal procedure. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
8910.html,Fuel Pressure Release: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,0,,,0L VIN K;1051;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;FUEL SYSTEM;LEMON;NOTE;PRESSURE;RELEASE;WARNING,"Fuel Pressure Release: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Engine, Cooling and Exhaust >> Engine >> Cylinder Head Assembly >> Fuel Pressure Release >> Service and Repair Fuel Pressure Release: Service and Repair FUEL SYSTEM PRESSURE RELEASE WARNING: - Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near any fuel-related component. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and may be ignited, resulting in possible personal injury. - Fuel in the fuel system remains under high pressure even when the engine is not running. Before repairing or disconnecting any of the fuel lines or fuel system components, the fuel system pressure must be relieved to prevent accidental spraying of fuel, causing personal injury or a fire hazard. 1. NOTE: The fuel pump relay is located in the battery junction box location C-1051. Remove the fuel pump relay. 2. Start the engine and allow it to idle until it stalls. 3. After the engine stalls, crank the engine for approximately 5 seconds to make sure the fuel injection supply manifold pressure has been released. 4. Turn the ignition switch to the OFF position. 5. When the fuel system service is complete, install the fuel pump relay. 6. NOTE: It may take more than one key cycle to pressurize the fuel system. Cycle the ignition key and wait three seconds to pressurize the fuel system. Check for leaks before starting the engine. 7. Start the vehicle and check the fuel system for leaks. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
