e bolts. 2 Remove the sprockets. 3 Lift the chain and guide up and out of the cylinder head. 16. Clean all surfaces. Clean all foreign material from engine. Installation 1. Install the chain guide through the cylinder head. 2. Install the chain. 3. Install the new chain guide bolts. 4. NOTE: The camshaft chain sprockets must be orientated correctly. Install the chain lower sprocket and the camshaft sprocket. 5. Install, but do not tighten the camshaft sprocket bolt. 6. Install the primary chain and gear. 7. Install the primary drive chain tensioner. 8. Hold the crankshaft from turning and tighten the jackshaft sprocket bolt in two stages. ^ Stage 1: Tighten bolt to 45 Nm (33 ft. lbs.). ^ Stage 2: Tighten bolt an additional 90 degrees. 9. Install the engine front cover. 10. Time the engine. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
