8940.html,Attachment III - Technical Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission,8,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2004 LS;2005;2005 LS;2WD V6-4;LEMON;OVERVIEW,"Attachment III - Technical Information — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Technical Service Bulletins >> Recalls >> Campaign - Additive For A/T Fluid >> Attachment III - Technical Information Attachment III - Technical Information OVERVIEW This program involves adding a fluid additive to the automatic transmission. ^ For Ranger and Explorer Sport Trac models, the additive will be added to the transmission through the fluid level indicator (dipstick) tube. ^ For 2004 LS and Thunderbird models, the additive will be added through the extension housing fill port. ^ For2005 LE and Thunderbird, and 2004 and 2005 Explorer, Mountaineer and Aviator models, the additive will be added to the transmission through the transmission pan fluid level tube while the engine is running. This procedure requires the transmission fluid temperature (TFT) to be below 38° C (100°F) to ensure fluid level is below the top of the fluid level tube. See Figure 1. Use WDS or NGS to determine transmission fluid temperature. Warning Label 2004 and 2005 Ranger and Explorer Sport Trac 2004 LS and Thunderbird 2005 LS and Thunderbird, and 2004 and 2005 Explorer/Mountaineer and Aviator scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
