9120.html,Evaporative Canister Filter: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;DUST SEPARATOR;EVAP;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL;WARNING,"Evaporative Canister Filter: Service and Repair — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Filters >> Evaporative Canister Filter >> Service and Repair Evaporative Canister Filter: Service and Repair DUST SEPARATOR REMOVAL WARNING: - The evaporative emission system contains fuel vapor and condensed fuel vapor. Although not present in large quantities, it still presents the danger of explosion or fire. Disconnect the battery ground cable from the battery to minimize the possibility of an electrical spark occurring, which can cause a fire or explosion if fuel vapor or liquefied fuel are present in the area. Failure to follow these instructions may result in personal injury. - Do not smoke or carry lighted tobacco or open flame of any type when working on or near fuel related components. Highly flammable mixtures are always present and can be ignited. Failure to follow these instructions can result in personal injury. 1. Lower and remove the spare tire . 2. Disconnect the battery ground cable. 3. Raise the vehicle on a hoist. 4. Remove the evaporative emission (EVAP) canister tray mounting bolts. 5. Slightly lower the rear of the EVAP canister assembly to allow access to the top of the assembly. 6. Disconnect the vapor hose from the passenger side EVAP canister and tilt the assembly to allow access to the driver side EVAP canister. 7. Disconnect the vent solenoid electrical connector and the wiring pin-type retainer. Disconnect the vapor hose. 8. Position the EVAP canister assembly on a firm flat surface. 9. Disconnect the hose from the dust separator. 10. Remove the dust separator. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Leak test the evaporative emission system. Evaporative Emission System Leak Test - Carry out the evaporative emission repair verification drive cycle. Evaporative Emission Repair Verification Drive Cycle scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
