9123.html,Drive Belt: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Suspension,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,Drive Belt: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Drive Belt >> Description and Operation Drive Belt: Description and Operation Accessory Drive Component Locations The accessory drive system consists of the following: ^ drive belt ^ generator pulley ^ power steering pump pulley ^ A/C compressor pulley ^ water pump pulley ^ drive belt tensioner ^ belt idler pulley ^ crankshaft pulley The accessory drive: ^ has a single serpentine drive belt (six ribs) ^ has an automatic tensioner. ^ is not adjustable. 4. If the concerns remain after inspection determine the symptoms. GO to Symptom Chart. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
9124.html,Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,3,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,"Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Drive Belt >> Testing and Inspection >> Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Initial Inspection and Diagnostic Overview Accessory Drive Inspection and Verification 1. Verify the customer's concern by operating the engine to duplicate the condition. 2. Inspect to determine if any of the mechanical concerns apply. Visual Inspection Chart 3. Inspect for drive belt cracking/chunking/wear 4. If the concerns remain after inspection, determine the symptoms. Go to Symptom Chart. Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures Under severe operating conditions (high temperature, low humidity), drive belt rib cracking can occur at less than 96,000 km (60,000 miles) . Drive belt rib cracking (cracks across grooves): ^ is not a reason for concern ^ has no detrimental effect on drive shaft performance. Cracks parallel to grooves are acceptable. The drive belt is still perfectly functional until rib chunking occurs. Drive belt chunking is where the rubber material actually chunks out between the cracks. A new drive belt should he installed if chunking occurs. V-Ribbed Serpentine Drive with Cracks Across Backing V-Ribbed Serpentine Drive with Chunks of Ribs Missing 5. If the concern(s) remains after inspection, determine the symptoms. GO to Symptom Chart. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
9125.html,Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON,Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Drive Belt >> Testing and Inspection >> Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures Symptom Related Diagnostic Procedures Symptom Chart Part 1 Of 2: Part 2 Of 2: scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals
9126.html,Component Tests and General Diagnostics — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine,0,"Tighten all accessories, mounting brackets and drive belt tensioner retaining hardware to specification. Recheck drive belt tracking. scientia non olet · About LEMON M",,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CAUTION;LEMON;NOTE,"Component Tests and General Diagnostics — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Maintenance >> Drive Belt >> Testing and Inspection >> Component Tests and General Diagnostics Component Tests and General Diagnostics Drive Belt - Misalignment CAUTION: Incorrect drive belt installation will cause excessive drive belt wear and may cause the drive belt to come off the drive pulleys. NOTE: Original equipment drive belts are made of a special cord construction and are subjected to special testing before they are approved for use. Non-standard new drive belts may track differently or incorrectly. If a new drive belt tracks incorrectly, install a new original equipment drive belt to avoid performance failure or loss of drive belt. With the engine running check drive belt tracking (the position of the drive belt on one of the grooveless pulleys idlers or drive belt tensioner. It the edge of the drive belt rides beyond the edge of the pulley noise and premature wear may result). It a drive belt tracking condition exists visually check the drive belt tensioner for damage especially the mounting pad surface. It the drive belt tensioner is not installed correctly with the locating pins in the locating holes, the mounting surface pad will be out of position. This will result in abnormal drive belt tension and chirp and squeal noises. If the above procedures do not correct the drive belt noise install a new drive belt. However the drive belt noise may return (with mileage) if one of the above conditions still exists uncorrected. ^ With engine running visually observe the grooves in the pulleys (not the pulley flanges) for excessive wobble. Install new components as necessary. ^ Check all accessories mounting brackets and drive belt tensioner for any interference that would prevent the component irons mounting correctly. Correct any interference condition and recheck belt tracking. ^ Tighten all accessories, mounting brackets and drive belt tensioner retaining hardware to specification. Recheck drive belt tracking. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
