9212.html,Ignition Lock Cylinder - Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Wiring,2,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CYLINDER;FUNCTIONAL;IGNITION LOCK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;REMOVAL 1,"Ignition Lock Cylinder - Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Sensors and Switches >> Sensors and Switches - Starting and Charging >> Ignition Switch >> Ignition Switch Lock Cylinder >> Service and Repair >> Ignition Lock Cylinder - Functional Ignition Lock Cylinder - Functional IGNITION LOCK CYLINDER - FUNCTIONAL REMOVAL 1. Disconnect the battery ground cable and wait at least one minute . 2. Remove the ignition switch lock cylinder . 1 Insert the ignition key and turn to the RUN position. 2 Press the ignition switch lock cylinder release pin while pulling out the ignition switch lock cylinder. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Verify ignition switch lock cylinder operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
9213.html,Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Suspension,5,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;CYLINDER;F85Z-11582-AA;IGNITION LOCK;INSTALLATION 1;LEMON;NON FUNCTIONAL;NOTE;REMOVAL 1;WARNING,"Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Sensors and Switches >> Sensors and Switches - Starting and Charging >> Ignition Switch >> Ignition Switch Lock Cylinder >> Service and Repair >> Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional Ignition Lock Cylinder - Non Functional IGNITION LOCK CYLINDER - NON FUNCTIONAL REMOVAL 1. WARNING: To reduce the risk of serious personal injury, read and follow all warnings, notes and instructions in the steering wheel removal and installation procedure. NOTE: Make sure the front wheels are in the straight-ahead position. Remove the steering wheel assembly. 2. Twist off the cap from the ignition switch cylinder. 3. NOTE: The lock cylinder is repaired by discarding the inoperative lock cylinder and building a new lock cylinder using the appropriate lock repair package (F85Z-11582-AA). The lock repair package includes a detailed instruction sheet to build the new lock cylinder to the current key code of the vehicle. Remove the ignition switch lock cylinder . - Use a 1/8-inch diameter drill bit to drill out the lock cylinder retaining pin. - Use a 3/8-inch drill bit to drill down the middle of the ignition lock key slot until the ignition switch lock cylinder breaks loose. - Remove and discard the ignition switch lock cylinder and clean the drill shavings from the steering column. 4. Remove the bearing retainer. 5. Remove the bearing and gear. - Thoroughly clean all drill shavings from the steering column and inspect it for damage. INSTALLATION 1. To install, reverse the removal procedure. - Install a new ignition switch lock cylinder . - Verify ignition switch lock cylinder operation. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
9214.html,Seat Belt Buckle Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Body;Interior,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;BUCKLE;LEMON;SAFETY BELT;SWITCHES,"Seat Belt Buckle Switch: Description and Operation — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Sensors and Switches >> Sensors and Switches - Restraints and Safety Systems >> Seat Belt Buckle Switch >> Description and Operation Seat Belt Buckle Switch: Description and Operation SAFETY BELT BUCKLE SWITCHES As part of the supplemental restraint system (SRS), the driver and front outboard passenger safety belt buckles are equipped with safety belt buckle switches. The safety belt buckle switches indicate to the restraints control module (RCM) whether the safety belts are connected or disconnected. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
