9275.html,Output Shaft Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,,0,,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;OUTPUT SHAFT;SPEED SENSOR,"Output Shaft Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Sensors and Switches >> Sensors and Switches - Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Vehicle Speed Sensor >> Description and Operation >> Output Shaft Speed Sensor Output Shaft Speed Sensor OUTPUT SHAFT SPEED SENSOR The Output Shaft Speed Sensor (OSS), provides the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) with information about the rotational speed of an output shaft.The (PCM) uses the information to control and diagnose powertrain behavior. In some applications, the sensor is also used as the source of vehicle speed. The sensor may be physically located in different places on the vehicle, depending upon the specific application. The design of each speed sensor is unique and depends on which powertrain control feature uses the information generated. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
9276.html,Vehicle Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals,Engine;Transmission,1,torque converter clutch scheduling. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals,,0L VIN K;1960-2025;2004;2WD V6-4;LEMON;SENSOR;VEHICLE SPEED,"Vehicle Speed Sensor — 2004 Ford Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel Service Manual ~ LEMON Manuals LEMON Manuals : Even more car manuals for everyone: 1960-2025 Home >> Ford >> 2004 >> Explorer Sport Trac 2WD V6-4.0L VIN K Flex Fuel >> Repair and Diagnosis >> Sensors and Switches >> Sensors and Switches - Powertrain Management >> Sensors and Switches - Computers and Control Systems >> Vehicle Speed Sensor >> Description and Operation >> Vehicle Speed Sensor Vehicle Speed Sensor VEHICLE SPEED SENSOR Typical Vehicle Speed Sensor (VSS): The vehicle speed sensor (VSS) (Figure 52) is a variable reluctance or Hall-effect sensor that generates a waveform with a frequency that is proportional to the speed of the vehicle. If the vehicle is moving at a relatively low velocity, the sensor produces a signal with a low frequency. As the vehicle velocity increases, the sensor generates a signal with a higher frequency. The PCM uses the frequency signal generated by the VSS (and other inputs) to control such parameters as fuel injection, ignition control, transmission/transaxle shift scheduling and torque converter clutch scheduling. scientia non olet · About LEMON Manuals"
